{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh21uu4BbbSy3Zue94rq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0181ZcE3FU48n1CL2svqYUL5","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","offset":360,"limit":360},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14151,"cache_read_input_tokens":24733,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14151},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"1c9bdedc-15b9-48eb-bd39-0e9aeeddebb7","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:02.491Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh21ufQsatRC7H4JkdRr","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0181ZcE3FU48n1CL2svqYUL5":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","offset":360,"limit":360}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0181ZcE3FU48n1CL2svqYUL5","type":"tool_result","content":"360\t\n361\tAll distances in world units (u), times in seconds. `T.name` marks a tunable (Appendix A has every default).\n362\t\n363\t### 7.1 The rink (`Rink`)\n364\t- **Arena map**: a TileMap of 70 × 44 tiles (1120 × 704 u); rink center `C = (560, 400)`.\n365\t- **Rink**: a rounded rectangle with half-length 432, half-width 192 and corner radius 96 (x 128–992, y 208–592).\n366\t  `Rink.inside(x, y, r)`, `Rink.normalAt(x, y)` and `Rink.clamp(body, r)` are analytic: no stair-stepped corners.\n367\t- **Markings** (painted by `floorTex(x, y)`, baked once per arena): red center line (5 u) at `C.x`; blue lines (5 u)\n368\t  at `C.x ± 108`; red goal lines (2 u) at `C.x ± 376`; 5 faceoff circles of radius 72 (center, and the end-zone dots at\n369\t  `C.x ± 280, C.y ± 112`); neutral-zone dots at `C.x ± 84, C.y ± 112`; creases (half-discs of radius 28, light blue\n370\t  `#9fd3ff` with a red rim); the center-ice logo (the home team's logo sprite scaled x3, sampled per pixel); ice\n371\t  `#e9f3fb` with subtle noise, cool shading near the boards and a faint sheen. Outside the rink: rubber matting or\n372\t  concrete; the pond uses snow.\n373\t- **Goals**: the mouth spans `y = C.y ± 16` (32 wide, from post center to post center), the crossbar is at z 20, and\n374\t  the net runs 20 deep behind the goal line. Posts are cylinders of r 1.5. The net's mesh is translucent white (a\n375\t  blend at .35, lines every 3 px) and **bulges** where the puck hits (6 control points that spring back, k = 18).\n376\t- **Boards**: 17 high (white, with a 2-u yellow kick plate, ads on the straight runs, and a top cap in the home\n377\t  color). Glass rises 28 above the boards on the sides and 40 at the ends. It is split into **48 panels** (14 per side,\n378\t  4 per end, 3 per corner arc), each with a state of `ok`, `cracked` or `shattered`, and the stanchions show between\n379\t  them.\n380\t- **Drawing order**: the floor first, then the scuff decals, then the far (north) boards, glass, benches, sin bins and\n381\t  stands as background (skaters are always in front of them), then the end and corner panels queued one by one (`r.queue`\n382\t  at the panel's center, so they sort per panel), then the near (south) boards queued **cut low** (6 u, no glass, only\n383\t  the top rail), so they never hide play. Glass draws with `px.blend(.25)`, a white highlight streak, and crack lines\n384\t  or an empty frame by state.\n385\t- **Stands**: north of the benches (y 0–176) in 5 stepped tiers (TileMap wall types 24–64 high, with `face`\n386\t  materials per arena), and at the west and east ends (x 0–112 and 1008–1120). Nothing is built south of the near\n387\t  boards' apron; the near crowd is the screen-space silhouette row (section 8).\n388\t- **Benches and sin bins** sit on the far side, outside the boards (y 184–208): the home bench at x `C.x−216…C.x−72`,\n389\t  the away bench at `C.x+72…C.x+216`, the sin bins at `C.x−60…C.x−12` (home) and `C.x+12…C.x+60` (away), and the\n390\t  scorekeeper between them. Each team's bench holds 2 sitting spares and its coach standing. A skater in the sin bin\n391\t  sits in the box, visible.\n392\t- **Scuff layer**: a grid of 54 × 24 cells (16 u) of `scuff` 0..1 and `melt` 0..1. Skating adds\n393\t  `0.0025 × speed/132` per step to its cell, a hockey stop +0.12, a knockdown +0.2 in radius 1, Kaboom skates\n394\t  `melt` +0.05 a step. Draw with `r.decal`: each cell over .05 draws 1–4 scratch lines (a pattern from the cell's hash,\n395\t  alpha by scuff), and melt draws blue-grey puddles with a shine. The Flood Wagon clears both.\n396\t\n397\t### 7.2 Skating (`Skater.skateStep`, pure: the network prediction runs it too)\n398\t- Max speed `T.skateMax` 132 × the speed rating (`0.85 + 0.05 × Spd`), × `T.turboMul` 1.45 with turbo, × 0.94 when\n399\t  carrying the puck, and × 0.6 while winding up a slapshot.\n400\t- Acceleration `T.skateAccel` 300 × `(1 − 0.6 (v/vmax)²)` along the stick. Gliding with no input decelerates by\n401\t  `T.iceGlide` 28.\n402\t- **Turning**: the velocity heading rotates toward the stick direction at `lerp(T.turnSlow 5.0, T.turnFast 2.6,\n403\t  v/vmax)` rad/s. The sideways component of velocity relative to the facing decays at `T.edgeGrip` 6/s, which gives\n404\t  carves rather than slides.\n405\t- **Hockey stop**: when the stick points more than 120° from the velocity at speed > 60, the skater enters `stop`\n406\t  (at least 0.22 s): deceleration `T.stopDecel` 700, a snow spray (event `stop`), the torso turned 70°. The skater then\n407\t  accelerates the new way.\n408\t- Facing follows velocity (the AI may skate backward at 0.75× speed to keep facing the puck, using C-cut legs).\n409\t- **Turbo** meter 0..1: drains `T.turboDrain` 0.45/s while held and moving, and regenerates `T.turboRegen` 0.18/s\n410\t  once released for 0.6 s.\n411\t- **Bodies**: r 7. Masses: heroic 1.0, bulky 1.35, goalie 1.6 (The Vault 2.2). Skater–skater overlap pushes them\n412\t  apart with a restitution of .3. A collision without the check state is a \"bump\": no knockdown unless the closing\n413\t  speed is above `T.accidentalHit` 180.\n414\t- **Boards**: reflect the normal velocity × .3 and keep 85% of the tangential. Faster than 120 into the boards: a\n415\t  \"rattle\" event (sound, glass shake).\n416\t\n417\t### 7.3 The puck (`Puck`)\n418\t- r 1.6, drawn as a black ellipse of 3×2 px with a 1-px highlight, plus a shadow. Above 300 u/s it gets a streak; the\n419\t  **Puck trail** setting chooses Off, Streak or Glow (neon).\n420\t- Free motion: `v −= (T.puckFriction 26 + T.puckDrag 0.12 × |v|) dt`. Gravity 700 in the air. Hitting the ice: vz ×\n421\t  −0.3, and speed × 0.9 when vz was below −60. Speed cap 760.\n422\t- **4 substeps** per step, each a swept test against: the boards (restitution `T.boardBounce` .62 normal, .92\n423\t  tangential; the glass .5 when z > 17); posts (.82 plus a **ping** event; the crossbar when z is 19–21 inside the\n424\t  mouth); the net (from behind or the sides .2, a \"net\" sound); goalies (section 7.6); sticks (pickup or deflection);\n425\t  bodies (r 7: .35, a \"body\" event; a shot hitting a skater is a **block**). Over the glass top, or through a\n426\t  shattered panel: **out of play**, then a faceoff at the nearest end-zone dot.\n427\t- **Goal**: the puck's center crosses the goal line inside the mouth (`|y − C.y| < 16 − 1.6`) with z < 20 − 1.6,\n428\t  moving inward. The puck stays in the net (`inNet`; the bulge plays).\n429\t- **Possession**: the owner's blade point is `pos + R(facing) · [11, hand × 4]` (`hand` +1 right shot, −1 left, from\n430\t  the player data). The puck eases toward the blade at k = 30/s and weaves ±3 across (`sin(t × 9)`) at low speed.\n431\t- **Pickup**: a loose puck within `T.pickupRadius` 8 × the handling multiplier of the blade point (or 10 of the body\n432\t  center), at z < 6, after the skater's `pickupCooldown` (0.25 s once it releases the puck). If the relative speed is\n433\t  under 300 it is taken. Faster, it is caught with chance `clamp(1.3 − rel/450 + 0.08 (Hnd − 3), 0.1, 1)`, otherwise\n434\t  it deflects off the blade (reflected around the blade's normal at 0.5×).\n435\t- **Puck battles**: when opposing blades are both within 8 of a loose or carried puck, every 0.2 s the one with the\n436\t  higher `Hnd + Hit/2 + RNG.sim() × 3` takes it (a \"battle\" event, stick-clack sounds).\n437\t\n438\t### 7.4 Passing\n439\t- **Target**: the teammate whose bearing is nearest the aim within 75°; otherwise the nearest teammate ahead; with\n440\t  mouse or right-stick aim, the teammate nearest the reticle within 80, otherwise a pass to the space at the reticle.\n441\t- **Lead**: aim at `mate.pos + mate.v × tFlight × 0.9`, iterated twice; speed `clamp(220 + 0.9 d, 240, 420) ×\n442\t  (0.9 + 0.033 Pas)`; angular error σ = `0.06 × (1.3 − 0.1 Pas)` rad.\n443\t- **Interception**: an opponent's blade that comes within 8 of the puck's path tries a pickup (7.3).\n444\t- **Saucer pass** (`lob`): `E.arc` with apex 10 and speed × 0.8. It can't be intercepted while z > 6, lands near the\n445\t  mate and wobbles on landing.\n446\t- **Receiving**: the pass sets `receiving` on the target. The CPU turns to it; a lone human's control switches to the\n447\t  receiver at once (auto-switch, standard in hockey games).\n448\t- **One-timer**: a receiver who presses shoot while a pass is on its way and within 0.35 s of arriving, or who holds\n449\t  shoot when it arrives, fires on contact: speed = the slap formula at charge .85 × `T.oneTimerBonus` 1.15, and the\n450\t  aim error halves. The prompt `{shoot} ONE-TIMER!` pops over the human receiver while the pass flies.\n451\t- **Call for pass**: a human without the puck whose CPU teammate carries it presses `pass`; the carrier passes to\n452\t  them within 0.3 s if the lane is clear, otherwise as soon as it opens (up to 1.2 s). The human's indicator flashes\n453\t  \"!\".\n454\t\n455\t### 7.5 Shooting\n456\t- `shoot` with the puck: released within 0.18 s it is a **wrist shot**: `T.wristSpeed` 330 × shot multiplier\n457\t  (`0.85 + 0.05 Sht`), lift 2–10 at the goal, error σ 5 × (1.3 − 0.1 Sht). Held longer it is a **slapshot**: the\n458\t  skater winds up (slowed to 0.6×; a meter fills over `T.slapCharge` 0.9 s; a poke or check can strip it). On release:\n459\t  speed `(T.slapBase 380 + T.slapGain 160 × charge) × shot multiplier`, lift 4–18, σ `7 × (1.3 − 0.1 Sht) × (1.4 −\n460\t  0.4 charge)`.\n461\t- **The aim point in the net**: without aim input, the open side (the side farther from the goalie's center) at mid\n462\t  height. With stick aim, up and down on the stick pick near or far side (mirrored for each attack direction). With the\n463\t  mouse, where the reticle's line meets the mouth. Slapshots go **top shelf** (z 14–18) when the goalie is down.\n464\t- Turbo adds +12% speed, the Lumber item gives +30% and zero error, and KABOOM turns a charge ≥ .95 into a **KABOOM\n465\t  shot** (7.10).\n466\t- Every shot is logged with type (`wrist`, `slap`, `onetimer`, `kaboom`, `deke`, `rebound`, `deflect`), speed and\n467\t  distance. \"On goal\" means the shot's line crosses the goal line inside the mouth. Shots from anywhere count\n468\t  (dump-ins too).\n469\t\n470\t### 7.6 Goalies (`Goalie`)\n471\t- **Positioning**: on an arc in front of the goal center, radius 10–26 (out to 26 to cut the angle when the puck is\n472\t  far, back to 10 when it is close), on the bisector toward the puck. Lateral speed `T.goalieLateral` 150 × (0.85 +\n473\t  0.05 Rfx), with T-push bursts to 230. When the puck is behind the net, the goalie hugs the post on the puck's side.\n474\t  Idle animations: tapping the posts, a crouch bounce.\n475\t- **Save solver**: whenever the puck's line will cross the goal line inside the mouth within 1 s (a shot, pass or\n476\t  deflection), predict the crossing `(yc, zc, tc)`. After a reaction delay (`T.goalieReact` 0.16 − 0.015 (Rfx − 3) +\n477\t  difficulty offset, plus 0.08 if **screened** by a body within 14 of the shot line, plus 0.12 if **deked** within the\n478\t  last 0.5 s at under 70 range), the goalie moves toward `yc`, picks a save type and, when the puck crosses the\n479\t  goalie's plane, tests its **save shape**. All widths scale with `0.9 + 0.033 Size` × the item and boss factors:\n480\t  - standing: `|dy| < 8`, z 0–22;\n481\t  - butterfly (zc < 9): `|dy| < 14`, z 0–10, plus the upper body `|dy| < 6`, z 10–20;\n482\t  - glove (high, catching side) and blocker (high, other side): a reach disc of r 5 out to `dy ±15`, z 10–21;\n483\t  - stack (desperation, needs `|dy| > 12` in under 0.2 s): `|dy| < 18`, z 0–8, then 1 s to get up.\n484\t- **Outcome**: glove saves freeze (`T.gloveCatch` 0.55; then a whistle and a faceoff in that zone). Pad and blocker\n485\t  saves **rebound** at 0.35 v, ±50° away from the net. Butterfly saves: 40% smother, 60% rebound. Rebounds are live.\n486\t- **Poke check**: when a carrier comes within 22 in front, a 40% (× Rfx) chance to strip the puck.\n487\t- **Kaboom blast**: a KABOOM shot that hits a goalie blows them back (`blasted`, 1.2 s, flailing into the net). With\n488\t  `T.kaboomBlast` 0.6 the puck carries through (a goal); otherwise it drops dead in the crease.\n489\t- **Manual goalie** (shootout only, for the defending human): the stick moves along the arc and in or out; ✕\n490\t  butterfly, □ poke, ○ stack toward the stick. Glove and blocker reach is automatic within the standing shape.\n491\t- **Balance targets** (checked by `tests/balance.mjs`, 18.4): wrist shots from more than 150 away saved 88–96%;\n492\t  one-timers across the crease 40–60%; breakaway dekes 45–65%; KABOOM shots on target 20–40% saved.\n493\t\n494\t### 7.7 Checking, the glass, grudges (`Hits`)\n495\t- `shoot` without the puck starts `check` (0.3 s): a lunge of +60 along the facing and a shoulder-lead pose.\n496\t- **Contact** with a rival (r 8 each) during `check`: `impulse = T.checkPower 1.0 × (closing speed + 60) × (attacker\n497\t  mass / target mass) × (0.8 + 0.067 Hit) × (turbo 1.45) × (KABOOM 2.0) × (Poutine 1.6)`.\n498\t  - Below 90: **bump**. The target staggers 0.25 s; a carrier loses the puck 50% of the time.\n499\t  - 90 up to `T.knockdown` 150: **check**. The target stumbles 0.5 s and loses the puck.\n500\t  - 150 and up: **BIG HIT**. The target is knocked down (`down` for 1.4 s: a tumble, then a belly slide at 0.8 ×\n501\t    impulse along the normal, then `getup` 0.5 s). Hit-stop 0.07 s, a shake of 3, a zoom punch to 1.1, the crowd\n502\t    goes \"OHHH\", BOOM +18, and the target's grudge against the hitter +35.\n503\t- **The glass**: a body sliding or knocked into the boards faster than `T.glassCrack` 170 cracks the panel there. If\n504\t  the panel was already cracked, or the speed is over `T.glassShatter` 240, it shatters: shards (`bits` in light blue\n505\t  and white), a crash, the front-row fans flinch, BOOM +8 or +15, and the commentary calls it. A shattered panel lets\n506\t  the puck out. At the next stoppage two glass techs skate out and put a new panel in (1.5 s, cosmetic).\n507\t- **Accidental contact** knocks the referee or the mascot over too (comedy). Goalies can be knocked down only by a\n508\t  KABOOM check (the crowd boos).\n509\t- **Grudge** (per ordered pair, 0..100): +35 for being big-hit, +10 for being checked, +15 for being chirped, +10\n510\t  when the rival big-hits a teammate. It decays 4/s after 3 s of peace.\n511\t\n512\t### 7.8 Deke and poke\n513\t- **Deke** (`deke` with the puck): 0.45 s, a sideways cut of +90 toward the stick (alternating when the stick is\n514\t  neutral), a spin animation (a spin-o-rama with turbo). Checks in its first 0.3 s miss with chance `0.7 + 0.04 (Hnd −\n515\t  3)`. Cooldown 0.8 s. A goalie within 70 \"bites\" (7.6). A deke that leaves a defender behind within 1 s is a\n516\t  `deke_beat` event (BOOM +6, commentary).\n517\t- **Poke** (`deke` without the puck): 0.35 s, the blade reaches 18 ahead. If it passes within 8 of a carried puck,\n518\t  steal chance is `T.pokeBase 0.55 + 0.08 (pokerHnd − carrierHnd)`. A miss leaves the poker off balance for 0.3 s.\n519\t\n520\t### 7.9 Chirping (`chirp`)\n521\tPressing chirp makes the skater shout a line from `TEXT.chirps` at the nearest rival within 120: a speech bubble (2 s,\n522\ttiny font, wrapped to 90 px) and babble in their voice. BOOM +3; the target's grudge +15; cooldown 4 s. CPU skaters\n523\tchirp after big hits and goals (30%), and the human's chirps raise the chance that a CPU rival with Fight ≥ 4\n524\tchallenges.\n525\t\n526\t### 7.10 The BOOM meter and KABOOM mode (`Boom`)\n527\t- **One meter per team**, 0..100, × `T.boomGain` 1.0. Gains: big hit +18, check +6, glass crack +8 or shatter +15,\n528\t  fight win +45, fight loss +5, goal +20, shot on goal +4, save (to the goalie's team) +5, completed pass +2,\n529\t  one-timer +6, deke beat +6, chirp +3, BOOM Box item +40, mascot down +10, perfect Flood Wagon +30, Doris's organ\n530\t  (chapter 5) +30.\n531\t- **At 100 → KABOOM** for `T.kaboomTime` 15 s, or until the other team scores. A screen flash, an explosion burst over\n532\t  the team's bench, \"KA-BOOM!\" (title font, shaking), the arena lights tint the team's color with a pulse, flame\n533\t  cannons in the Dome, and the music's `kaboom` layer fades in (drums and distorted bass). For that team: infinite\n534\t  turbo, the slapshot charges 2× faster, a full charge fires a **KABOOM shot**, checks are 2× strong, skates throw\n535\t  sparks and leave molten `melt` trails, and their goalie reacts 0.03 s faster. The meter then resets to 0.\n536\t- **KABOOM shot**: 760 u/s with zero error. The puck is a fireball (a glowing sprite, fire particles every step, a light\n537\t  following it). Into the goalie → the blast (7.6). Into a skater → an explosion and a knockdown. Into the boards → an\n538\t  explosion, and a hit panel shatters. A KABOOM goal: the net tips back in an explosion, a confetti and fire burst, a\n539\t  double horn and fireworks in the Dome.\n540\t- **Gilded Mode** is the Grizzlies' KABOOM (chapter 5): the same rules with gold flames.\n541\t\n542\t### 7.11 Fights and the sin bin (`Fight`)\n543\t- **Trigger**: a human-controlled skater within 40 of a rival when either holds a grudge ≥ 40 against the other gets\n544\t  the prompt `HOLD {lob} — DROP THE GLOVES`. Holding △ for 0.5 s challenges. A CPU rival accepts with\n545\t  `clamp(0.4 + 0.12 (Fgt − 3) + grudge/200, 0.1, 0.95)` (forced in chapter 3 when the Bruise Brothers are involved).\n546\t  A human rival (local or online) gets `HOLD {lob} TO ACCEPT` for 3 s. Declining is **turtling**: the decliner's team\n547\t  BOOM −10 and the challenger's +10, and the crowd boos. A **CPU** with Fgt ≥ 4 and grudge ≥ 70 near a human-controlled\n548\t  skater challenges them the same way. At most one fight per 60 s of clock and `T.fightMax` 3 per game.\n549\t- **Staging**: a whistle; the clock stops; the camera moves to `brawler`, zoom 1.6, framing the two (`cam.frame`).\n550\t  Gloves and helmets drop as sprites on the ice; the other skaters circle at 50; the referee and the linesman hover;\n551\t  the crowd stands; the organ plays the fight vamp. The fight HUD shows two portraits with balance and stamina bars.\n552\t- **Fighters**: balance 100 (`T.fightBalance`) and stamina 100 (regen 25/s); damage × `0.8 + 0.067 Fgt`.\n553\t  - **Jab** (✕): 0.25 s, 6 damage, 8 stamina, staggers 0.12 s (rig: `jab`).\n554\t  - **Haymaker** (□): wind-up 0.35 s (a clear telegraph: the arm draws back, a glint), active 0.1, recover 0.35. 18\n555\t    damage (+6 if held up to 0.6 s), 22 stamina. A whiff leaves you open for 0.5 s (rig: `haymaker`, or `hook`\n556\t    alternating).\n557\t  - **Duck** (○): 0.35 s, immune to haymakers and half damage from jabs; 10 stamina; cooldown 0.4 (pose: `crouch` +\n558\t    lean back).\n559\t  - **Yank** (△): 0.3 s. If it lands, the rival's guard breaks for 0.6 s and they lose 15 stamina. **Three yanks\n560\t    within 4 s pull the jersey over their head** (their rig gets `hood: true` in jersey color): blind for 1.5 s.\n561\t  - With no stamina, everything is 40% slower.\n562\t  - The CPU fighter ducks a haymaker wind-up with probability = its skill, and otherwise mixes jabs, haymakers and\n563\t    yanks by personality.\n564\t- **End**: balance ≤ 0 → that fighter falls (`down`); the winner raises a fist (`cheer`); a crowd roar; the winner's\n565\t  team BOOM +45. The loser goes to the **sin bin** for `T.sinBin` 20 s of play clock (a \"POWER PLAY\" banner and timer\n566\t  under the score bug), seated in the box, then steps out through the box door. If 20 s pass, the linesmen separate\n567\t  them: a draw with no penalty and BOOM +10 each. Play resumes with a faceoff at the nearest dot.\n568\t\n569\t### 7.12 Fan throws, power-ups and hazards (`Items`)\n570\t- **Throws**: every `T.itemEvery` 25–45 s of play, and 25% of the time right after a big hit or goal, a fan in the\n571\t  stands throws (a lob arc from the crowd over the glass) onto the neutral or attacking zone. The item slides to a stop\n572\t  and lasts 12 s (blinking for its last 3). Arena pools are in 11.2.\n573\t- **Pickup**: a skater body within 12. Icons and timers show over the holder's head.\n574\t\n575\t| Item | Look | Effect |\n576\t|---|---|---|\n577\t| HOT SAUCE | red bottle (store `bottle`) | infinite turbo 8 s, fire trail |\n578\t| GRANDMA'S TAPE | white tape roll | 10 s: can't lose the puck to pokes or checks below a big hit; passes can't be intercepted |\n579\t| POUTINE | bowl of fries (store `bowl`) | 10 s: can't be knocked down; every check is a big hit (×1.6) |\n580\t| LUMBER | a stick with a lightning bolt | the next 3 shots: +30% speed, zero error |\n581\t| BRICK PADS | a brick | the holder's goalie grows ×1.35 for 12 s |\n582\t| BOOM BOX | a boombox | +40 team BOOM |\n583\t| HOT COCOA (pond only) | a steaming thermos | turbo refilled + 20% speed 8 s |\n584\t\n585\t| Hazard | Where | Effect |\n586\t|---|---|---|\n587\t| OCTOPUS | Grindhouse, Dome, cheat | a slip patch r 10: skaters crossing it `slip` (1.2 s, legs up, a slide); at the next stoppage the referee picks it up and twirls it overhead |\n588\t| RUBBER RAT | Grindhouse | scurries randomly for 10 s; trips skaters (as slip) |\n589\t| HATS | after any hat trick | 20–40 hats rain from the stands (cosmetic, swept up at the stoppage) |\n590\t\n591\t- **AI item greed**: a CPU skater not involved in the play (not the carrier, its marker or the pressure player)\n592\t  detours to an item within 120 (`T.aiItemGreed`).\n593\t- **Arena hazards**:\n594\t  - **Thin ice** (pond): 3 elliptical patches (40 × 24) at fixed spots outside the creases, each with integrity 100.\n595\t    A knockdown on a patch costs 50 and a big hit there 100. At 0 the patch breaks into a hole: black water, ripples\n596\t    and a splash. A skater who enters a hole is `frozen` for 3 s (rig tinted icy blue inside a translucent block),\n597\t    then pops out at the edge. A puck that falls in is lost, then a faceoff. Holes refreeze (as a darker patch) after\n598\t    30 s or at intermission.\n599\t  - **Snowbanks** (pond): the boards are snowbanks with no glass. Restitution .3 and a snow puff. A big hit into one\n600\t    leaves the target `buried` for 1.5 s with only the head and skates showing.\n601\t  - **Polar Pete** (mall): the mascot skates figure eights in the neutral zone during play. A moving obstacle (mass\n602\t    1.5) that can be checked (\"MASCOT DOWN!\", BOOM +10); it gets up after 3 s and waves.\n603\t  - **Discount Drop** (mall): every 40 s a ceiling claw lowers a crate to center ice; it breaks into a power-up.\n604\t\n605\t### 7.13 Team AI (`AI`)\n606\t- **Cadence**: each CPU skater re-thinks every `lerp(0.3, 0.12, skill)` s and reacts after `lerp(0.35, 0.1, skill)`\n607\t  s; between decisions it steers. Steering: seek the target, stay 12 from the boards unless chasing the puck, keep 40\n608\t  from teammates, and avoid rivals while carrying.\n609\t- **With the puck** (offense):\n610\t  - **Carrier**: shoot when in the shooting zone (within 200 of the net, within ±60° of its axis, at most one body in the\n611\t    lane), or when a one-timer pass is on. Pass when pressured (a rival within 26 ahead) or when a teammate is clearly\n612\t    better placed (open lane, at least 60 closer to the net). Deke when a defender is square in front within 30 (40%\n613\t    × Hnd/3). Otherwise carry toward the net, slaloming around defenders, with turbo in open ice.\n614\t  - **Support forward**: get open on the far side at the dot height (about 150 from the goal line); once the carrier\n615\t    crosses the blue line, drift to the far post or the slot for a one-timer.\n616\t  - **Point**: stay at the blue line as an outlet; crash the net for rebounds when aggression is high.\n617\t- **Without the puck** (defense):\n618\t  - **Pressure**: the nearest skater intercepts the carrier's position 0.3 s ahead, then checks (when Hit ≥ 3 and\n619\t    `RNG.sim() < aggression`) or pokes.\n620\t  - **Cover**: marks the most dangerous rival without the puck (in the passing lane, or between them and the net).\n621\t  - **Home**: guards the slot between the puck and its own net.\n622\t- **Loose puck**: each team sends the skater who can reach the predicted puck position first. The rest take offense or\n623\t  defense spots according to which team will probably win the race.\n624\t- **Faceoffs**: centers face off at the dot; wingers line up on both sides; the point man behind.\n625\t- **Difficulty** (Settings): Rookie, Pro, All-Star, Legend set AI skill .35 / .55 / .75 / .95, CPU goalie reaction\n626\t  offsets +.06 / +.02 / 0 / −.02 s, and the human team's goalie −.03 / −.01 / 0 / +.01. Light rubber-banding (CPU\n627\t  skill −.1 while it leads by 3 or more) on Rookie only.\n628\t- **Teammates of humans** use the same AI and also obey call-for-pass. Team tactics from story choices: **Finesse**\n629\t  (pass bias +30%, speed +4%) or **Grit** (check bias +30%, BOOM gain +15%).\n630\t\n631\t### 7.14 Match flow (`Match`)\n632\t- **Configuration**: `{ home, away, arena, periods: 3, periodLen: 120, ot: 'sudden' (120 s, 3-on-3) | 'none',\n633\t  shootout: true, intros: true, replays: 'auto', flood: 'ask' | 'always' | 'never', difficulty, cheats, objectives,\n634\t  script, humans: [{ team, input }] }`.\n635\t- **Phases**: `intro` → `faceoff` → `play` ⇄ `stoppage` → `goal` → `replay` → `faceoff` … `periodEnd` →\n636\t  `intermission` (Flood Wagon) → `faceoff` … `final` → `results`. Also `fight`, `ot`, `shootout` and `celebration`.\n637\t  The clock counts down only in `play`. The engine's pause freezes everything.\n638\t- **Faceoff**: the referee holds the puck, raises an arm and drops it after a random 0.6–1.2 s. Each center presses\n639\t  `pass` or `shoot` when it drops; the earlier press within 0–0.25 s after the drop wins (a press before the drop is a\n640\t  slow, mistimed swipe); a CPU center reacts after its skill delay. The winner's swipe sends the puck back to a\n641\t  teammate.\n642\t- **Stoppages**: a frozen puck, the puck out of play, after a fight, at the end of a sin-bin call. Each brings a\n643\t  whistle, a 1.5 s pause, a lower-third stat card (shots, hits, faceoffs %), an organ sting, and then the faceoff.\n644\t- **Goals**: the horn (3 s), the red goal light spinning behind that net, the team's goal song sting, the crowd jumping,\n645\t  the scorer's celebration (chosen by personality: fist pump, sniper aim, knee slide, stick guitar, a bounce off the\n646\t  glass), and teammates converging. \"GOAL!\" in the title font, the scoring summary (scorer and assists, the\n647\t  last two touches by the scorer's team), then an **instant replay** (7.16), then a center faceoff.\n648\t- **Hat trick**: a player's third goal makes hats rain, and the commentary calls it. **Hoser Hat Trick**: one player\n649\t  with a goal, an assist and a fight win in one game, shown as a toast.\n650\t- **Periods**: the buzzer at 0:00, then the period summary card. **Intermission**: the Flood Wagon minigame (offered\n651\t  per the `flood` option; skipping runs a 6 s AI resurfacing fast-forward), then the next period. Teams switch ends\n652\t  every period.\n653\t- **Overtime**: sudden death; a tie after it goes to the shootout (exhibition and story). In session mode: at most 60\n654\t  s of sudden death, then a tie.\n655\t- **Shootout**: 3 rounds each (home first), then sudden-death rounds. A shooter starts at center with the puck and an\n656\t  8-second shot clock; the attempt ends on a shot, a save, a goal, or the puck going backward. Humans shoot for their\n657\t  team (the skaters rotate) and play goalie against the CPU's shooters (6.1). The HUD shows big ✓ and ✗ marks.\n658\t- **Final**: the final horn, the winning team celebrates, the losers slump (`kneel`), then **results**.\n659\t- **Stats** per skater: goals, assists, shots, hits, big hits, takeaways, fights won, turbo used, top shot speed.\n660\t  Per goalie: saves and shots against. Per team: everything summed, plus BOOM filled and Kabooms.\n661\t- **Three stars**: rank players by `3 G + 2 A + 0.5 bigHits + 1.5 fightsWon + 0.3 shots` (goalies:\n662\t  `0.12 saves + 2 × (save% − .85) × 10`) and announce the third, second and first stars, each with a portrait card and a\n663\t  commentary line.\n664\t- **Objectives**: declarative `{ id, text, on: 'goal' | 'hit' | …, where(e, match) }` counters plus a `need`, checked\n665\t  live. A star toast when one is met.\n666\t\n667\t### 7.15 Camera director (`Cam`)\n668\t- **Play**: focus on the puck (or carrier) plus a lead of 0.25 s of puck velocity. If a lone human's skater is more\n669\t  than 220 from the puck, shift 25% toward them. With several local humans, `cam.frame([puck, ...humans],\n670\t  { margin: 60, zoom: [.78, 1] })`. `cam.smooth` .15; bounds from `map.bounds(view)`.\n671\t- **Zoom**: 1.0 (Settings → Camera distance: Near 1.15, Normal 1.0, Far 0.85); 1.15 at faceoffs; a 1.1 punch on big\n672\t  hits (0.3 s); out to 0.85 briefly when the puck flies faster than 400.\n673\t- **Fights**: `brawler`, zoom 1.6, framing the fighters. **Celebrations**: 1.3 on the scorer. **Intros**: a dolly\n674\t  along the lineup. **Replays**: 7.16. Then back to the player's camera setting (Broadcast `threequarter` or Overhead\n675\t  `topdown`, cycled by the `camera` action and saved).\n676\t\n677\t### 7.16 Instant replay (`Replay`)\n678\t- **Recorder**: every second step, push `{ puck, skaters and goalies: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, rigState }, events }`\n679\t  into an 8 s ring buffer. `rigState` is the object passed to `rig.update`, so the replay re-poses rigs exactly.\n680\t- **Goal replay**: once the celebration has played for 1.5 s, cut (a puck-shaped wipe) to the last 4 s before the goal\n681\t  at 0.5× in the `brawler` view following the puck at zoom 1.25, with letterbox bars, a \"REPLAY\" bug, and the\n682\t  recorded events re-firing their effects. ✕ (or confirm) skips. Setting: Replays Auto or Off. Big-hit and Kaboom\n683\t  replays (3 s) also play at the next stoppage when Replays is Auto: when such an event happens, copy its clip (2 s\n684\t  before to 1 s after) out of the ring buffer, because the buffer will have moved on by the stoppage.\n685\t- **Highlights**: keep the 3 best clips of a story run (goal type and hit power score them) in memory for the end\n686\t  credits.\n687\t\n688\t### 7.17 Commentary (`Talk`)\n689\t- **Booth**: CHUCK WALLOP (play-by-play) and MOOSE PLUNKETT (color), with live portraits (rigs in suits) in a bottom\n690\t  subtitle box. Two lines at most; non-modal, auto-advancing (`talk.say(text, { modal: false, auto: 2.4, portrait,\n691\t  name })`).\n692\t- **Selection**: each event type has a pool (`TEXT.talk[type]`) with priority and cooldowns: a global 1.2 s, the\n693\t  same line 120 s, the same type 6 s. Goals, fights, Kabooms and glass breaks interrupt; filler (Moose's anecdotes)\n694\t  only plays after 8 s of quiet play. Variables: `{name} {team} {victim} {goalie} {score} {arena} {period}`.\n695\t- **Voices**: every line babbles (10.1) in the speaker's voice. Settings: Commentary On/Off, Subtitles On/Off,\n696\t  Voices volume.\n697\t- **Tips** (Coach Marge) are separate: a banner just below the score bug with glyph chips, shown the first time its\n698\t  trigger fires per save profile (Appendix D).\n699\t\n700\t### 7.18 HUD (`Hud`; it keeps clear of `game.cornerArea()` and inside a 92% title-safe area)\n701\t- **Score bug** (top center, about 200 × 30): team logo chips, abbreviations, scores at font scale 2, the period\n702\t  (`1ST 2ND 3RD OT SO`), the clock `m:ss`, and under each team its BOOM meter (80 × 4; flames and a countdown while in\n703\t  KABOOM).\n704\t- **Power play** strip under it: `POWER PLAY MUK 0:14`, with the sin-binned player's tag.\n705\t- **Player markers**: a colored ring decal under each human's skater (P1–P4 in `E.PLAYER_COLORS`, the seat colors\n706\t  online), a chevron with `P1` above, and an arrow on the screen edge when they are off screen. A turbo bar (16 × 2)\n707\t  under the chevron. The shot meter above the shooter while charging (gold when full).\n708\t- **Radar** (bottom right, about 108 × 48): the rink outline, skaters as team-colored dots, humans as larger dots with\n709\t  rings, the puck white.\n710\t- **Prompts** (bottom center, above the subtitles): context chips (`{shoot} ONE-TIMER!`, `HOLD {lob} DROP THE GLOVES`,\n711\t  `{pass} SKIP`).\n712\t- **Banners**: GOAL!, SAVE!, POST!, BIG HIT!, THROUGH THE GLASS!, KA-BOOM!, FIGHT!, POWER PLAY, HAT TRICK!, PERIOD\n713\t  2, FINAL, in the title font with shake and color cycling (honoring reduce motion).\n714\t- **Fight HUD**: two portraits with bars at the top corners, and the fight control chips at the bottom.\n715\t- **Lower-thirds** at stoppages: one broadcast-style stat card for 3 s.\n716\t\n717\t---\n718\t\n719\t## 8. Art direction"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"6326645d-6259-4e2d-b8c3-4a88111284b6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:02.647Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","content":"\nAll distances in world units (u), times in seconds. `T.name` marks a tunable (Appendix A has every default).\n\n### 7.1 The rink (`Rink`)\n- **Arena map**: a TileMap of 70 × 44 tiles (1120 × 704 u); rink center `C = (560, 400)`.\n- **Rink**: a rounded rectangle with half-length 432, half-width 192 and corner radius 96 (x 128–992, y 208–592).\n  `Rink.inside(x, y, r)`, `Rink.normalAt(x, y)` and `Rink.clamp(body, r)` are analytic: no stair-stepped corners.\n- **Markings** (painted by `floorTex(x, y)`, baked once per arena): red center line (5 u) at `C.x`; blue lines (5 u)\n  at `C.x ± 108`; red goal lines (2 u) at `C.x ± 376`; 5 faceoff circles of radius 72 (center, and the end-zone dots at\n  `C.x ± 280, C.y ± 112`); neutral-zone dots at `C.x ± 84, C.y ± 112`; creases (half-discs of radius 28, light blue\n  `#9fd3ff` with a red rim); the center-ice logo (the home team's logo sprite scaled x3, sampled per pixel); ice\n  `#e9f3fb` with subtle noise, cool shading near the boards and a faint sheen. Outside the rink: rubber matting or\n  concrete; the pond uses snow.\n- **Goals**: the mouth spans `y = C.y ± 16` (32 wide, from post center to post center), the crossbar is at z 20, and\n  the net runs 20 deep behind the goal line. Posts are cylinders of r 1.5. The net's mesh is translucent white (a\n  blend at .35, lines every 3 px) and **bulges** where the puck hits (6 control points that spring back, k = 18).\n- **Boards**: 17 high (white, with a 2-u yellow kick plate, ads on the straight runs, and a top cap in the home\n  color). Glass rises 28 above the boards on the sides and 40 at the ends. It is split into **48 panels** (14 per side,\n  4 per end, 3 per corner arc), each with a state of `ok`, `cracked` or `shattered`, and the stanchions show between\n  them.\n- **Drawing order**: the floor first, then the scuff decals, then the far (north) boards, glass, benches, sin bins and\n  stands as background (skaters are always in front of them), then the end and corner panels queued one by one (`r.queue`\n  at the panel's center, so they sort per panel), then the near (south) boards queued **cut low** (6 u, no glass, only\n  the top rail), so they never hide play. Glass draws with `px.blend(.25)`, a white highlight streak, and crack lines\n  or an empty frame by state.\n- **Stands**: north of the benches (y 0–176) in 5 stepped tiers (TileMap wall types 24–64 high, with `face`\n  materials per arena), and at the west and east ends (x 0–112 and 1008–1120). Nothing is built south of the near\n  boards' apron; the near crowd is the screen-space silhouette row (section 8).\n- **Benches and sin bins** sit on the far side, outside the boards (y 184–208): the home bench at x `C.x−216…C.x−72`,\n  the away bench at `C.x+72…C.x+216`, the sin bins at `C.x−60…C.x−12` (home) and `C.x+12…C.x+60` (away), and the\n  scorekeeper between them. Each team's bench holds 2 sitting spares and its coach standing. A skater in the sin bin\n  sits in the box, visible.\n- **Scuff layer**: a grid of 54 × 24 cells (16 u) of `scuff` 0..1 and `melt` 0..1. Skating adds\n  `0.0025 × speed/132` per step to its cell, a hockey stop +0.12, a knockdown +0.2 in radius 1, Kaboom skates\n  `melt` +0.05 a step. Draw with `r.decal`: each cell over .05 draws 1–4 scratch lines (a pattern from the cell's hash,\n  alpha by scuff), and melt draws blue-grey puddles with a shine. The Flood Wagon clears both.\n\n### 7.2 Skating (`Skater.skateStep`, pure: the network prediction runs it too)\n- Max speed `T.skateMax` 132 × the speed rating (`0.85 + 0.05 × Spd`), × `T.turboMul` 1.45 with turbo, × 0.94 when\n  carrying the puck, and × 0.6 while winding up a slapshot.\n- Acceleration `T.skateAccel` 300 × `(1 − 0.6 (v/vmax)²)` along the stick. Gliding with no input decelerates by\n  `T.iceGlide` 28.\n- **Turning**: the velocity heading rotates toward the stick direction at `lerp(T.turnSlow 5.0, T.turnFast 2.6,\n  v/vmax)` rad/s. The sideways component of velocity relative to the facing decays at `T.edgeGrip` 6/s, which gives\n  carves rather than slides.\n- **Hockey stop**: when the stick points more than 120° from the velocity at speed > 60, the skater enters `stop`\n  (at least 0.22 s): deceleration `T.stopDecel` 700, a snow spray (event `stop`), the torso turned 70°. The skater then\n  accelerates the new way.\n- Facing follows velocity (the AI may skate backward at 0.75× speed to keep facing the puck, using C-cut legs).\n- **Turbo** meter 0..1: drains `T.turboDrain` 0.45/s while held and moving, and regenerates `T.turboRegen` 0.18/s\n  once released for 0.6 s.\n- **Bodies**: r 7. Masses: heroic 1.0, bulky 1.35, goalie 1.6 (The Vault 2.2). Skater–skater overlap pushes them\n  apart with a restitution of .3. A collision without the check state is a \"bump\": no knockdown unless the closing\n  speed is above `T.accidentalHit` 180.\n- **Boards**: reflect the normal velocity × .3 and keep 85% of the tangential. Faster than 120 into the boards: a\n  \"rattle\" event (sound, glass shake).\n\n### 7.3 The puck (`Puck`)\n- r 1.6, drawn as a black ellipse of 3×2 px with a 1-px highlight, plus a shadow. Above 300 u/s it gets a streak; the\n  **Puck trail** setting chooses Off, Streak or Glow (neon).\n- Free motion: `v −= (T.puckFriction 26 + T.puckDrag 0.12 × |v|) dt`. Gravity 700 in the air. Hitting the ice: vz ×\n  −0.3, and speed × 0.9 when vz was below −60. Speed cap 760.\n- **4 substeps** per step, each a swept test against: the boards (restitution `T.boardBounce` .62 normal, .92\n  tangential; the glass .5 when z > 17); posts (.82 plus a **ping** event; the crossbar when z is 19–21 inside the\n  mouth); the net (from behind or the sides .2, a \"net\" sound); goalies (section 7.6); sticks (pickup or deflection);\n  bodies (r 7: .35, a \"body\" event; a shot hitting a skater is a **block**). Over the glass top, or through a\n  shattered panel: **out of play**, then a faceoff at the nearest end-zone dot.\n- **Goal**: the puck's center crosses the goal line inside the mouth (`|y − C.y| < 16 − 1.6`) with z < 20 − 1.6,\n  moving inward. The puck stays in the net (`inNet`; the bulge plays).\n- **Possession**: the owner's blade point is `pos + R(facing) · [11, hand × 4]` (`hand` +1 right shot, −1 left, from\n  the player data). The puck eases toward the blade at k = 30/s and weaves ±3 across (`sin(t × 9)`) at low speed.\n- **Pickup**: a loose puck within `T.pickupRadius` 8 × the handling multiplier of the blade point (or 10 of the body\n  center), at z < 6, after the skater's `pickupCooldown` (0.25 s once it releases the puck). If the relative speed is\n  under 300 it is taken. Faster, it is caught with chance `clamp(1.3 − rel/450 + 0.08 (Hnd − 3), 0.1, 1)`, otherwise\n  it deflects off the blade (reflected around the blade's normal at 0.5×).\n- **Puck battles**: when opposing blades are both within 8 of a loose or carried puck, every 0.2 s the one with the\n  higher `Hnd + Hit/2 + RNG.sim() × 3` takes it (a \"battle\" event, stick-clack sounds).\n\n### 7.4 Passing\n- **Target**: the teammate whose bearing is nearest the aim within 75°; otherwise the nearest teammate ahead; with\n  mouse or right-stick aim, the teammate nearest the reticle within 80, otherwise a pass to the space at the reticle.\n- **Lead**: aim at `mate.pos + mate.v × tFlight × 0.9`, iterated twice; speed `clamp(220 + 0.9 d, 240, 420) ×\n  (0.9 + 0.033 Pas)`; angular error σ = `0.06 × (1.3 − 0.1 Pas)` rad.\n- **Interception**: an opponent's blade that comes within 8 of the puck's path tries a pickup (7.3).\n- **Saucer pass** (`lob`): `E.arc` with apex 10 and speed × 0.8. It can't be intercepted while z > 6, lands near the\n  mate and wobbles on landing.\n- **Receiving**: the pass sets `receiving` on the target. The CPU turns to it; a lone human's control switches to the\n  receiver at once (auto-switch, standard in hockey games).\n- **One-timer**: a receiver who presses shoot while a pass is on its way and within 0.35 s of arriving, or who holds\n  shoot when it arrives, fires on contact: speed = the slap formula at charge .85 × `T.oneTimerBonus` 1.15, and the\n  aim error halves. The prompt `{shoot} ONE-TIMER!` pops over the human receiver while the pass flies.\n- **Call for pass**: a human without the puck whose CPU teammate carries it presses `pass`; the carrier passes to\n  them within 0.3 s if the lane is clear, otherwise as soon as it opens (up to 1.2 s). The human's indicator flashes\n  \"!\".\n\n### 7.5 Shooting\n- `shoot` with the puck: released within 0.18 s it is a **wrist shot**: `T.wristSpeed` 330 × shot multiplier\n  (`0.85 + 0.05 Sht`), lift 2–10 at the goal, error σ 5 × (1.3 − 0.1 Sht). Held longer it is a **slapshot**: the\n  skater winds up (slowed to 0.6×; a meter fills over `T.slapCharge` 0.9 s; a poke or check can strip it). On release:\n  speed `(T.slapBase 380 + T.slapGain 160 × charge) × shot multiplier`, lift 4–18, σ `7 × (1.3 − 0.1 Sht) × (1.4 −\n  0.4 charge)`.\n- **The aim point in the net**: without aim input, the open side (the side farther from the goalie's center) at mid\n  height. With stick aim, up and down on the stick pick near or far side (mirrored for each attack direction). With the\n  mouse, where the reticle's line meets the mouth. Slapshots go **top shelf** (z 14–18) when the goalie is down.\n- Turbo adds +12% speed, the Lumber item gives +30% and zero error, and KABOOM turns a charge ≥ .95 into a **KABOOM\n  shot** (7.10).\n- Every shot is logged with type (`wrist`, `slap`, `onetimer`, `kaboom`, `deke`, `rebound`, `deflect`), speed and\n  distance. \"On goal\" means the shot's line crosses the goal line inside the mouth. Shots from anywhere count\n  (dump-ins too).\n\n### 7.6 Goalies (`Goalie`)\n- **Positioning**: on an arc in front of the goal center, radius 10–26 (out to 26 to cut the angle when the puck is\n  far, back to 10 when it is close), on the bisector toward the puck. Lateral speed `T.goalieLateral` 150 × (0.85 +\n  0.05 Rfx), with T-push bursts to 230. When the puck is behind the net, the goalie hugs the post on the puck's side.\n  Idle animations: tapping the posts, a crouch bounce.\n- **Save solver**: whenever the puck's line will cross the goal line inside the mouth within 1 s (a shot, pass or\n  deflection), predict the crossing `(yc, zc, tc)`. After a reaction delay (`T.goalieReact` 0.16 − 0.015 (Rfx − 3) +\n  difficulty offset, plus 0.08 if **screened** by a body within 14 of the shot line, plus 0.12 if **deked** within the\n  last 0.5 s at under 70 range), the goalie moves toward `yc`, picks a save type and, when the puck crosses the\n  goalie's plane, tests its **save shape**. All widths scale with `0.9 + 0.033 Size` × the item and boss factors:\n  - standing: `|dy| < 8`, z 0–22;\n  - butterfly (zc < 9): `|dy| < 14`, z 0–10, plus the upper body `|dy| < 6`, z 10–20;\n  - glove (high, catching side) and blocker (high, other side): a reach disc of r 5 out to `dy ±15`, z 10–21;\n  - stack (desperation, needs `|dy| > 12` in under 0.2 s): `|dy| < 18`, z 0–8, then 1 s to get up.\n- **Outcome**: glove saves freeze (`T.gloveCatch` 0.55; then a whistle and a faceoff in that zone). Pad and blocker\n  saves **rebound** at 0.35 v, ±50° away from the net. Butterfly saves: 40% smother, 60% rebound. Rebounds are live.\n- **Poke check**: when a carrier comes within 22 in front, a 40% (× Rfx) chance to strip the puck.\n- **Kaboom blast**: a KABOOM shot that hits a goalie blows them back (`blasted`, 1.2 s, flailing into the net). With\n  `T.kaboomBlast` 0.6 the puck carries through (a goal); otherwise it drops dead in the crease.\n- **Manual goalie** (shootout only, for the defending human): the stick moves along the arc and in or out; ✕\n  butterfly, □ poke, ○ stack toward the stick. Glove and blocker reach is automatic within the standing shape.\n- **Balance targets** (checked by `tests/balance.mjs`, 18.4): wrist shots from more than 150 away saved 88–96%;\n  one-timers across the crease 40–60%; breakaway dekes 45–65%; KABOOM shots on target 20–40% saved.\n\n### 7.7 Checking, the glass, grudges (`Hits`)\n- `shoot` without the puck starts `check` (0.3 s): a lunge of +60 along the facing and a shoulder-lead pose.\n- **Contact** with a rival (r 8 each) during `check`: `impulse = T.checkPower 1.0 × (closing speed + 60) × (attacker\n  mass / target mass) × (0.8 + 0.067 Hit) × (turbo 1.45) × (KABOOM 2.0) × (Poutine 1.6)`.\n  - Below 90: **bump**. The target staggers 0.25 s; a carrier loses the puck 50% of the time.\n  - 90 up to `T.knockdown` 150: **check**. The target stumbles 0.5 s and loses the puck.\n  - 150 and up: **BIG HIT**. The target is knocked down (`down` for 1.4 s: a tumble, then a belly slide at 0.8 ×\n    impulse along the normal, then `getup` 0.5 s). Hit-stop 0.07 s, a shake of 3, a zoom punch to 1.1, the crowd\n    goes \"OHHH\", BOOM +18, and the target's grudge against the hitter +35.\n- **The glass**: a body sliding or knocked into the boards faster than `T.glassCrack` 170 cracks the panel there. If\n  the panel was already cracked, or the speed is over `T.glassShatter` 240, it shatters: shards (`bits` in light blue\n  and white), a crash, the front-row fans flinch, BOOM +8 or +15, and the commentary calls it. A shattered panel lets\n  the puck out. At the next stoppage two glass techs skate out and put a new panel in (1.5 s, cosmetic).\n- **Accidental contact** knocks the referee or the mascot over too (comedy). Goalies can be knocked down only by a\n  KABOOM check (the crowd boos).\n- **Grudge** (per ordered pair, 0..100): +35 for being big-hit, +10 for being checked, +15 for being chirped, +10\n  when the rival big-hits a teammate. It decays 4/s after 3 s of peace.\n\n### 7.8 Deke and poke\n- **Deke** (`deke` with the puck): 0.45 s, a sideways cut of +90 toward the stick (alternating when the stick is\n  neutral), a spin animation (a spin-o-rama with turbo). Checks in its first 0.3 s miss with chance `0.7 + 0.04 (Hnd −\n  3)`. Cooldown 0.8 s. A goalie within 70 \"bites\" (7.6). A deke that leaves a defender behind within 1 s is a\n  `deke_beat` event (BOOM +6, commentary).\n- **Poke** (`deke` without the puck): 0.35 s, the blade reaches 18 ahead. If it passes within 8 of a carried puck,\n  steal chance is `T.pokeBase 0.55 + 0.08 (pokerHnd − carrierHnd)`. A miss leaves the poker off balance for 0.3 s.\n\n### 7.9 Chirping (`chirp`)\nPressing chirp makes the skater shout a line from `TEXT.chirps` at the nearest rival within 120: a speech bubble (2 s,\ntiny font, wrapped to 90 px) and babble in their voice. BOOM +3; the target's grudge +15; cooldown 4 s. CPU skaters\nchirp after big hits and goals (30%), and the human's chirps raise the chance that a CPU rival with Fight ≥ 4\nchallenges.\n\n### 7.10 The BOOM meter and KABOOM mode (`Boom`)\n- **One meter per team**, 0..100, × `T.boomGain` 1.0. Gains: big hit +18, check +6, glass crack +8 or shatter +15,\n  fight win +45, fight loss +5, goal +20, shot on goal +4, save (to the goalie's team) +5, completed pass +2,\n  one-timer +6, deke beat +6, chirp +3, BOOM Box item +40, mascot down +10, perfect Flood Wagon +30, Doris's organ\n  (chapter 5) +30.\n- **At 100 → KABOOM** for `T.kaboomTime` 15 s, or until the other team scores. A screen flash, an explosion burst over\n  the team's bench, \"KA-BOOM!\" (title font, shaking), the arena lights tint the team's color with a pulse, flame\n  cannons in the Dome, and the music's `kaboom` layer fades in (drums and distorted bass). For that team: infinite\n  turbo, the slapshot charges 2× faster, a full charge fires a **KABOOM shot**, checks are 2× strong, skates throw\n  sparks and leave molten `melt` trails, and their goalie reacts 0.03 s faster. The meter then resets to 0.\n- **KABOOM shot**: 760 u/s with zero error. The puck is a fireball (a glowing sprite, fire particles every step, a light\n  following it). Into the goalie → the blast (7.6). Into a skater → an explosion and a knockdown. Into the boards → an\n  explosion, and a hit panel shatters. A KABOOM goal: the net tips back in an explosion, a confetti and fire burst, a\n  double horn and fireworks in the Dome.\n- **Gilded Mode** is the Grizzlies' KABOOM (chapter 5): the same rules with gold flames.\n\n### 7.11 Fights and the sin bin (`Fight`)\n- **Trigger**: a human-controlled skater within 40 of a rival when either holds a grudge ≥ 40 against the other gets\n  the prompt `HOLD {lob} — DROP THE GLOVES`. Holding △ for 0.5 s challenges. A CPU rival accepts with\n  `clamp(0.4 + 0.12 (Fgt − 3) + grudge/200, 0.1, 0.95)` (forced in chapter 3 when the Bruise Brothers are involved).\n  A human rival (local or online) gets `HOLD {lob} TO ACCEPT` for 3 s. Declining is **turtling**: the decliner's team\n  BOOM −10 and the challenger's +10, and the crowd boos. A **CPU** with Fgt ≥ 4 and grudge ≥ 70 near a human-controlled\n  skater challenges them the same way. At most one fight per 60 s of clock and `T.fightMax` 3 per game.\n- **Staging**: a whistle; the clock stops; the camera moves to `brawler`, zoom 1.6, framing the two (`cam.frame`).\n  Gloves and helmets drop as sprites on the ice; the other skaters circle at 50; the referee and the linesman hover;\n  the crowd stands; the organ plays the fight vamp. The fight HUD shows two portraits with balance and stamina bars.\n- **Fighters**: balance 100 (`T.fightBalance`) and stamina 100 (regen 25/s); damage × `0.8 + 0.067 Fgt`.\n  - **Jab** (✕): 0.25 s, 6 damage, 8 stamina, staggers 0.12 s (rig: `jab`).\n  - **Haymaker** (□): wind-up 0.35 s (a clear telegraph: the arm draws back, a glint), active 0.1, recover 0.35. 18\n    damage (+6 if held up to 0.6 s), 22 stamina. A whiff leaves you open for 0.5 s (rig: `haymaker`, or `hook`\n    alternating).\n  - **Duck** (○): 0.35 s, immune to haymakers and half damage from jabs; 10 stamina; cooldown 0.4 (pose: `crouch` +\n    lean back).\n  - **Yank** (△): 0.3 s. If it lands, the rival's guard breaks for 0.6 s and they lose 15 stamina. **Three yanks\n    within 4 s pull the jersey over their head** (their rig gets `hood: true` in jersey color): blind for 1.5 s.\n  - With no stamina, everything is 40% slower.\n  - The CPU fighter ducks a haymaker wind-up with probability = its skill, and otherwise mixes jabs, haymakers and\n    yanks by personality.\n- **End**: balance ≤ 0 → that fighter falls (`down`); the winner raises a fist (`cheer`); a crowd roar; the winner's\n  team BOOM +45. The loser goes to the **sin bin** for `T.sinBin` 20 s of play clock (a \"POWER PLAY\" banner and timer\n  under the score bug), seated in the box, then steps out through the box door. If 20 s pass, the linesmen separate\n  them: a draw with no penalty and BOOM +10 each. Play resumes with a faceoff at the nearest dot.\n\n### 7.12 Fan throws, power-ups and hazards (`Items`)\n- **Throws**: every `T.itemEvery` 25–45 s of play, and 25% of the time right after a big hit or goal, a fan in the\n  stands throws (a lob arc from the crowd over the glass) onto the neutral or attacking zone. The item slides to a stop\n  and lasts 12 s (blinking for its last 3). Arena pools are in 11.2.\n- **Pickup**: a skater body within 12. Icons and timers show over the holder's head.\n\n| Item | Look | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| HOT SAUCE | red bottle (store `bottle`) | infinite turbo 8 s, fire trail |\n| GRANDMA'S TAPE | white tape roll | 10 s: can't lose the puck to pokes or checks below a big hit; passes can't be intercepted |\n| POUTINE | bowl of fries (store `bowl`) | 10 s: can't be knocked down; every check is a big hit (×1.6) |\n| LUMBER | a stick with a lightning bolt | the next 3 shots: +30% speed, zero error |\n| BRICK PADS | a brick | the holder's goalie grows ×1.35 for 12 s |\n| BOOM BOX | a boombox | +40 team BOOM |\n| HOT COCOA (pond only) | a steaming thermos | turbo refilled + 20% speed 8 s |\n\n| Hazard | Where | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| OCTOPUS | Grindhouse, Dome, cheat | a slip patch r 10: skaters crossing it `slip` (1.2 s, legs up, a slide); at the next stoppage the referee picks it up and twirls it overhead |\n| RUBBER RAT | Grindhouse | scurries randomly for 10 s; trips skaters (as slip) |\n| HATS | after any hat trick | 20–40 hats rain from the stands (cosmetic, swept up at the stoppage) |\n\n- **AI item greed**: a CPU skater not involved in the play (not the carrier, its marker or the pressure player)\n  detours to an item within 120 (`T.aiItemGreed`).\n- **Arena hazards**:\n  - **Thin ice** (pond): 3 elliptical patches (40 × 24) at fixed spots outside the creases, each with integrity 100.\n    A knockdown on a patch costs 50 and a big hit there 100. At 0 the patch breaks into a hole: black water, ripples\n    and a splash. A skater who enters a hole is `frozen` for 3 s (rig tinted icy blue inside a translucent block),\n    then pops out at the edge. A puck that falls in is lost, then a faceoff. Holes refreeze (as a darker patch) after\n    30 s or at intermission.\n  - **Snowbanks** (pond): the boards are snowbanks with no glass. Restitution .3 and a snow puff. A big hit into one\n    leaves the target `buried` for 1.5 s with only the head and skates showing.\n  - **Polar Pete** (mall): the mascot skates figure eights in the neutral zone during play. A moving obstacle (mass\n    1.5) that can be checked (\"MASCOT DOWN!\", BOOM +10); it gets up after 3 s and waves.\n  - **Discount Drop** (mall): every 40 s a ceiling claw lowers a crate to center ice; it breaks into a power-up.\n\n### 7.13 Team AI (`AI`)\n- **Cadence**: each CPU skater re-thinks every `lerp(0.3, 0.12, skill)` s and reacts after `lerp(0.35, 0.1, skill)`\n  s; between decisions it steers. Steering: seek the target, stay 12 from the boards unless chasing the puck, keep 40\n  from teammates, and avoid rivals while carrying.\n- **With the puck** (offense):\n  - **Carrier**: shoot when in the shooting zone (within 200 of the net, within ±60° of its axis, at most one body in the\n    lane), or when a one-timer pass is on. Pass when pressured (a rival within 26 ahead) or when a teammate is clearly\n    better placed (open lane, at least 60 closer to the net). Deke when a defender is square in front within 30 (40%\n    × Hnd/3). Otherwise carry toward the net, slaloming around defenders, with turbo in open ice.\n  - **Support forward**: get open on the far side at the dot height (about 150 from the goal line); once the carrier\n    crosses the blue line, drift to the far post or the slot for a one-timer.\n  - **Point**: stay at the blue line as an outlet; crash the net for rebounds when aggression is high.\n- **Without the puck** (defense):\n  - **Pressure**: the nearest skater intercepts the carrier's position 0.3 s ahead, then checks (when Hit ≥ 3 and\n    `RNG.sim() < aggression`) or pokes.\n  - **Cover**: marks the most dangerous rival without the puck (in the passing lane, or between them and the net).\n  - **Home**: guards the slot between the puck and its own net.\n- **Loose puck**: each team sends the skater who can reach the predicted puck position first. The rest take offense or\n  defense spots according to which team will probably win the race.\n- **Faceoffs**: centers face off at the dot; wingers line up on both sides; the point man behind.\n- **Difficulty** (Settings): Rookie, Pro, All-Star, Legend set AI skill .35 / .55 / .75 / .95, CPU goalie reaction\n  offsets +.06 / +.02 / 0 / −.02 s, and the human team's goalie −.03 / −.01 / 0 / +.01. Light rubber-banding (CPU\n  skill −.1 while it leads by 3 or more) on Rookie only.\n- **Teammates of humans** use the same AI and also obey call-for-pass. Team tactics from story choices: **Finesse**\n  (pass bias +30%, speed +4%) or **Grit** (check bias +30%, BOOM gain +15%).\n\n### 7.14 Match flow (`Match`)\n- **Configuration**: `{ home, away, arena, periods: 3, periodLen: 120, ot: 'sudden' (120 s, 3-on-3) | 'none',\n  shootout: true, intros: true, replays: 'auto', flood: 'ask' | 'always' | 'never', difficulty, cheats, objectives,\n  script, humans: [{ team, input }] }`.\n- **Phases**: `intro` → `faceoff` → `play` ⇄ `stoppage` → `goal` → `replay` → `faceoff` … `periodEnd` →\n  `intermission` (Flood Wagon) → `faceoff` … `final` → `results`. Also `fight`, `ot`, `shootout` and `celebration`.\n  The clock counts down only in `play`. The engine's pause freezes everything.\n- **Faceoff**: the referee holds the puck, raises an arm and drops it after a random 0.6–1.2 s. Each center presses\n  `pass` or `shoot` when it drops; the earlier press within 0–0.25 s after the drop wins (a press before the drop is a\n  slow, mistimed swipe); a CPU center reacts after its skill delay. The winner's swipe sends the puck back to a\n  teammate.\n- **Stoppages**: a frozen puck, the puck out of play, after a fight, at the end of a sin-bin call. Each brings a\n  whistle, a 1.5 s pause, a lower-third stat card (shots, hits, faceoffs %), an organ sting, and then the faceoff.\n- **Goals**: the horn (3 s), the red goal light spinning behind that net, the team's goal song sting, the crowd jumping,\n  the scorer's celebration (chosen by personality: fist pump, sniper aim, knee slide, stick guitar, a bounce off the\n  glass), and teammates converging. \"GOAL!\" in the title font, the scoring summary (scorer and assists, the\n  last two touches by the scorer's team), then an **instant replay** (7.16), then a center faceoff.\n- **Hat trick**: a player's third goal makes hats rain, and the commentary calls it. **Hoser Hat Trick**: one player\n  with a goal, an assist and a fight win in one game, shown as a toast.\n- **Periods**: the buzzer at 0:00, then the period summary card. **Intermission**: the Flood Wagon minigame (offered\n  per the `flood` option; skipping runs a 6 s AI resurfacing fast-forward), then the next period. Teams switch ends\n  every period.\n- **Overtime**: sudden death; a tie after it goes to the shootout (exhibition and story). In session mode: at most 60\n  s of sudden death, then a tie.\n- **Shootout**: 3 rounds each (home first), then sudden-death rounds. A shooter starts at center with the puck and an\n  8-second shot clock; the attempt ends on a shot, a save, a goal, or the puck going backward. Humans shoot for their\n  team (the skaters rotate) and play goalie against the CPU's shooters (6.1). The HUD shows big ✓ and ✗ marks.\n- **Final**: the final horn, the winning team celebrates, the losers slump (`kneel`), then **results**.\n- **Stats** per skater: goals, assists, shots, hits, big hits, takeaways, fights won, turbo used, top shot speed.\n  Per goalie: saves and shots against. Per team: everything summed, plus BOOM filled and Kabooms.\n- **Three stars**: rank players by `3 G + 2 A + 0.5 bigHits + 1.5 fightsWon + 0.3 shots` (goalies:\n  `0.12 saves + 2 × (save% − .85) × 10`) and announce the third, second and first stars, each with a portrait card and a\n  commentary line.\n- **Objectives**: declarative `{ id, text, on: 'goal' | 'hit' | …, where(e, match) }` counters plus a `need`, checked\n  live. A star toast when one is met.\n\n### 7.15 Camera director (`Cam`)\n- **Play**: focus on the puck (or carrier) plus a lead of 0.25 s of puck velocity. If a lone human's skater is more\n  than 220 from the puck, shift 25% toward them. With several local humans, `cam.frame([puck, ...humans],\n  { margin: 60, zoom: [.78, 1] })`. `cam.smooth` .15; bounds from `map.bounds(view)`.\n- **Zoom**: 1.0 (Settings → Camera distance: Near 1.15, Normal 1.0, Far 0.85); 1.15 at faceoffs; a 1.1 punch on big\n  hits (0.3 s); out to 0.85 briefly when the puck flies faster than 400.\n- **Fights**: `brawler`, zoom 1.6, framing the fighters. **Celebrations**: 1.3 on the scorer. **Intros**: a dolly\n  along the lineup. **Replays**: 7.16. Then back to the player's camera setting (Broadcast `threequarter` or Overhead\n  `topdown`, cycled by the `camera` action and saved).\n\n### 7.16 Instant replay (`Replay`)\n- **Recorder**: every second step, push `{ puck, skaters and goalies: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, rigState }, events }`\n  into an 8 s ring buffer. `rigState` is the object passed to `rig.update`, so the replay re-poses rigs exactly.\n- **Goal replay**: once the celebration has played for 1.5 s, cut (a puck-shaped wipe) to the last 4 s before the goal\n  at 0.5× in the `brawler` view following the puck at zoom 1.25, with letterbox bars, a \"REPLAY\" bug, and the\n  recorded events re-firing their effects. ✕ (or confirm) skips. Setting: Replays Auto or Off. Big-hit and Kaboom\n  replays (3 s) also play at the next stoppage when Replays is Auto: when such an event happens, copy its clip (2 s\n  before to 1 s after) out of the ring buffer, because the buffer will have moved on by the stoppage.\n- **Highlights**: keep the 3 best clips of a story run (goal type and hit power score them) in memory for the end\n  credits.\n\n### 7.17 Commentary (`Talk`)\n- **Booth**: CHUCK WALLOP (play-by-play) and MOOSE PLUNKETT (color), with live portraits (rigs in suits) in a bottom\n  subtitle box. Two lines at most; non-modal, auto-advancing (`talk.say(text, { modal: false, auto: 2.4, portrait,\n  name })`).\n- **Selection**: each event type has a pool (`TEXT.talk[type]`) with priority and cooldowns: a global 1.2 s, the\n  same line 120 s, the same type 6 s. Goals, fights, Kabooms and glass breaks interrupt; filler (Moose's anecdotes)\n  only plays after 8 s of quiet play. Variables: `{name} {team} {victim} {goalie} {score} {arena} {period}`.\n- **Voices**: every line babbles (10.1) in the speaker's voice. Settings: Commentary On/Off, Subtitles On/Off,\n  Voices volume.\n- **Tips** (Coach Marge) are separate: a banner just below the score bug with glyph chips, shown the first time its\n  trigger fires per save profile (Appendix D).\n\n### 7.18 HUD (`Hud`; it keeps clear of `game.cornerArea()` and inside a 92% title-safe area)\n- **Score bug** (top center, about 200 × 30): team logo chips, abbreviations, scores at font scale 2, the period\n  (`1ST 2ND 3RD OT SO`), the clock `m:ss`, and under each team its BOOM meter (80 × 4; flames and a countdown while in\n  KABOOM).\n- **Power play** strip under it: `POWER PLAY MUK 0:14`, with the sin-binned player's tag.\n- **Player markers**: a colored ring decal under each human's skater (P1–P4 in `E.PLAYER_COLORS`, the seat colors\n  online), a chevron with `P1` above, and an arrow on the screen edge when they are off screen. A turbo bar (16 × 2)\n  under the chevron. The shot meter above the shooter while charging (gold when full).\n- **Radar** (bottom right, about 108 × 48): the rink outline, skaters as team-colored dots, humans as larger dots with\n  rings, the puck white.\n- **Prompts** (bottom center, above the subtitles): context chips (`{shoot} ONE-TIMER!`, `HOLD {lob} DROP THE GLOVES`,\n  `{pass} SKIP`).\n- **Banners**: GOAL!, SAVE!, POST!, BIG HIT!, THROUGH THE GLASS!, KA-BOOM!, FIGHT!, POWER PLAY, HAT TRICK!, PERIOD\n  2, FINAL, in the title font with shake and color cycling (honoring reduce motion).\n- **Fight HUD**: two portraits with bars at the top corners, and the fight control chips at the bottom.\n- **Lower-thirds** at stoppages: one broadcast-style stat card for 3 s.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art direction","numLines":360,"startLine":360,"totalLines":1473}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0181ZcE3FU48n1CL2svqYUL5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh22FVHDBwKe3HgMgapQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UNoYZyHfpqVF3pyoTa34H2","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","offset":719,"limit":340},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14583,"cache_read_input_tokens":38884,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":14583},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"81a6403f-b2b6-4403-81ab-cdae25f747dd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:05.969Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh22FG8i2HFXZf9BzLdH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UNoYZyHfpqVF3pyoTa34H2":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","offset":719,"limit":340}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UNoYZyHfpqVF3pyoTa34H2","type":"tool_result","content":"719\t## 8. Art direction\n720\t\n721\t**Base**: the engine's native look (`res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`, HD Humanoids at size 1.2–1.3, lit scenes, shaded with\n722\t`E.tones`, props, particles), aimed at Symphony of the Night and Metal Slug quality, as AI_GUIDE asks. Act on every\n723\tlook note from `tools/check.mjs`.\n724\t\n725\t- **Skaters**: build `heroic` at size 1.2 (enforcers `bulky` at 1.3). Long-sleeved jersey (`outfit: 'shirt'`,\n726\t  `sleeves: 'long'`, `colors.cloth` the jersey, `trim` the stripe), breezers in `pants`, socks in the team color, skates,\n727\t  big gloves (`glove`), a hockey helmet, number and letter, `weapon: 'stick'`, and shoulder pads (`armor: true`, plate\n728\t  in the jersey color). Hair shows under the helmet (some flow, mullets on the Lumberjacks). Beards come from a darker\n729\t  skin tone on the jaw: add a `beard` color option if needed and log it.\n730\t- **Goalies**: `bulky` at 1.3 (The Vault 1.75), pads, blocker, catcher, mask, `gstick`, and pad and mask colors per\n731\t  team.\n732\t- **Referees**: `heroic` at 1.15, white shirt with black stripes, orange armbands (`trim`), a black helmet, a whistle\n733\t  (one dot).\n734\t- **Crowd**: as in the SPORTS kit: two small fans per stand tile (4 × 5 shirt, 3 × 3 head), colored 70% home and 30%\n735\t  away, swaying. Excitement drives them: claps, standing, jumping on goals, hands on heads after a big hit, a wave\n736\t  around the arena when quiet for 20 s. Fans hold signs (tiny-font text: `BARN BURNER`, `KABOOM!`, `MARGE 4 PM`,\n737\t  `SAVE THE ICEBOX`, `PIPESY ♥`). Behind each net, 4–6 bigger **glass pounders** (Humanoid at size 0.9 in the classic\n738\t  style) bang the glass when play comes near. On the near side, a row of dark head-and-shoulder silhouettes is drawn\n739\t  in screen space along the bottom edge when the camera is low (the broadcast foreground).\n740\t- **Team logos**: a 24 × 24 string sprite each (`E.sprite` rows plus a palette of 4–6 colors), used at center ice (×3),\n741\t  in the score bug (scaled down to 12 or 16), on menu cards (×3) and on bench banners. Section 11.1 describes them.\n742\t- **Effects**: ice spray on stops and turns (white `dust` and `bits`); a skate shower when someone is hit; glass shards;\n743\t  a puck streak; a slapshot shockwave ring; KABOOM fire, explosions and sparks; steam from melt; snow (weather) at the\n744\t  pond; confetti; hats; an octopus splat; a flying tooth on a big fight punch (a white bit, \"chiclets\"); dizzy stars\n745\t  circling a knocked-down head; sweat drops in fights; turbo speed lines.\n746\t- **Lighting**: canvas lights in every arena (11.2 lists them). Goal lights pulse red behind the net. KABOOM tints the\n747\t  arena. Spotlights sweep during intros and the title.\n748\t- **UI style**: dark blue-black panels (`E.ui.box` gradients) with ice-white text and a gold accent (`#ffd36a`),\n749\t  with team colors on cards. Theme the engine's HTML screens with `new E.Shell(game, { theme })` in the same colors and\n750\t  a large font: body text at least 24 CSS px at 1080p (check a screenshot).\n751\t\n752\t---\n753\t\n754\t## 9. Animation (the engine's procedural rigs plus new hockey motion)\n755\t\n756\tHockey motion is added by **wrapping `rig.solvePose`** on each skater and goalie rig (`Rigs`). It overrides feet,\n757\tknees, hips, torso lean, hands and stick joints (`E.ik3` for knees and elbows) from a small state the Skater passes\n758\tin (`skate: { phase, push, lean, stop, back, cross }`, `stick: { blade: [f, s, z], top, follow }`). Fights, cheers and\n759\tfalls use the engine's own `attack` moves, `pose`, `down` and `flip`. Every animation below must play in all three views.\n760\t\n761\t| Motion | How |\n762\t|---|---|\n763\t| Skating stride | Phase advances by `speed / 22`. Each foot pushes back and out diagonally (3 o'clock or 9 o'clock), then recovers under the hip. Knees bend 35°, hips drop 2.5, the torso leans .35 rad (.5 with turbo). The free arm swings when not stick-handling |\n764\t| Glide | Feet parallel, knees soft, a slight sway |\n765\t| Crossovers | Turning hard at speed: the outside foot crosses over in front, alternating |\n766\t| Hockey stop | The torso turns 70° off the velocity, both blades skid sideways with a deep knee bend, a spray at the feet |\n767\t| Backward C-cuts | The hips swing, the feet trace C shapes (AI defenders only) |\n768\t| Stick-handling | The blade weaves ±3 in front; the hands follow (the top hand at the hip, the bottom hand 40% down the shaft) |\n769\t| Pass / saucer | The blade sweeps back to front toward the target; a saucer flicks up at the end |\n770\t| Wrist shot | Weight shift, a fast sweep, a high follow-through |\n771\t| Slapshot | Wind-up (the stick rises behind the shoulder and holds while charging), downswing to the ice, follow-through pointing at the target |\n772\t| One-timer | A short wind-up already held, then the strike on contact |\n773\t| Deke | Spin-o-rama (a 360° body spin with `flip`-like twist), toe drag (the blade pulls the puck back across) |\n774\t| Check | The shoulder leads (lean into it), the stick across the chest |\n775\t| Hit reaction / fall | A stagger (bump); `down` + `flip` tumble + a belly slide (big hit); squashed against the glass (`rig.kick(-.4)`) when hit into it; `getup` from a kneel |\n776\t| Poke | The stick shoots forward along the ice in a lunge |\n777\t| Slip | Feet fly up, landing on the back, a spin-slide (octopus, rat) |\n778\t| Goalie | A ready crouch (pads together, glove up), shuffle and T-push, butterfly (knees down, pads flared), glove and blocker saves, pad stack, poke, covering the puck, celebrating, blasted (flailing backward into the net) |\n779\t| Faceoff | Centers crouch with sticks down; the referee raises an arm and drops the puck; the swipe |\n780\t| Celebrations | Fist pump, sniper aim (the stick held like a rifle), knee slide, stick guitar, bouncing off the glass, a team huddle |\n781\t| Fights | Gloves off (sprites fall), circling in `stance: 'guard'`, one hand gripping the rival's jersey (the hand held at the rival's shoulder), `jab`, `haymaker` and `hook` from `E.MOVES`, a duck, jersey over the head (`hood`), the knockdown, the winner's `cheer` |\n782\t| Bench and coach | Spares sit (a sit pose via solvePose: hips at bench height, knees forward); Coach Marge gestures (`wave`, `hips`) |\n783\t| Story set pieces | The handshake line (two lines sliding past, hands out), the Cup lift (`cheer` with the Cup sprite held at the hands), the Flood Wagon driver seated and steering, Polar Pete's dance (a bulky white rig, a big round head from an extra ball drawn over it, ears), the organist playing (hands bobbing on the beat via `audio.onBeat`) |\n784\t\n785\t**Animation lab** (`#lab`, also in the Dev panel): one skater, one goalie and one referee on a small rink, a list of\n786\tevery motion above, a slider for speed and phase, and a `brawler` / `threequarter` / `topdown` toggle. Film each\n787\tmotion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (`--seed 1`) and check: the wind-up, the strike, the settle, no snaps or backward\n788\tsweeps.\n789\t\n790\t---\n791\t\n792\t## 10. Audio (all synthesized in code; no audio files)\n793\t\n794\t### 10.1 Voices: babble (Animalese/Simlish style)\n795\t- `Synth.babble(text, voice, { onLetter })` turns a line into syllables. Each letter that sounds (vowels, and\n796\t  consonants as onsets) is a 55–85 ms blip: a `pulse` or `saw` source through two bandpass filters at the vowel's\n797\t  formants (a: 800/1200 Hz, e: 500/1900, i: 300/2300, o: 500/900, u: 350/700; consonants borrow the next vowel and add\n798\t  a 10 ms noise click for `s t k p` sounds). Pitch is the voice's base × (a letter-hash offset of ±3 semitones). `!`\n799\t  raises the last 4 syllables by 4 semitones; `?` glides the last syllable up; `,` and `.` add 120 / 220 ms pauses.\n800\t  It runs on the engine's new `voice` bus.\n801\t- A voice is `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, speed: syllables/s, wave, formantShift, gruff (noise mix) }`. Marge: low,\n802\t  gruff, slow. Dunny: mid and bright. Snipes: high and fast. Lou: very low, soft and slow. Lemmy: mid and wobbly\n803\t  (vibrato). Glitterman: nasal (formants × 1.15), fast. Chuck: mid-high, very fast. Moose: low and gruff. The referee\n804\t  barks single syllables. The crowd's chant mixes 6 voices.\n805\t- It hooks into `E.Dialog` through the voice hook (section 4) for cutscenes and the booth, and into chirp bubbles,\n806\t  intros (\"Number NINE… DUNNY… MACPHAIL!\"), the referee's calls and crowd chants. Its randomness comes from `RNG.fx`\n807\t  so it never changes the simulation.\n808\t\n809\t### 10.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` voices; custom graphs where noted)\n810\tSkate stride swish (filtered noise, pitch by speed, one per push); hockey stop \"shhhk\" (noise, a bandpass sweep down);\n811\tpuck on stick \"tock\"; pass \"thwap\"; wrist shot \"snap\"; slapshot crack plus whoosh; one-timer (a louder crack); **post\n812\t\"PING\"** (triangle 1850 Hz, 0.9 s decay, a slight detune: the most recognizable sound in hockey); crossbar ping (2100\n813\tHz); puck on boards (a low thud and a rattle); puck on glass (a sharp clack and a ring); net swish; body check thump\n814\tplus a babble \"oof\"; big hit (a deeper thump, a glass rattle, crowd \"OHHH\"); glass crack (a sharp tick) and glass\n815\tshatter (a noise burst and a descending sine tinkle cluster of 12 voices); the referee's whistle (a two-tone pea\n816\twhistle with vibrato); **the goal horn** (a custom graph: 3 detuned `brass` oscillators at 98, 147 and 196 Hz through\n817\tthe lowpass `lp: 900`, 0.25 s attack, 2.6 s hold, then release, plus noise \"air\"); the period buzzer (square at 220 Hz,\n818\t1.5 s); punches (a thud and a whoosh); dizzy stars twinkle; power-up pickup (an arpeggio); item throw (a whoosh);\n819\toctopus \"splort\"; KABOOM explosion (engine `explode` + a sub-bass drop); the Flood Wagon engine (a looped low saw\n820\tputter, pitch by speed), its horn \"A-OOGA\"; menu move, select and back (soft organ blips).\n821\t\n822\t### 10.3 Crowd and organ\n823\t- **Crowd bed**: two looped noise sources (bandpass 400 Hz and 1.2 kHz, an LFO swell) whose gain follows\n824\t  `Crowd.excitement` (0..1: raised by shots, near misses, hits, goals; decays). Plus reactions: \"OHHH\" (a swell\n825\t  sweeping down), \"AHHH\" (a near miss), cheer (a burst with high-voiced babble), boo (low, filtered babble), the\n826\t  \"KA-BOOM!\" chant (6-voice babble on the beat, with claps), and claps in rhythm.\n827\t- **The organ** (`organ` wave, a Leslie-like vibrato of 6 Hz at .004): original stings only. A rising charge fanfare\n828\t  (G4 C5 E5 G5 – E5 G5), a chromatic walk-up vamp for faceoffs, a clap-along vamp (\"da-da-da da-da\"), a sad trombone\n829\t  slide for an opponent's penalty, a fight vamp (minor and tense), and a goal sting per team. In the Ol' Icebox, Doris\n830\t  the organist plays them visibly. **Never copy existing chants or songs** (no \"Charge!\" bugle call, no stadium rock\n831\t  standards).\n832\t\n833\t### 10.4 Music (engine song format; the new `organ` and `brass` waves; named layers)\n834\t| Song | Use | Character |\n835\t|---|---|---|\n836\t| `theme` | title, attract | arena chip-rock anthem: saw power chords, a driving square lead, drums; the \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\" hook |\n837\t| `menu` | menus, setup | a relaxed loop from the theme's chords |\n838\t| `locker` | cutscenes (locker room) | gritty bass and a snare shuffle, organ pads |\n839\t| `pond` | pond cutscenes, the pond arena's stoppages | a folksy pulse-wave fiddle tune in 6/8 |\n840\t| `grind` | Grindhouse | a punk loop |\n841\t| `mall` | MegaMall | cheesy synth-pop |\n842\t| `final` | Dome cutscenes, the final | epic, brass |\n843\t| `play` | under play (quiet) | a low pulse plus layers `drive` (in the third period and OT), `kaboom` (KABOOM mode), `fight` (fights) |\n844\t| `flood` | the Flood Wagon minigame | an original skaters' waltz (3/4, organ) |\n845\t| `victory`, `defeat` | results | a fanfare, a sad trombone |\n846\t| `credits` | the end credits | the theme as a ballad, then full band |\n847\t| goal stings ×6 | one per team | 2 bars over the horn |\n848\t\n849\t**Mix**: buses `music` (setting), `sfx` (setting), `voice` (setting: Voices) and the crowd (on sfx, plus its own\n850\tsetting: Crowd). Duck the music under the commentary voice (−4 dB) and in the pause menu (the engine does this).\n851\t\n852\t---\n853\t\n854\t## 11. Content\n855\t\n856\t### 11.1 Teams (3 skaters + 1 goalie each; ratings 1–5: Spd / Sht / Pas / Hit / Fgt / Hnd; goalies Rfx / Size / Reb)\n857\t| Team | Abbr | Home dark / away white trim | Logo (24×24) | Players |\n858\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n859\t| **Mukluk Falls Muskrats** | MUK | brown `#5a3a22`, gold `#e8b43a`, cream `#f3e6c8` | a buck-toothed muskrat face in a gold ring | #9 Duncan \"Dunny\" MacPhail, C, playmaker 4/3/5/3/2/4, shoots L · #19 Priya \"Snipes\" Sandhu, sniper 5/5/3/2/2/5, R · #44 Lou \"Big Lou\" Beaudoin, enforcer D (bulky) 2/4/2/5/5/2, R · G #31 Lemmy \"The Sieve\" Kowalchuk 3/4/3 (trait: **Talks to Posts**: 20% of goals within 4 of a post ring off it instead) |\n860\t| **Dryfork Drillers** | DRY | black `#1d1d22`, orange `#f07a1a` | an oil derrick with a drop | #7 \"Rig\" McCoy, C 3/3/4/3/3/3 · #15 \"Gusher\" Gomez 4/4/3/2/2/4 · #2 \"Drill Bit\" Dobbs, D 3/2/2/4/3/2 · G #35 Derrick Okafor 2/3/2 |\n861\t| **Logjam Lumberjacks** | LOG | red plaid `#b3262a` + black, cream | a bearded log face | #10 Axel Sundqvist, C 3/4/3/3/3/3 · #27 \"Sawdust\" Sally Lindgren 4/4/3/3/2/4 · #88 \"Big Timber\" Thibodeau, enforcer (bulky) 2/3/2/5/4/2 · G #1 \"Stumpy\" O'Rourke 3/4/3 |\n862\t| **Grindhouse Bruise Brothers** | GRD | purple `#4b2a6b`, lime `#9be04a` | a fist inside a gear | #66 Rocco Bruiser (bulky) 3/3/2/5/5/2 · #67 Rollo Bruiser (bulky) 3/3/2/5/5/2 · #12 \"Mumbles\" Malone 4/4/3/2/3/4 · G #29 \"Tank\" Tankersley 3/5/2 |\n863\t| **Megaplex Marauders** | MEG | teal `#18b5b0`, magenta `#e0389a` | a shopping cart flying a pirate flag | #23 Chad Glitterman, C 4/3/4/2/1/4 · #8 \"Zoom\" Zhang 5/3/3/2/2/4 · #5 \"Promo\" Perkins, D 3/3/3/4/3/3 · G #40 \"Kiosk\" Kingsley 4/3/4 |\n864\t| **Gilded Grizzlies** | GLD | gold `#d9a520`, black `#141414`, white | a grizzly head in a crown | #1 Sterling Glitterman Jr. 5/5/4/3/2/5 (**Golden Twister**) · #91 \"Silk\" Sullivan 4/3/5/2/2/5 · #55 \"Brick\" Brickowski (bulky) 3/4/2/5/5/2 · G #00 **The Vault** 5/5/5 (boss: size 1.75) |\n865\t\n866\t- **Rating multipliers**: speed `0.85 + 0.05 Spd`; shot speed `0.85 + 0.05 Sht`, shot error `1.3 − 0.1 Sht`; pass\n867\t  speed `0.9 + 0.033 Pas`; check `0.8 + 0.067 Hit`; fight damage `0.8 + 0.067 Fgt`; pickup radius `0.85 + 0.05 Hnd`.\n868\t  Goalie reaction `−0.015 (Rfx − 3)`, save shapes × `0.9 + 0.033 Size`, freeze chance `+0.06 (Reb − 3)`.\n869\t- **Golden Twister** (Sterling): in the offensive zone, 1 in 3 carries end in a 0.6 s spin with a golden glow\n870\t  (telegraphed), then a curving shot (spin 1.2, like the SPORTS kit's curl) that cuts the CPU goalie's save chance by\n871\t  25%. Checking him during the spin is a guaranteed big hit and BOOM +10.\n872\t- **The Vault**: size 1.75; the first two KABOOM shots only stagger him (\"VAULT LOCKED\"). After the second, \"THE\n873\t  VAULT IS CRACKED!\": size 1.4 and Rfx −1 for the rest of the game. Weak to cross-crease one-timers (lateral speed ×\n874\t  0.8) and dekes (he bites 1.5×).\n875\t- **Coach and staff portraits**: Coach Marge Pelletier (grey bun, cardigan, whistle), Old Gus (90, cap, the Flood\n876\t  Wagon driver), Doris (organist, beehive hair), Goldie Glitterman (gold fur coat, sunglasses), Polar Pete (mascot),\n877\t  and Chuck and Moose (suits; Moose is missing teeth).\n878\t\n879\t### 11.2 Arenas\n880\t| Arena | Chapter | Look | Lights | Items | Hazard | Music |\n881\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n882\t| **The Ol' Icebox** (Mukluk Falls) | 1, title, practice | wooden barrel-vault beams, string lights, 1962 championship banners, wooden stands, fans in toques, Doris's organ booth, a hand-painted scoreboard, ads (`MUKLUK MUFFLER & TIRE`, `KOWALCHUK'S PEROGIES`, `BAIT 'N' BAGELS`) | ambient .65 warm, 6 hanging lamps over the ice (light radius 260) | Hot Sauce, Tape, Poutine, BOOM Box | – | organ, `play` |\n883\t| **Lake Kabonk** (pond) | 2 | a frozen lake at dusk, snowbank boards, pines, two cabins with lit windows, a bonfire with fans in parkas, string lights on poles, snowmen (store) | ambient .45 blue dusk, bonfire flicker, cabin windows, string lights; weather snow .5 | Hot Cocoa, Tape, Lumber, BOOM Box | thin ice ×3, snowbanks | `pond` |\n884\t| **The Grindhouse** | 3 | a steel-truss mill arena, chain-link above the end boards, steam pipes, rowdy stands, a cage-match vibe, ads (`RUSTBELT SCRAP`, `IRON GUT CHILI`) | ambient .5 cool green, flickering fluorescents (`RNG.fx`), steam vents | Poutine, Lumber, BOOM Box | octopus throws after goals, rubber rats | `grind` |\n885\t| **MegaMall Ice Palace** | 4 | a rink in a mall atrium: storefront neon, escalators, a fountain, a food court, ads on every inch (`GLITTERMAN MEGAPLEX — COMING SOON!`) | ambient .7, neon emissives in magenta and teal, fountain glow | Discount Drop crates (any item) | Polar Pete, Discount Drop | `mall` |\n886\t| **The Kaboom Dome** | 5 | a huge arena: gold-trimmed boards, flame cannons in the corners, laser lights, fireworks, a sold-out crowd, a jumbotron frame on replays | ambient .55, strong white ceiling lights, moving spotlights in intros, flame light on goals and Kabooms | Hot Sauce, Brick Pads, BOOM Box | octopus (rare), Gilded Mode | `final` |\n887\t\n888\tEvery arena uses the same rink geometry. Walls, stands and props come from the TileMap (`types` for tiers with `face`\n889\tmaterials), `r.shape` / `E.SHAPES` (new entries: `locker`, `bench-box`, `organ`, `net`, `glass-crew-cart`,\n890\t`flood-wagon`, `flame-cannon`, `cabin`, `fountain`, `escalator`, `storefront`, `scoreboard`, `kaboom-cup`) and\n891\t`r.prop` (lamps, banners, signs, torches as bonfire, trees).\n892\t\n893\t### 11.3 Story: THE CUP RUN\n894\t\n895\t**Premise**: Mukluk Falls (pop. 812) has one thing: the Ol' Icebox, a 1950s barn where the town learned to skate.\n896\tDeveloper Goldie Glitterman bought the land and plans a \"Megaplex Parking Experience\". Coach Marge digs up **Town\n897\tBylaw 1897-B**: *any rink that houses the Kaboom Cup shall stand forever.* So the Muskrats, a ragtag team of three\n898\tskaters, a superstitious goalie and a 72-year-old coach, have to win the regional Kaboom Cup: five games, five\n899\tbarns, five rivals. **Tone**: a small-town sports-movie comedy told like a hockey broadcast, with hockey clichés\n900\tplayed with a straight face, chirps that rhyme, and big heart. PG: no blood, no slurs, no swearing (a beep and\n901\tbabble stand in for \"a curse word\").\n902\t\n903\t**Chapter flow**: storymap (a snowy highway map; the team bus drives between 5 town stops, each showing its stars and\n904\tlock) → pre-game cutscene (with one choice) → [chapter 1: optional warm-up drills 1–3] → player intros → the game (its\n905\tobjectives listed on the pause screen and a pre-game card) → intermission Flood Wagon (offered) → post-game cutscene →\n906\tresults and three stars → stars and unlocks → back to the map. **A loss**: a short Marge pep talk (a different one for\n907\teach chapter, in TEXT) and Retry or Back to Map. Progress autosaves (`game.saves`) after each chapter and choice.\n908\t\n909\t**Choices** (one per chapter; they set the game's team tactic, 7.13): chapter 1 \"Clean and fast\" (Finesse) / \"Mean and\n910\tloud\" (Grit); chapter 2 the same two; chapter 3 \"Let Lou loose\" (Lou Fgt +1, fights likelier) / \"Keep it on the ice\" (Lou\n911\tPas +1); chapter 4 \"Ignore the bear\" / \"Hunt the bear\" (the AI targets Polar Pete); chapter 5 \"Doris plays early\"\n912\t(the organ boost at the start of the 2nd period) / \"Doris plays late\" (at 5:00 left in the 3rd, +50% stronger).\n913\t\n914\t| # | Chapter | Arena / rival / rules | New mechanic spotlighted | Objectives (★ each) |\n915\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n916\t| 1 | **Home Opener** | Ol' Icebox vs Dryfork Drillers, 3 × 1:30; the rivals play one difficulty step below the setting (never below Rookie) | skating, passing, shooting, one-timers, checking, BOOM meter, Flood Wagon | Win · Score a one-timer · Land 3 big hits |\n917\t| 2 | **Pond Rules** | Lake Kabonk vs Logjam Lumberjacks, 3 × 1:30 | KABOOM mode (Marge explains it), power-ups, thin ice, snowbanks | Win · Break the ice under a Lumberjack · Trigger KABOOM |\n918\t| 3 | **Gloves Off** | Grindhouse vs Bruise Brothers, 3 × 1:30, they challenge often | fights, the sin bin, power plays, hazards (octopi, rats), chirps | Win · Win 2 fights · Score a power-play goal |\n919\t| 4 | **Mall Brawl** | MegaMall vs Megaplex Marauders, 3 × 1:30 with no OT, then a **Shootout Showcase** every time (it decides a tie; otherwise it is a bonus round for mall money and a toast) | the mascot, Discount Drop, the shootout and manual goalie | Win · Score a KABOOM goal · Knock down Polar Pete |\n920\t| 5 | **The Kaboom Cup** | Kaboom Dome vs Gilded Grizzlies, 3 × 2:00, OT and shootout if tied | the boss: Sterling's Golden Twister, The Vault, Gilded Mode, Glitterman's Gilded Boost (Grizzlies +10% speed from the 3rd period), Doris's organ counter (Muskrats BOOM +30 and +10% speed for 20 s) | Win · Beat The Vault with a deke goal · One player scores a hat trick |\n921\t\n922\t**Script beats** (TEXT holds the full lines; these set the voice. Speakers in caps, choices in brackets):\n923\t\n924\t*Chapter 1 pre-game (locker room)*\n925\t- MARGE: \"Sit down, shut up, and listen. I got a letter.\"\n926\t- MARGE: \"Goldie Glitterman bought the land under the Icebox. Wants to pave it for a {c=#ffd36a}Megaplex Parking\n927\t  Experience{/c}.\"\n928\t- DUNNY: \"A parking… experience? Beauty. Wait. No. Not beauty.\"\n929\t- SNIPES: \"This barn's got more character than his whole bank account. And his haircut.\"\n930\t- MARGE: \"Bylaw 1897-B. Any rink that houses the Kaboom Cup stands forever. So we win the Cup.\"\n931\t- LOU (knitting): \"Five games, then. Like the five petals of the wild rose.\"\n932\t- LEMMY: \"Pipesy says we win. Clang's not so sure. Clang's a pessimist.\"\n933\t- GLITTERMAN (in the doorway): \"Enjoy the barn, folks. I've ordered the parking meters. Gold ones.\"\n934\t- MARGE: \"Captain. Tell 'em how we play tonight.\" [CLEAN AND FAST / MEAN AND LOUD]\n935\t- DUNNY: \"We get pucks deep, we get bodies to the net, and we— uh— {$tacticLine}\"\n936\t- MARGE: \"Warm-up's on. Then we drill the Drillers.\"\n937\t\n938\t*Chapter 1 post-game*: CHUCK: \"The Muskrats take the opener! The Icebox is ROCKIN'!\" · GLITTERMAN: \"Beginner's luck.\n939\tThe meters are still on order.\" · MARGE: \"Pack your long johns. Lake Kabonk. Pond rules.\"\n940\t\n941\t*Chapter 2 pre-game (the lake at dusk, by the bonfire)*: BIG TIMBER: \"Welcome to the woods, Muskrats. We don't check.\n942\tWe FELL.\" · SNIPES: \"Cute beard. Did you grow it, or did a beaver move in?\" · LEMMY: \"The ice is talking. It says\n943\t'crack'.\" · MARGE: \"Thin ice is a tool. Hit 'em where it's thin.\" · MARGE: \"And listen. When the whole team's hummin'\n944\t— hits, passes, the crowd losin' its mind — the ice starts to shake. That's a KABOOM. Fill the meter and let it\n945\trip.\" · LOU: \"Like thunder in a teacup.\" · [tactic choice]\n946\t*Post*: BIG TIMBER: \"You hit like a falling spruce. Good on ya.\" · DUNNY: \"Thanks! You smell like one!\" · MARGE: \"Next\n947\tstop, the Grindhouse. Bring a mouthguard. Bring two.\"\n948\t\n949\t*Chapter 3 pre-game (the Grindhouse's dim locker room)*: ROCCO: \"Well, well. Lou Beaudoin.\" · ROLLO: \"Lou 'The\n950\tLibrary' Beaudoin.\" · ROCCO: \"Heard you knit now.\" · ROLLO: \"Heard you purl.\" · LOU: \"I have retired from fisticuffs,\n951\tgentlemen.\" · MARGE: \"Retire after the game.\" · MARGE: \"In this barn they drop the gloves, you drop 'em back. Win the\n952\tscrap, win the barn. Lose it, you sit in the sin bin and think about your choices.\" · [LET LOU LOOSE / KEEP IT ON THE\n953\tICE]\n954\t*Post*: ROLLO: \"He knitted me a scarf.\" · ROCCO: \"For my neck.\" · ROLLO: \"Which he bruised.\" · LOU: \"There is an ice pack\n955\tin the pocket.\" · MARGE: \"Next, the Megaplex. Glitterman's turf. Watch your wallets.\"\n956\t\n957\t*Chapter 4 pre-game (rink-side under the neon)*: CHAD (filming himself): \"What's up, Mall Rats! Smash that glass,\n958\tbro!\" · DUNNY: \"We're Muskrats.\" · CHAD: \"Same content, bro.\" · GLITTERMAN (to Lemmy): \"Name your price, goalie.\" ·\n959\tLEMMY: \"…Pipesy says no. Clang says no with a curse word.\" · POLAR PETE: (a dance and a muffled babble) · MARGE:\n960\t\"That bear's on the ice all game. Treat him like furniture.\" [IGNORE THE BEAR / HUNT THE BEAR] · MARGE: \"And win or\n961\ttie, the mall's got a Shootout Showcase after. Mall money. We want it.\"\n962\t*Post*: GLITTERMAN: \"Fine. The Final. My Grizzlies. My Dome. My rules.\" · SNIPES: \"Your Dome's gonna need a new roof.\"\n963\t\n964\t*Chapter 5 pre-game (the Dome's tunnel, then the spotlight intro)*: STERLING: \"I've never lost. Not once. Not even\n965\tat Go Fish.\" · SNIPES: \"There's a first time for everything, Goldilocks.\" · THE VAULT: \"…\" · LEMMY: \"He's very big,\n966\tPipesy.\" · MARGE: \"Forty-six years behind that bench. I've seen better teams. Prettier teams. Teams that could spell.\"\n967\t· MARGE: \"Never saw one that wanted it more. Go make it go KABOOM.\" · [DORIS EARLY / DORIS LATE]\n968\t*In-game*: when the Grizzlies' Gilded Boost starts, GLITTERMAN on the jumbotron: \"Synergy, boys!\" When Doris\n969\tplays, MARGE: \"DORIS! PLAY THE SONG!\" (the organ's charge fanfare, the crowd claps, the boost).\n970\t*Post (win), the ending*: the handshake line (both teams) → Dunny lifts the Kaboom Cup, which goes off in a confetti\n971\texplosion. CHUCK: \"THE KABOOM CUP IS… KA-BOOMING!\" → GLITTERMAN: \"My parking meters…\" → MARGE: \"Bylaw 1897-B, Goldie.\n972\tLook it up.\" → GUS: \"Yep.\" → the Flood Wagon drives a lap with the team on top → **credits** over the run's highlight\n973\treplays (7.16), then Coach Marge: \"Same time next year.\" → the title, with the **Cup on display** in the Icebox from\n974\tthen on.\n975\t\n976\t**Unlocks** (15 stars in all; exhibition cheats): 3★ Big Heads (`headR` × 1.8) · 6★ Octopus Rain · 9★ Glow Puck · 12★\n977\tAlways KABOOM (for humans) · 15★ Retro Rigs (`style: 'classic'`). Finishing the story makes the Gilded Grizzlies and\n978\tThe Vault playable in exhibition and adds the Cup to the title screen.\n979\t\n980\t### 11.4 Practice: Coach Marge's Drills (at the Ol' Icebox, house lights half on)\n981\t| # | Drill | Pass condition | Teaches |\n982\t|---|---|---|---|\n983\t| 1 | Wheels | skate through 6 gates in order in 25 s (one gate wants a hockey stop) | skating, turbo, stops |\n984\t| 2 | Tape to Tape | 5 completed passes to moving teammates + 1 saucer over a sled | passes, saucers, aim |\n985\t| 3 | Top Shelf | hit 4 corner targets on an empty net (wrist and slap) | shots, aim, lift |\n986\t| 4 | One-Timers | 3 one-timer goals on Lemmy from Dunny's cross-crease feeds | one-timers |\n987\t| 5 | Finish Your Check | big-hit 3 training dummies into the glass and break a panel | checks, turbo hits, glass |\n988\t| 6 | Gloves Off | win a spar with Big Lou (he goes easy) | the fight controls |\n989\t| 7 | KABOOM! | with a full meter, score with a KABOOM shot and survive Lou's KABOOM check | KABOOM mode |\n990\t\n991\tEach drill opens with a Marge line (voiced) and a prompt panel with glyph chips, tracks its counter in the HUD, and\n992\tsaves its completion. Completing all 7 earns the \"Marge Approved\" badge (Records). Chapter 1 offers drills 1–3 as\n993\tits warm-up.\n994\t\n995\t### 11.5 Text pools (in `07-data-text.js`; sizes are the minimums)\n996\tCommentary: 18 event types × 4–8 lines (≈ 110 lines) plus 20 Moose filler anecdotes; chirps: 30; tips: 14;\n997\tthree-stars lines: 12; loss pep talks: 5; menu blurbs: 1 per item; About pages (12.1). Appendix D has samples for each.\n998\t\n999\t---\n1000\t\n1001\t## 12. Screens and flows (10-foot UI)\n1002\t\n1003\t**Rules for every screen**: at most 6 choices visible; big tiles and cards; one line of help; a legend at the bottom\n1004\twith glyph chips (`{pass} SELECT  {deke} BACK`, as keycaps or mouse icons for keyboard and mouse). D-pad, stick,\n1005\tarrows and WASD move focus; ✕ / Enter / Space pick; ○ / Esc / Backspace go back. **The mouse hovering a tile focuses\n1006\tit and a click picks it.** Focus has an animated gold border, a slight scale-up and an organ blip. No dense tables\n1007\tanywhere: stats are a few big numbers.\n1008\t\n1009\t1. **Title**: the Ol' Icebox at night, spotlights sweeping the ice, two teams skating lazily (AI). The logo slams in\n1010\t   with an explosion and the horn, then `PRESS ANY BUTTON` (`TAP` is never shown; see 15.2). Then the main menu: 6 tiles\n1011\t   in 2 rows: **CUP RUN** (Continue/New when a save exists), **EXHIBITION**, **PRACTICE**, **RECORDS**, **SETTINGS**\n1012\t   (the engine's settings screen: `game.menu('settings')`), **ABOUT**. The version label (`E.versionLabel()` + the\n1013\t   game's version) sits small in a corner, and the engine corner buttons stay at the top right.\n1014\t2. **Exhibition → Sides**: every joined player is a token in the middle column (CPU); push left or right to join HOME\n1015\t   or AWAY; ✕ to ready. \"Press START on a free controller, or 2 on the keyboard, to join\" (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4\n1016\t   })`). The keyboard halves show their keys. Mouse: click HOME or AWAY to move the keyboard player's token.\n1017\t3. **Exhibition → Setup**: 3 big cards side by side: HOME team, ARENA, AWAY team (left/right on a focused card cycles\n1018\t   it; each team card shows its logo ×3, name, and 4 pip bars: Speed, Shooting, Hitting, Goalie). Below, one row of\n1019\t   option chips: Periods (1/2/3), Period length (1:00 / 1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 4:00), Difficulty, Cheats (unlocked\n1020\t   ones). **FACE OFF!** starts.\n1021\t4. **Story map**: the bus on a snowy highway with 5 stops (each a town sign with its logo and earned stars). The stop\n1022\t   in focus shows the chapter title and objectives. Click a stop to pick it.\n1023\t5. **Cutscene**: the set (the locker room or rink-side), characters staged, `E.Dialog` boxes with live portraits,\n1024\t   babble and typed text; choices are 2 big options. ✕ advances; holding ○ for 1 s skips the scene (with a fill ring).\n1025\t6. **Pre-game card**: matchup logos, the arena, the objectives with ★ slots, the tactic chosen. ✕ FACE OFF.\n1026\t7. **Match** (HUD 7.18). **Pause** (engine): Resume, Objectives & Info (the story objectives, or the exhibition's\n1027\t   setup), Restart Game, **Dev Mode**, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title.\n1028\t8. **Intermission**: the period summary card (goals, shots, hits: big numbers), then `{pass} DRIVE THE FLOOD WAGON`\n1029\t   or `{deke} SKIP`.\n1030\t9. **Results**: the final score huge, the **three stars** revealed one by one (portrait cards, a stat line, a\n1031\t   commentary line), the objectives ticking ★, then CONTINUE / REMATCH / MAIN MENU.\n1032\t10. **Records**: big numbers with a label each: Hardest Shot (km/h = u/s ÷ 16 × 3.6), Biggest Hit, Most Goals in a\n1033\t    Game, Fights Won, KABOOMs, Story Stars x/15, Drills x/7. Two pages at most.\n1034\t11. **About**: section 12.1's pages, paged with L1/R1, left/right or a click on the arrows.\n1035\t12. **Credits**: the end roll over highlight replays.\n1036\t\n1037\t### 12.1 About / Credits screen\n1038\tPages (at most 8 lines each, in the large font): **Credits** (game design and code: Claude Opus 5.5, `claude-opus-5-5`,\n1039\tfor Michael Crosato's cc-matrix; engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2, MIT; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; every sound, voice and\n1040\tsong synthesized in code; asset-store props from CC0 sets, listed by name) · **Source Information** (every field TASK.md\n1041\tlists) · **Testing Feedback** · **Engine Feedback** · **Prompt Feedback** · **Engine changes** (the summary of\n1042\tENGINE-CHANGES.md). The builder fills the feedback pages at the end with the same text as the chat reply and\n1043\t`exit-interview.json`, writing \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed.\n1044\t\n1045\t---\n1046\t\n1047\t## 13. Settings (via `menu.settings`; the engine's Display, Sound, Comfort and Controls stay)\n1048\tButton symbols (PlayStation / Xbox) · Difficulty (Rookie / Pro / All-Star / Legend) · Period length (exhibition default)\n1049\t· Camera (Broadcast / Overhead) · Camera distance (Near / Normal / Far) · Commentary (On / Off) · Subtitles (On / Off) ·\n1050\tVoices volume · Crowd volume · Player intros (On / Off) · Replays (Auto / Off) · Flood Wagon (Ask / Always / Never) ·\n1051\tPuck trail (Off / Streak / Glow) · Tips (On / Off) · Reset tips. Every one is read live.\n1052\t\n1053\t---\n1054\t\n1055\t## 14. Online: AI Hub sessions (`Net`, shared-world)\n1056\t\n1057\t### 14.1 Page tags (in `<head>`, after the session client)\n1058\t```html"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"970eae63-56db-4500-8fa3-32d5f6b53c80","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:06.113Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 8. Art direction\n\n**Base**: the engine's native look (`res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`, HD Humanoids at size 1.2–1.3, lit scenes, shaded with\n`E.tones`, props, particles), aimed at Symphony of the Night and Metal Slug quality, as AI_GUIDE asks. Act on every\nlook note from `tools/check.mjs`.\n\n- **Skaters**: build `heroic` at size 1.2 (enforcers `bulky` at 1.3). Long-sleeved jersey (`outfit: 'shirt'`,\n  `sleeves: 'long'`, `colors.cloth` the jersey, `trim` the stripe), breezers in `pants`, socks in the team color, skates,\n  big gloves (`glove`), a hockey helmet, number and letter, `weapon: 'stick'`, and shoulder pads (`armor: true`, plate\n  in the jersey color). Hair shows under the helmet (some flow, mullets on the Lumberjacks). Beards come from a darker\n  skin tone on the jaw: add a `beard` color option if needed and log it.\n- **Goalies**: `bulky` at 1.3 (The Vault 1.75), pads, blocker, catcher, mask, `gstick`, and pad and mask colors per\n  team.\n- **Referees**: `heroic` at 1.15, white shirt with black stripes, orange armbands (`trim`), a black helmet, a whistle\n  (one dot).\n- **Crowd**: as in the SPORTS kit: two small fans per stand tile (4 × 5 shirt, 3 × 3 head), colored 70% home and 30%\n  away, swaying. Excitement drives them: claps, standing, jumping on goals, hands on heads after a big hit, a wave\n  around the arena when quiet for 20 s. Fans hold signs (tiny-font text: `BARN BURNER`, `KABOOM!`, `MARGE 4 PM`,\n  `SAVE THE ICEBOX`, `PIPESY ♥`). Behind each net, 4–6 bigger **glass pounders** (Humanoid at size 0.9 in the classic\n  style) bang the glass when play comes near. On the near side, a row of dark head-and-shoulder silhouettes is drawn\n  in screen space along the bottom edge when the camera is low (the broadcast foreground).\n- **Team logos**: a 24 × 24 string sprite each (`E.sprite` rows plus a palette of 4–6 colors), used at center ice (×3),\n  in the score bug (scaled down to 12 or 16), on menu cards (×3) and on bench banners. Section 11.1 describes them.\n- **Effects**: ice spray on stops and turns (white `dust` and `bits`); a skate shower when someone is hit; glass shards;\n  a puck streak; a slapshot shockwave ring; KABOOM fire, explosions and sparks; steam from melt; snow (weather) at the\n  pond; confetti; hats; an octopus splat; a flying tooth on a big fight punch (a white bit, \"chiclets\"); dizzy stars\n  circling a knocked-down head; sweat drops in fights; turbo speed lines.\n- **Lighting**: canvas lights in every arena (11.2 lists them). Goal lights pulse red behind the net. KABOOM tints the\n  arena. Spotlights sweep during intros and the title.\n- **UI style**: dark blue-black panels (`E.ui.box` gradients) with ice-white text and a gold accent (`#ffd36a`),\n  with team colors on cards. Theme the engine's HTML screens with `new E.Shell(game, { theme })` in the same colors and\n  a large font: body text at least 24 CSS px at 1080p (check a screenshot).\n\n---\n\n## 9. Animation (the engine's procedural rigs plus new hockey motion)\n\nHockey motion is added by **wrapping `rig.solvePose`** on each skater and goalie rig (`Rigs`). It overrides feet,\nknees, hips, torso lean, hands and stick joints (`E.ik3` for knees and elbows) from a small state the Skater passes\nin (`skate: { phase, push, lean, stop, back, cross }`, `stick: { blade: [f, s, z], top, follow }`). Fights, cheers and\nfalls use the engine's own `attack` moves, `pose`, `down` and `flip`. Every animation below must play in all three views.\n\n| Motion | How |\n|---|---|\n| Skating stride | Phase advances by `speed / 22`. Each foot pushes back and out diagonally (3 o'clock or 9 o'clock), then recovers under the hip. Knees bend 35°, hips drop 2.5, the torso leans .35 rad (.5 with turbo). The free arm swings when not stick-handling |\n| Glide | Feet parallel, knees soft, a slight sway |\n| Crossovers | Turning hard at speed: the outside foot crosses over in front, alternating |\n| Hockey stop | The torso turns 70° off the velocity, both blades skid sideways with a deep knee bend, a spray at the feet |\n| Backward C-cuts | The hips swing, the feet trace C shapes (AI defenders only) |\n| Stick-handling | The blade weaves ±3 in front; the hands follow (the top hand at the hip, the bottom hand 40% down the shaft) |\n| Pass / saucer | The blade sweeps back to front toward the target; a saucer flicks up at the end |\n| Wrist shot | Weight shift, a fast sweep, a high follow-through |\n| Slapshot | Wind-up (the stick rises behind the shoulder and holds while charging), downswing to the ice, follow-through pointing at the target |\n| One-timer | A short wind-up already held, then the strike on contact |\n| Deke | Spin-o-rama (a 360° body spin with `flip`-like twist), toe drag (the blade pulls the puck back across) |\n| Check | The shoulder leads (lean into it), the stick across the chest |\n| Hit reaction / fall | A stagger (bump); `down` + `flip` tumble + a belly slide (big hit); squashed against the glass (`rig.kick(-.4)`) when hit into it; `getup` from a kneel |\n| Poke | The stick shoots forward along the ice in a lunge |\n| Slip | Feet fly up, landing on the back, a spin-slide (octopus, rat) |\n| Goalie | A ready crouch (pads together, glove up), shuffle and T-push, butterfly (knees down, pads flared), glove and blocker saves, pad stack, poke, covering the puck, celebrating, blasted (flailing backward into the net) |\n| Faceoff | Centers crouch with sticks down; the referee raises an arm and drops the puck; the swipe |\n| Celebrations | Fist pump, sniper aim (the stick held like a rifle), knee slide, stick guitar, bouncing off the glass, a team huddle |\n| Fights | Gloves off (sprites fall), circling in `stance: 'guard'`, one hand gripping the rival's jersey (the hand held at the rival's shoulder), `jab`, `haymaker` and `hook` from `E.MOVES`, a duck, jersey over the head (`hood`), the knockdown, the winner's `cheer` |\n| Bench and coach | Spares sit (a sit pose via solvePose: hips at bench height, knees forward); Coach Marge gestures (`wave`, `hips`) |\n| Story set pieces | The handshake line (two lines sliding past, hands out), the Cup lift (`cheer` with the Cup sprite held at the hands), the Flood Wagon driver seated and steering, Polar Pete's dance (a bulky white rig, a big round head from an extra ball drawn over it, ears), the organist playing (hands bobbing on the beat via `audio.onBeat`) |\n\n**Animation lab** (`#lab`, also in the Dev panel): one skater, one goalie and one referee on a small rink, a list of\nevery motion above, a slider for speed and phase, and a `brawler` / `threequarter` / `topdown` toggle. Film each\nmotion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (`--seed 1`) and check: the wind-up, the strike, the settle, no snaps or backward\nsweeps.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Audio (all synthesized in code; no audio files)\n\n### 10.1 Voices: babble (Animalese/Simlish style)\n- `Synth.babble(text, voice, { onLetter })` turns a line into syllables. Each letter that sounds (vowels, and\n  consonants as onsets) is a 55–85 ms blip: a `pulse` or `saw` source through two bandpass filters at the vowel's\n  formants (a: 800/1200 Hz, e: 500/1900, i: 300/2300, o: 500/900, u: 350/700; consonants borrow the next vowel and add\n  a 10 ms noise click for `s t k p` sounds). Pitch is the voice's base × (a letter-hash offset of ±3 semitones). `!`\n  raises the last 4 syllables by 4 semitones; `?` glides the last syllable up; `,` and `.` add 120 / 220 ms pauses.\n  It runs on the engine's new `voice` bus.\n- A voice is `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, speed: syllables/s, wave, formantShift, gruff (noise mix) }`. Marge: low,\n  gruff, slow. Dunny: mid and bright. Snipes: high and fast. Lou: very low, soft and slow. Lemmy: mid and wobbly\n  (vibrato). Glitterman: nasal (formants × 1.15), fast. Chuck: mid-high, very fast. Moose: low and gruff. The referee\n  barks single syllables. The crowd's chant mixes 6 voices.\n- It hooks into `E.Dialog` through the voice hook (section 4) for cutscenes and the booth, and into chirp bubbles,\n  intros (\"Number NINE… DUNNY… MACPHAIL!\"), the referee's calls and crowd chants. Its randomness comes from `RNG.fx`\n  so it never changes the simulation.\n\n### 10.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` voices; custom graphs where noted)\nSkate stride swish (filtered noise, pitch by speed, one per push); hockey stop \"shhhk\" (noise, a bandpass sweep down);\npuck on stick \"tock\"; pass \"thwap\"; wrist shot \"snap\"; slapshot crack plus whoosh; one-timer (a louder crack); **post\n\"PING\"** (triangle 1850 Hz, 0.9 s decay, a slight detune: the most recognizable sound in hockey); crossbar ping (2100\nHz); puck on boards (a low thud and a rattle); puck on glass (a sharp clack and a ring); net swish; body check thump\nplus a babble \"oof\"; big hit (a deeper thump, a glass rattle, crowd \"OHHH\"); glass crack (a sharp tick) and glass\nshatter (a noise burst and a descending sine tinkle cluster of 12 voices); the referee's whistle (a two-tone pea\nwhistle with vibrato); **the goal horn** (a custom graph: 3 detuned `brass` oscillators at 98, 147 and 196 Hz through\nthe lowpass `lp: 900`, 0.25 s attack, 2.6 s hold, then release, plus noise \"air\"); the period buzzer (square at 220 Hz,\n1.5 s); punches (a thud and a whoosh); dizzy stars twinkle; power-up pickup (an arpeggio); item throw (a whoosh);\noctopus \"splort\"; KABOOM explosion (engine `explode` + a sub-bass drop); the Flood Wagon engine (a looped low saw\nputter, pitch by speed), its horn \"A-OOGA\"; menu move, select and back (soft organ blips).\n\n### 10.3 Crowd and organ\n- **Crowd bed**: two looped noise sources (bandpass 400 Hz and 1.2 kHz, an LFO swell) whose gain follows\n  `Crowd.excitement` (0..1: raised by shots, near misses, hits, goals; decays). Plus reactions: \"OHHH\" (a swell\n  sweeping down), \"AHHH\" (a near miss), cheer (a burst with high-voiced babble), boo (low, filtered babble), the\n  \"KA-BOOM!\" chant (6-voice babble on the beat, with claps), and claps in rhythm.\n- **The organ** (`organ` wave, a Leslie-like vibrato of 6 Hz at .004): original stings only. A rising charge fanfare\n  (G4 C5 E5 G5 – E5 G5), a chromatic walk-up vamp for faceoffs, a clap-along vamp (\"da-da-da da-da\"), a sad trombone\n  slide for an opponent's penalty, a fight vamp (minor and tense), and a goal sting per team. In the Ol' Icebox, Doris\n  the organist plays them visibly. **Never copy existing chants or songs** (no \"Charge!\" bugle call, no stadium rock\n  standards).\n\n### 10.4 Music (engine song format; the new `organ` and `brass` waves; named layers)\n| Song | Use | Character |\n|---|---|---|\n| `theme` | title, attract | arena chip-rock anthem: saw power chords, a driving square lead, drums; the \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\" hook |\n| `menu` | menus, setup | a relaxed loop from the theme's chords |\n| `locker` | cutscenes (locker room) | gritty bass and a snare shuffle, organ pads |\n| `pond` | pond cutscenes, the pond arena's stoppages | a folksy pulse-wave fiddle tune in 6/8 |\n| `grind` | Grindhouse | a punk loop |\n| `mall` | MegaMall | cheesy synth-pop |\n| `final` | Dome cutscenes, the final | epic, brass |\n| `play` | under play (quiet) | a low pulse plus layers `drive` (in the third period and OT), `kaboom` (KABOOM mode), `fight` (fights) |\n| `flood` | the Flood Wagon minigame | an original skaters' waltz (3/4, organ) |\n| `victory`, `defeat` | results | a fanfare, a sad trombone |\n| `credits` | the end credits | the theme as a ballad, then full band |\n| goal stings ×6 | one per team | 2 bars over the horn |\n\n**Mix**: buses `music` (setting), `sfx` (setting), `voice` (setting: Voices) and the crowd (on sfx, plus its own\nsetting: Crowd). Duck the music under the commentary voice (−4 dB) and in the pause menu (the engine does this).\n\n---\n\n## 11. Content\n\n### 11.1 Teams (3 skaters + 1 goalie each; ratings 1–5: Spd / Sht / Pas / Hit / Fgt / Hnd; goalies Rfx / Size / Reb)\n| Team | Abbr | Home dark / away white trim | Logo (24×24) | Players |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Mukluk Falls Muskrats** | MUK | brown `#5a3a22`, gold `#e8b43a`, cream `#f3e6c8` | a buck-toothed muskrat face in a gold ring | #9 Duncan \"Dunny\" MacPhail, C, playmaker 4/3/5/3/2/4, shoots L · #19 Priya \"Snipes\" Sandhu, sniper 5/5/3/2/2/5, R · #44 Lou \"Big Lou\" Beaudoin, enforcer D (bulky) 2/4/2/5/5/2, R · G #31 Lemmy \"The Sieve\" Kowalchuk 3/4/3 (trait: **Talks to Posts**: 20% of goals within 4 of a post ring off it instead) |\n| **Dryfork Drillers** | DRY | black `#1d1d22`, orange `#f07a1a` | an oil derrick with a drop | #7 \"Rig\" McCoy, C 3/3/4/3/3/3 · #15 \"Gusher\" Gomez 4/4/3/2/2/4 · #2 \"Drill Bit\" Dobbs, D 3/2/2/4/3/2 · G #35 Derrick Okafor 2/3/2 |\n| **Logjam Lumberjacks** | LOG | red plaid `#b3262a` + black, cream | a bearded log face | #10 Axel Sundqvist, C 3/4/3/3/3/3 · #27 \"Sawdust\" Sally Lindgren 4/4/3/3/2/4 · #88 \"Big Timber\" Thibodeau, enforcer (bulky) 2/3/2/5/4/2 · G #1 \"Stumpy\" O'Rourke 3/4/3 |\n| **Grindhouse Bruise Brothers** | GRD | purple `#4b2a6b`, lime `#9be04a` | a fist inside a gear | #66 Rocco Bruiser (bulky) 3/3/2/5/5/2 · #67 Rollo Bruiser (bulky) 3/3/2/5/5/2 · #12 \"Mumbles\" Malone 4/4/3/2/3/4 · G #29 \"Tank\" Tankersley 3/5/2 |\n| **Megaplex Marauders** | MEG | teal `#18b5b0`, magenta `#e0389a` | a shopping cart flying a pirate flag | #23 Chad Glitterman, C 4/3/4/2/1/4 · #8 \"Zoom\" Zhang 5/3/3/2/2/4 · #5 \"Promo\" Perkins, D 3/3/3/4/3/3 · G #40 \"Kiosk\" Kingsley 4/3/4 |\n| **Gilded Grizzlies** | GLD | gold `#d9a520`, black `#141414`, white | a grizzly head in a crown | #1 Sterling Glitterman Jr. 5/5/4/3/2/5 (**Golden Twister**) · #91 \"Silk\" Sullivan 4/3/5/2/2/5 · #55 \"Brick\" Brickowski (bulky) 3/4/2/5/5/2 · G #00 **The Vault** 5/5/5 (boss: size 1.75) |\n\n- **Rating multipliers**: speed `0.85 + 0.05 Spd`; shot speed `0.85 + 0.05 Sht`, shot error `1.3 − 0.1 Sht`; pass\n  speed `0.9 + 0.033 Pas`; check `0.8 + 0.067 Hit`; fight damage `0.8 + 0.067 Fgt`; pickup radius `0.85 + 0.05 Hnd`.\n  Goalie reaction `−0.015 (Rfx − 3)`, save shapes × `0.9 + 0.033 Size`, freeze chance `+0.06 (Reb − 3)`.\n- **Golden Twister** (Sterling): in the offensive zone, 1 in 3 carries end in a 0.6 s spin with a golden glow\n  (telegraphed), then a curving shot (spin 1.2, like the SPORTS kit's curl) that cuts the CPU goalie's save chance by\n  25%. Checking him during the spin is a guaranteed big hit and BOOM +10.\n- **The Vault**: size 1.75; the first two KABOOM shots only stagger him (\"VAULT LOCKED\"). After the second, \"THE\n  VAULT IS CRACKED!\": size 1.4 and Rfx −1 for the rest of the game. Weak to cross-crease one-timers (lateral speed ×\n  0.8) and dekes (he bites 1.5×).\n- **Coach and staff portraits**: Coach Marge Pelletier (grey bun, cardigan, whistle), Old Gus (90, cap, the Flood\n  Wagon driver), Doris (organist, beehive hair), Goldie Glitterman (gold fur coat, sunglasses), Polar Pete (mascot),\n  and Chuck and Moose (suits; Moose is missing teeth).\n\n### 11.2 Arenas\n| Arena | Chapter | Look | Lights | Items | Hazard | Music |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **The Ol' Icebox** (Mukluk Falls) | 1, title, practice | wooden barrel-vault beams, string lights, 1962 championship banners, wooden stands, fans in toques, Doris's organ booth, a hand-painted scoreboard, ads (`MUKLUK MUFFLER & TIRE`, `KOWALCHUK'S PEROGIES`, `BAIT 'N' BAGELS`) | ambient .65 warm, 6 hanging lamps over the ice (light radius 260) | Hot Sauce, Tape, Poutine, BOOM Box | – | organ, `play` |\n| **Lake Kabonk** (pond) | 2 | a frozen lake at dusk, snowbank boards, pines, two cabins with lit windows, a bonfire with fans in parkas, string lights on poles, snowmen (store) | ambient .45 blue dusk, bonfire flicker, cabin windows, string lights; weather snow .5 | Hot Cocoa, Tape, Lumber, BOOM Box | thin ice ×3, snowbanks | `pond` |\n| **The Grindhouse** | 3 | a steel-truss mill arena, chain-link above the end boards, steam pipes, rowdy stands, a cage-match vibe, ads (`RUSTBELT SCRAP`, `IRON GUT CHILI`) | ambient .5 cool green, flickering fluorescents (`RNG.fx`), steam vents | Poutine, Lumber, BOOM Box | octopus throws after goals, rubber rats | `grind` |\n| **MegaMall Ice Palace** | 4 | a rink in a mall atrium: storefront neon, escalators, a fountain, a food court, ads on every inch (`GLITTERMAN MEGAPLEX — COMING SOON!`) | ambient .7, neon emissives in magenta and teal, fountain glow | Discount Drop crates (any item) | Polar Pete, Discount Drop | `mall` |\n| **The Kaboom Dome** | 5 | a huge arena: gold-trimmed boards, flame cannons in the corners, laser lights, fireworks, a sold-out crowd, a jumbotron frame on replays | ambient .55, strong white ceiling lights, moving spotlights in intros, flame light on goals and Kabooms | Hot Sauce, Brick Pads, BOOM Box | octopus (rare), Gilded Mode | `final` |\n\nEvery arena uses the same rink geometry. Walls, stands and props come from the TileMap (`types` for tiers with `face`\nmaterials), `r.shape` / `E.SHAPES` (new entries: `locker`, `bench-box`, `organ`, `net`, `glass-crew-cart`,\n`flood-wagon`, `flame-cannon`, `cabin`, `fountain`, `escalator`, `storefront`, `scoreboard`, `kaboom-cup`) and\n`r.prop` (lamps, banners, signs, torches as bonfire, trees).\n\n### 11.3 Story: THE CUP RUN\n\n**Premise**: Mukluk Falls (pop. 812) has one thing: the Ol' Icebox, a 1950s barn where the town learned to skate.\nDeveloper Goldie Glitterman bought the land and plans a \"Megaplex Parking Experience\". Coach Marge digs up **Town\nBylaw 1897-B**: *any rink that houses the Kaboom Cup shall stand forever.* So the Muskrats, a ragtag team of three\nskaters, a superstitious goalie and a 72-year-old coach, have to win the regional Kaboom Cup: five games, five\nbarns, five rivals. **Tone**: a small-town sports-movie comedy told like a hockey broadcast, with hockey clichés\nplayed with a straight face, chirps that rhyme, and big heart. PG: no blood, no slurs, no swearing (a beep and\nbabble stand in for \"a curse word\").\n\n**Chapter flow**: storymap (a snowy highway map; the team bus drives between 5 town stops, each showing its stars and\nlock) → pre-game cutscene (with one choice) → [chapter 1: optional warm-up drills 1–3] → player intros → the game (its\nobjectives listed on the pause screen and a pre-game card) → intermission Flood Wagon (offered) → post-game cutscene →\nresults and three stars → stars and unlocks → back to the map. **A loss**: a short Marge pep talk (a different one for\neach chapter, in TEXT) and Retry or Back to Map. Progress autosaves (`game.saves`) after each chapter and choice.\n\n**Choices** (one per chapter; they set the game's team tactic, 7.13): chapter 1 \"Clean and fast\" (Finesse) / \"Mean and\nloud\" (Grit); chapter 2 the same two; chapter 3 \"Let Lou loose\" (Lou Fgt +1, fights likelier) / \"Keep it on the ice\" (Lou\nPas +1); chapter 4 \"Ignore the bear\" / \"Hunt the bear\" (the AI targets Polar Pete); chapter 5 \"Doris plays early\"\n(the organ boost at the start of the 2nd period) / \"Doris plays late\" (at 5:00 left in the 3rd, +50% stronger).\n\n| # | Chapter | Arena / rival / rules | New mechanic spotlighted | Objectives (★ each) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Home Opener** | Ol' Icebox vs Dryfork Drillers, 3 × 1:30; the rivals play one difficulty step below the setting (never below Rookie) | skating, passing, shooting, one-timers, checking, BOOM meter, Flood Wagon | Win · Score a one-timer · Land 3 big hits |\n| 2 | **Pond Rules** | Lake Kabonk vs Logjam Lumberjacks, 3 × 1:30 | KABOOM mode (Marge explains it), power-ups, thin ice, snowbanks | Win · Break the ice under a Lumberjack · Trigger KABOOM |\n| 3 | **Gloves Off** | Grindhouse vs Bruise Brothers, 3 × 1:30, they challenge often | fights, the sin bin, power plays, hazards (octopi, rats), chirps | Win · Win 2 fights · Score a power-play goal |\n| 4 | **Mall Brawl** | MegaMall vs Megaplex Marauders, 3 × 1:30 with no OT, then a **Shootout Showcase** every time (it decides a tie; otherwise it is a bonus round for mall money and a toast) | the mascot, Discount Drop, the shootout and manual goalie | Win · Score a KABOOM goal · Knock down Polar Pete |\n| 5 | **The Kaboom Cup** | Kaboom Dome vs Gilded Grizzlies, 3 × 2:00, OT and shootout if tied | the boss: Sterling's Golden Twister, The Vault, Gilded Mode, Glitterman's Gilded Boost (Grizzlies +10% speed from the 3rd period), Doris's organ counter (Muskrats BOOM +30 and +10% speed for 20 s) | Win · Beat The Vault with a deke goal · One player scores a hat trick |\n\n**Script beats** (TEXT holds the full lines; these set the voice. Speakers in caps, choices in brackets):\n\n*Chapter 1 pre-game (locker room)*\n- MARGE: \"Sit down, shut up, and listen. I got a letter.\"\n- MARGE: \"Goldie Glitterman bought the land under the Icebox. Wants to pave it for a {c=#ffd36a}Megaplex Parking\n  Experience{/c}.\"\n- DUNNY: \"A parking… experience? Beauty. Wait. No. Not beauty.\"\n- SNIPES: \"This barn's got more character than his whole bank account. And his haircut.\"\n- MARGE: \"Bylaw 1897-B. Any rink that houses the Kaboom Cup stands forever. So we win the Cup.\"\n- LOU (knitting): \"Five games, then. Like the five petals of the wild rose.\"\n- LEMMY: \"Pipesy says we win. Clang's not so sure. Clang's a pessimist.\"\n- GLITTERMAN (in the doorway): \"Enjoy the barn, folks. I've ordered the parking meters. Gold ones.\"\n- MARGE: \"Captain. Tell 'em how we play tonight.\" [CLEAN AND FAST / MEAN AND LOUD]\n- DUNNY: \"We get pucks deep, we get bodies to the net, and we— uh— {$tacticLine}\"\n- MARGE: \"Warm-up's on. Then we drill the Drillers.\"\n\n*Chapter 1 post-game*: CHUCK: \"The Muskrats take the opener! The Icebox is ROCKIN'!\" · GLITTERMAN: \"Beginner's luck.\nThe meters are still on order.\" · MARGE: \"Pack your long johns. Lake Kabonk. Pond rules.\"\n\n*Chapter 2 pre-game (the lake at dusk, by the bonfire)*: BIG TIMBER: \"Welcome to the woods, Muskrats. We don't check.\nWe FELL.\" · SNIPES: \"Cute beard. Did you grow it, or did a beaver move in?\" · LEMMY: \"The ice is talking. It says\n'crack'.\" · MARGE: \"Thin ice is a tool. Hit 'em where it's thin.\" · MARGE: \"And listen. When the whole team's hummin'\n— hits, passes, the crowd losin' its mind — the ice starts to shake. That's a KABOOM. Fill the meter and let it\nrip.\" · LOU: \"Like thunder in a teacup.\" · [tactic choice]\n*Post*: BIG TIMBER: \"You hit like a falling spruce. Good on ya.\" · DUNNY: \"Thanks! You smell like one!\" · MARGE: \"Next\nstop, the Grindhouse. Bring a mouthguard. Bring two.\"\n\n*Chapter 3 pre-game (the Grindhouse's dim locker room)*: ROCCO: \"Well, well. Lou Beaudoin.\" · ROLLO: \"Lou 'The\nLibrary' Beaudoin.\" · ROCCO: \"Heard you knit now.\" · ROLLO: \"Heard you purl.\" · LOU: \"I have retired from fisticuffs,\ngentlemen.\" · MARGE: \"Retire after the game.\" · MARGE: \"In this barn they drop the gloves, you drop 'em back. Win the\nscrap, win the barn. Lose it, you sit in the sin bin and think about your choices.\" · [LET LOU LOOSE / KEEP IT ON THE\nICE]\n*Post*: ROLLO: \"He knitted me a scarf.\" · ROCCO: \"For my neck.\" · ROLLO: \"Which he bruised.\" · LOU: \"There is an ice pack\nin the pocket.\" · MARGE: \"Next, the Megaplex. Glitterman's turf. Watch your wallets.\"\n\n*Chapter 4 pre-game (rink-side under the neon)*: CHAD (filming himself): \"What's up, Mall Rats! Smash that glass,\nbro!\" · DUNNY: \"We're Muskrats.\" · CHAD: \"Same content, bro.\" · GLITTERMAN (to Lemmy): \"Name your price, goalie.\" ·\nLEMMY: \"…Pipesy says no. Clang says no with a curse word.\" · POLAR PETE: (a dance and a muffled babble) · MARGE:\n\"That bear's on the ice all game. Treat him like furniture.\" [IGNORE THE BEAR / HUNT THE BEAR] · MARGE: \"And win or\ntie, the mall's got a Shootout Showcase after. Mall money. We want it.\"\n*Post*: GLITTERMAN: \"Fine. The Final. My Grizzlies. My Dome. My rules.\" · SNIPES: \"Your Dome's gonna need a new roof.\"\n\n*Chapter 5 pre-game (the Dome's tunnel, then the spotlight intro)*: STERLING: \"I've never lost. Not once. Not even\nat Go Fish.\" · SNIPES: \"There's a first time for everything, Goldilocks.\" · THE VAULT: \"…\" · LEMMY: \"He's very big,\nPipesy.\" · MARGE: \"Forty-six years behind that bench. I've seen better teams. Prettier teams. Teams that could spell.\"\n· MARGE: \"Never saw one that wanted it more. Go make it go KABOOM.\" · [DORIS EARLY / DORIS LATE]\n*In-game*: when the Grizzlies' Gilded Boost starts, GLITTERMAN on the jumbotron: \"Synergy, boys!\" When Doris\nplays, MARGE: \"DORIS! PLAY THE SONG!\" (the organ's charge fanfare, the crowd claps, the boost).\n*Post (win), the ending*: the handshake line (both teams) → Dunny lifts the Kaboom Cup, which goes off in a confetti\nexplosion. CHUCK: \"THE KABOOM CUP IS… KA-BOOMING!\" → GLITTERMAN: \"My parking meters…\" → MARGE: \"Bylaw 1897-B, Goldie.\nLook it up.\" → GUS: \"Yep.\" → the Flood Wagon drives a lap with the team on top → **credits** over the run's highlight\nreplays (7.16), then Coach Marge: \"Same time next year.\" → the title, with the **Cup on display** in the Icebox from\nthen on.\n\n**Unlocks** (15 stars in all; exhibition cheats): 3★ Big Heads (`headR` × 1.8) · 6★ Octopus Rain · 9★ Glow Puck · 12★\nAlways KABOOM (for humans) · 15★ Retro Rigs (`style: 'classic'`). Finishing the story makes the Gilded Grizzlies and\nThe Vault playable in exhibition and adds the Cup to the title screen.\n\n### 11.4 Practice: Coach Marge's Drills (at the Ol' Icebox, house lights half on)\n| # | Drill | Pass condition | Teaches |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Wheels | skate through 6 gates in order in 25 s (one gate wants a hockey stop) | skating, turbo, stops |\n| 2 | Tape to Tape | 5 completed passes to moving teammates + 1 saucer over a sled | passes, saucers, aim |\n| 3 | Top Shelf | hit 4 corner targets on an empty net (wrist and slap) | shots, aim, lift |\n| 4 | One-Timers | 3 one-timer goals on Lemmy from Dunny's cross-crease feeds | one-timers |\n| 5 | Finish Your Check | big-hit 3 training dummies into the glass and break a panel | checks, turbo hits, glass |\n| 6 | Gloves Off | win a spar with Big Lou (he goes easy) | the fight controls |\n| 7 | KABOOM! | with a full meter, score with a KABOOM shot and survive Lou's KABOOM check | KABOOM mode |\n\nEach drill opens with a Marge line (voiced) and a prompt panel with glyph chips, tracks its counter in the HUD, and\nsaves its completion. Completing all 7 earns the \"Marge Approved\" badge (Records). Chapter 1 offers drills 1–3 as\nits warm-up.\n\n### 11.5 Text pools (in `07-data-text.js`; sizes are the minimums)\nCommentary: 18 event types × 4–8 lines (≈ 110 lines) plus 20 Moose filler anecdotes; chirps: 30; tips: 14;\nthree-stars lines: 12; loss pep talks: 5; menu blurbs: 1 per item; About pages (12.1). Appendix D has samples for each.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Screens and flows (10-foot UI)\n\n**Rules for every screen**: at most 6 choices visible; big tiles and cards; one line of help; a legend at the bottom\nwith glyph chips (`{pass} SELECT  {deke} BACK`, as keycaps or mouse icons for keyboard and mouse). D-pad, stick,\narrows and WASD move focus; ✕ / Enter / Space pick; ○ / Esc / Backspace go back. **The mouse hovering a tile focuses\nit and a click picks it.** Focus has an animated gold border, a slight scale-up and an organ blip. No dense tables\nanywhere: stats are a few big numbers.\n\n1. **Title**: the Ol' Icebox at night, spotlights sweeping the ice, two teams skating lazily (AI). The logo slams in\n   with an explosion and the horn, then `PRESS ANY BUTTON` (`TAP` is never shown; see 15.2). Then the main menu: 6 tiles\n   in 2 rows: **CUP RUN** (Continue/New when a save exists), **EXHIBITION**, **PRACTICE**, **RECORDS**, **SETTINGS**\n   (the engine's settings screen: `game.menu('settings')`), **ABOUT**. The version label (`E.versionLabel()` + the\n   game's version) sits small in a corner, and the engine corner buttons stay at the top right.\n2. **Exhibition → Sides**: every joined player is a token in the middle column (CPU); push left or right to join HOME\n   or AWAY; ✕ to ready. \"Press START on a free controller, or 2 on the keyboard, to join\" (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4\n   })`). The keyboard halves show their keys. Mouse: click HOME or AWAY to move the keyboard player's token.\n3. **Exhibition → Setup**: 3 big cards side by side: HOME team, ARENA, AWAY team (left/right on a focused card cycles\n   it; each team card shows its logo ×3, name, and 4 pip bars: Speed, Shooting, Hitting, Goalie). Below, one row of\n   option chips: Periods (1/2/3), Period length (1:00 / 1:30 / 2:00 / 3:00 / 4:00), Difficulty, Cheats (unlocked\n   ones). **FACE OFF!** starts.\n4. **Story map**: the bus on a snowy highway with 5 stops (each a town sign with its logo and earned stars). The stop\n   in focus shows the chapter title and objectives. Click a stop to pick it.\n5. **Cutscene**: the set (the locker room or rink-side), characters staged, `E.Dialog` boxes with live portraits,\n   babble and typed text; choices are 2 big options. ✕ advances; holding ○ for 1 s skips the scene (with a fill ring).\n6. **Pre-game card**: matchup logos, the arena, the objectives with ★ slots, the tactic chosen. ✕ FACE OFF.\n7. **Match** (HUD 7.18). **Pause** (engine): Resume, Objectives & Info (the story objectives, or the exhibition's\n   setup), Restart Game, **Dev Mode**, Settings, Controls, Full screen, Quit to title.\n8. **Intermission**: the period summary card (goals, shots, hits: big numbers), then `{pass} DRIVE THE FLOOD WAGON`\n   or `{deke} SKIP`.\n9. **Results**: the final score huge, the **three stars** revealed one by one (portrait cards, a stat line, a\n   commentary line), the objectives ticking ★, then CONTINUE / REMATCH / MAIN MENU.\n10. **Records**: big numbers with a label each: Hardest Shot (km/h = u/s ÷ 16 × 3.6), Biggest Hit, Most Goals in a\n    Game, Fights Won, KABOOMs, Story Stars x/15, Drills x/7. Two pages at most.\n11. **About**: section 12.1's pages, paged with L1/R1, left/right or a click on the arrows.\n12. **Credits**: the end roll over highlight replays.\n\n### 12.1 About / Credits screen\nPages (at most 8 lines each, in the large font): **Credits** (game design and code: Claude Opus 5.5, `claude-opus-5-5`,\nfor Michael Crosato's cc-matrix; engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2, MIT; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; every sound, voice and\nsong synthesized in code; asset-store props from CC0 sets, listed by name) · **Source Information** (every field TASK.md\nlists) · **Testing Feedback** · **Engine Feedback** · **Prompt Feedback** · **Engine changes** (the summary of\nENGINE-CHANGES.md). The builder fills the feedback pages at the end with the same text as the chat reply and\n`exit-interview.json`, writing \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Settings (via `menu.settings`; the engine's Display, Sound, Comfort and Controls stay)\nButton symbols (PlayStation / Xbox) · Difficulty (Rookie / Pro / All-Star / Legend) · Period length (exhibition default)\n· Camera (Broadcast / Overhead) · Camera distance (Near / Normal / Far) · Commentary (On / Off) · Subtitles (On / Off) ·\nVoices volume · Crowd volume · Player intros (On / Off) · Replays (Auto / Off) · Flood Wagon (Ask / Always / Never) ·\nPuck trail (Off / Streak / Glow) · Tips (On / Off) · Reset tips. Every one is read live.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Online: AI Hub sessions (`Net`, shared-world)\n\n### 14.1 Page tags (in `<head>`, after the session client)\n```html","numLines":340,"startLine":719,"totalLines":1473}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UNoYZyHfpqVF3pyoTa34H2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh22WKkWT9GMdkv9AbKg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CyH5dZmoMBRKjkWyQSpJm1","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","offset":1058,"limit":420},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15248,"cache_read_input_tokens":53467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15248},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"57810eb1-16b0-4f9b-be62-a155ca4fc0f4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:09.112Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh22W5sYbiyiABXTcG1i","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CyH5dZmoMBRKjkWyQSpJm1":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","offset":1058,"limit":420}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CyH5dZmoMBRKjkWyQSpJm1","type":"tool_result","content":"1058\t```html\n1059\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1060\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1061\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n1062\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n1063\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Outscore the other team in one 3-minute period\">\n1064\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD skate · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L deke · R2/Shift turbo\">\n1065\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n1066\t<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1067\t```\n1068\t\n1069\t### 14.2 Flow (when `AIHub.active`)\n1070\t1. There is no title, attract or menu. Boot first calls\n1071\t   `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If `info` is null, carry on\n1072\t   exactly as outside a session. Otherwise it picks the teams and the arena (step 2), builds the arena, and calls\n1073\t   `AIHub.ready()` (step 4).\n1074\t2. **Teams**: even seats (0, 2) are HOME and odd seats (1, 3) AWAY; with one player, that player is HOME vs the CPU.\n1075\t   The two teams and the arena are picked by `AIHub.rng('setup')`, the same on every copy; the host's first snapshot\n1076\t   confirms them. The CPU fills the rest. In a 2v1, the lone human's CPU teammates get AI skill +.15.\n1077\t3. **Our own card** (scene `session`, until `start`): the arena at night with spotlights; each player's skater lined\n1078\t   up on their team's blue line with a nameplate in their seat color (names sanitized for the pixel font, drawn on\n1079\t   the canvas, never put into HTML); \"HOW TO WIN: Outscore the other team in one 3-minute period\"; THIS PLAYER'S\n1080\t   CONTROLS as glyph chips for their device; a ✓ on each ready player; the countdown from the `card` event. Enter or\n1081\t   ✕ (button 0), or a click or tap on READY, calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △ (button 3), T, or a click on MORE TIME\n1082\t   calls `AIHub.answer('more')` (pressing again takes it back). The card changes nothing in the round.\n1083\t4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once the arena is built, with no key press.\n1084\t5. On `start`, show a big 3–2–1 while `AIHub.time() < 0`, then a faceoff at time 0. The match config is 1 period of\n1085\t   3:00, then sudden-death OT capped at 1:00, then a tie. Replays are 3 s, there are no intros and no Flood Wagon;\n1086\t   fights and items are on.\n1087\t6. **The host** (`info.isHost`) runs `Match.step` with all CPU AI and the remote players' intents. It calls\n1088\t   `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` exactly once: at the final horn, on `time-up` (at once, with\n1089\t   the current score), or when a round that began with 2+ players is down to one human (`leave`; the leavers are left\n1090\t   out of the standings). Standings list the winning team's remaining players in one array and the losers in the\n1091\t   next; a tie puts everyone in one array. With 1 player,\n1092\t   `standings: [[id]]` and `won: true | false`. `scores` maps each id to their own points (goals + assists); `stats`\n1093\t   maps each id to `{ Goals, Assists, Hits, Fights }`; `awards` are the three stars that are humans\n1094\t   (`{ id, title: '1st Star', detail }`).\n1095\t7. **Leaving**: a human who leaves becomes a CPU skater. The hub voids the round when the host leaves.\n1096\t8. On `end`: stop input and sound (`audio.music(null)`, mute), freeze on the final score, and send nothing more.\n1097\t9. **No pausing in a session**: the gameplay scene is not `pausable` and `autoPause` is off. Options (or Esc) opens a\n1098\t   small non-pausing overlay (Sound, Music, Voices, Button symbols, Camera, Back), during which the local skater\n1099\t   coasts. There is no Quit, Restart or Dev Mode. Create + Options belongs to the hub (engine patch 2). Use no\n1100\t   `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`, and no network but the hub.\n1101\t10. **Server copies** (`info.server`: the host with no player): they run the same host code with no local input or\n1102\t    camera and draw only a small \"HOSTING\" line.\n1103\t\n1104\t### 14.3 Netcode (it stays within 20 messages a second per copy and 16 KB per message)\n1105\t- **Clients → host**, 15 Hz, unreliable, `{ t: 'in', s: seq, at: AIHub.time() rounded, mx, my (×100 rounded),\n1106\t  h: bits (shoot, lob, turbo), c: [pass, shoot, deke, lob, chirp, switch] press counters (mod 256), ax, ay (aim, or\n1107\t  omitted) }`. The host turns counter differences into presses, so a lost packet loses no taps, and treats the\n1108\t  latest packet as held state. The host acknowledges with `ack` per player.\n1109\t- **Host → all**, 15 Hz, unreliable, under 1,200 bytes: `{ t: 's', n: tick, at, ph: phase code, p: period,\n1110\t  k: clock ×10, sc: [h, a], b: [boomH, boomA, kaboomFlags], pk: [x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, owner], e: [[id, x, y, vx, vy,\n1111\t  facing (0–255), state code, stateT ×10, flags], × 8 (6 skaters + 2 goalies)], ack: { playerId: seq }, it: items,\n1112\t  f: fight state (when fighting), ev: [recent events with ids, each repeated in 4 snapshots] }`. Integers only.\n1113\t- **Reliable host messages** (rare): `setup` (teams, arena, seat → skater map), `phase` changes (goal, period end,\n1114\t  final, fight start and end), and `glass` and `hole` state changes.\n1115\t- **Clients render** others interpolated about 120 ms behind the newest snapshot (two snapshot intervals less a\n1116\t  margin; tune it with the harness's latency and jitter settings). **Their own skater is predicted**: it\n1117\t  starts from the snapshot's authoritative state at `ack`, re-applies the pending intents with `Skater.skateStep`\n1118\t  (ignoring collisions), and blends the drawn position toward the result over 0.1 s, snapping when off by more than\n1119\t  48. While the client's skater owns the puck, the puck is drawn at its predicted blade. Each client plays effects,\n1120\t  sounds and commentary from the snapshot events it receives (deduplicated by id); the host sends commentary line ids\n1121\t  inside the events. Instant replays run on each copy from its own snapshot history.\n1122\t- **Budget**: the host sends 15 snapshots a second plus a few reliable messages, so it stays under 20/s. Each client\n1123\t  sends 15 inputs a second plus rare reliable messages.\n1124\t\n1125\t---\n1126\t\n1127\t## 15. Attract mode, touch-only devices and dev mode\n1128\t\n1129\t### 15.1 Attract mode (scene `attract`)\n1130\t- **Idle timer** on title, menus, side select, setup, the story map, records and about: 10 s without any input (keys,\n1131\t  buttons, clicks, wheel, a mouse move of more than 8 px, a stick or trigger past .3) → `game.go('attract', null,\n1132\t  { fade: 'dissolve' })`. Not during cutscenes, matches or the engine's open menus, and never in sessions.\n1133\t- **The reel**: a script (`game.script`) of segments, each built on the real match simulation with every skater on\n1134\t  AI, cheats free (infinite turbo, forced events, warping the puck or players). Each loop picks a new arena and teams.\n1135\t  1. *Puck Drop* (8 s): the intro spotlights, a faceoff, play.\n1136\t  2. *Big Hits* (8 s): a forced turbo big hit into the glass, which shatters.\n1137\t  3. *Highlight Goal* (12 s): a set-up 2-on-1, a cross-crease pass, a one-timer goal, the horn and the instant replay.\n1138\t  4. *Gloves Off* (10 s): an AI-vs-AI fight to a knockdown.\n1139\t  5. *KABOOM!* (10 s): forced KABOOM mode, a KABOOM shot that blasts the goalie into the net.\n1140\t  6. *Fan Frenzy* (7 s): items thrown and grabbed; an octopus slip.\n1141\t  7. *Story teaser* (8 s): 3 cutscene lines with portraits and babble.\n1142\t  8. *Flood Wagon* (6 s): the AI driver resurfacing scuffed ice.\n1143\t  9. *Records card* (5 s): the logo, `PRESS ANY BUTTON`, and the top records.\n1144\t  The loop is about 75 s, then it starts again.\n1145\t- **Overlay**: a `DEMO` tag, the logo bug, and `PRESS ANY BUTTON` (glyph per device) blinking. On touch-only devices\n1146\t  it reads \"Controller or keyboard required\" instead.\n1147\t- **Any input** ends it: back to the title with that input consumed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it triggers nothing\n1148\t  else. The audio follows the settings (browsers stay silent until a first gesture anyway).\n1149\t\n1150\t### 15.2 Touch-only devices\n1151\t- **Detection**: `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, no gamepad\n1152\t  seen, and no key pressed since load. Re-check on `gamepadconnected` and the first `keydown`; either one switches to\n1153\t  normal at once.\n1154\t- **Touch-only**: no touch controls anywhere (`touch: []` on every scene, the engine's touch buttons hidden). The title\n1155\t  shows a large banner, \"Controller or keyboard required\", and a big **SETTINGS** button (a tap opens\n1156\t  `game.menu('settings')`); the engine's corner menu button stays. Taps don't start the game. The attract mode runs by\n1157\t  the same 10 s rule, and taps don't leave it (only to open Settings).\n1158\t\n1159\t### 15.3 Dev mode (scene overlay `Dev`, from the pause menu's **Dev Mode** item; also `#dev`)\n1160\t- Choosing it closes the engine's pause menu and opens the Dev panel. While the panel is open the match holds its own\n1161\t  `devPause` flag (the engine's `game.paused` is false, so the panel can read input), unless **Live** is toggled on: the panel docks to the right at 45% width and the game runs behind it, so slider\n1162\t  changes show at once.\n1163\t- **Navigation**: L1/R1 (or Tab, or a click) switch tabs; up/down move; left/right adjust (hold to accelerate; L2/R2\n1164\t  ×10 steps); △ (or R) resets the row; **RESET ALL TO DEFAULTS** is the first row of TUNING; ○ / Esc closes. The mouse\n1165\t  hovers to focus rows, drags sliders and clicks toggles. Each row shows its value and its default.\n1166\t- **TUNING** tab: every `T` key with a slider (Appendix A), grouped Skating, Puck & Passing, Shooting, Goalies,\n1167\t  Hitting, AI, BOOM & Items, Fights, Match. Values persist in `E.store('dev:tuning')`. **Log tuning** prints a JSON of\n1168\t  the non-default values to the console, for designers.\n1169\t- **CHEATS**: infinite turbo; god mode (no knockdowns); always KABOOM; puck magnet (the puck comes to the human's\n1170\t  blade); freeze AI; CPU goalies off; big heads; octopus rain; glow puck; retro rigs; instant BOOM full (an action).\n1171\t- **WARP**: start any chapter or cutscene; jump to period 2, 3 or OT, or the shootout; set the clock to 0:10; score\n1172\t  +1 for home or away; win or lose this game now; spawn each item or hazard at center; start a fight; start KABOOM;\n1173\t  break the thin ice; shatter a panel; trigger the Flood Wagon; go to results, attract, about or the lab.\n1174\t- **DEBUG**: overlays (bodies and radii, blade points, AI roles and targets, the puck's predicted path, goalie save\n1175\t  shapes, grudge numbers, rig skeletons via `rig.debug(r)`), FPS, slow motion (1, .5, .25), frame step (paused: ✕\n1176\t  advances one step), free camera (the stick pans, the triggers zoom), hide the HUD (screenshot mode), the RNG seed,\n1177\t  and a **sound test** (play every sfx, song, layer, organ sting and voice, including a babble line per character).\n1178\t- **Not available in AI Hub sessions.**\n1179\t\n1180\t---\n1181\t\n1182\t## 16. Build order and milestones\n1183\tBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tests/run.mjs`) and a look at its screenshots.\n1184\tThe game must be playable from M3 on.\n1185\t\n1186\t| M | Deliverable | Acceptance |\n1187\t|---|---|---|\n1188\t| **M0 Setup** | dev folder, the engine copied, the vendor files, `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` running an empty suite, `src/` skeleton, a title scene that boots in the browser and headless, ENGINE-CHANGES.md started | the built HTML opens from `file://` with no errors (`tools/check.mjs`); the headless boot test passes |\n1189\t| **M1 Rink, skating, rigs** | `Rink` geometry and drawing (ice, lines, boards, glass panels, nets, benches), the floor TileMap, `skateStep`, SkaterRig (stride, glide, stop, crossovers, stick idle), the broadcast camera, the animation lab | unit tests for geometry and skating; filmstrips of stride and stop look right; screenshots of the Icebox rink in all 3 views |\n1190\t| **M2 Puck play** | the puck, possession, stick-handling, passes (lead, saucer), one-timers, wrist and slap shots, goal detection, posts, net bulge, Goalie v1 (positioning, save solver, rebounds, freeze), HOCKEY_KEYS, mouse and right-stick aim, glyph chips, font patch, HUD v1 | headless: a pass reaches a stationary and a moving mate; a shot into an empty net scores; a shot at the goalie is saved; a post hit emits `post`; glyph labels per device |\n1191\t| **M3 First playable match** | Match flow (faceoffs, clock, stoppages, goals, celebrations, periods, final, results, three stars), team AI, the referee, the crowd v1, audio v1 (sfx, the horn, the organ, the crowd bed, the theme), Exhibition Setup (1 player) | AI vs AI plays 3 periods with no errors and 3–12 goals; a bot-driven human match (the bot of 18.3) completes; `balance.mjs` runs |\n1192\t| **M4 Over the top** | checks, knockdowns, the glass, turbo, deke, poke, BOOM and KABOOM, items and hazards, chirps, commentary with babble voices, instant replay, Fx | headless: the big-hit threshold, glass crack then shatter, KABOOM start, shot and end, item effects, replay playback ends and returns to a faceoff |\n1193\t| **M5 Fights, OT, multiplayer, menus** | fights and the sin bin, OT and the shootout (manual goalie), local 1–4 players and side select, all 10-foot menus, settings, records, about | headless: a fight from gloves to a winner and the sin bin timer; a shootout to a decision; 4 inputs each moving their own skater; mouse hover focus and click in menus (browser) |\n1194\t| **M6 Story and content** | all 5 arenas dressed (lights, props, crowds, hazards), all 6 teams, the story map, the cutscene runner and every script, choices, objectives, stars and unlocks, the Flood Wagon minigame, the 7 practice drills, the boss (The Vault, Golden Twister, Gilded Mode, Boost and organ), the ending and credits with highlights, saves | the whole-story playthrough test passes (18.3); screenshots of every arena and every cutscene set |\n1195\t| **M7 Attract, touch, dev** | the attract reel, idle detection, touch-only mode, the Dev panel (all 4 tabs), the sound test | headless: idle 10 s → attract; all 9 segments visited; any input → title; dev slider change and reset; browser: a touch-only emulation shows the banner and attract runs |\n1196\t| **M8 AI Hub** | `Net` (connect, card, host and client, prediction, events, finish), the metas, session flow | the fake-hub headless test (18.5) passes; the real harness passes in all 4 configurations (18.6) |\n1197\t| **M9 Polish and balance** | tuning passes with `balance.mjs`, act on `check.mjs` look notes, every screenshot reviewed at 1280×720 and 1920×1080, the About pages and `exit-interview.json` filled in, the final build | the full `node tests/run.mjs` is green; no TODO or placeholder strings; `exit-interview.json` parses; the HTML runs from `file://` with no network requests |\n1198\t\n1199\t---\n1200\t\n1201\t## 17. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1202\t| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n1203\t|---|---|---|\n1204\t| Skater and stick animation | new motion on a procedural rig decides whether it reads as hockey | built first (M1) in the animation lab; filmstrip every motion; keep solvePose overrides small and data-driven; fall back to the engine's poses for rare states |\n1205\t| Puck feel (possession, passes, one-timers) | the core of the fun; easy to get floaty or sticky | every constant a slider from day one; headless pass and shot tests; play it at M2 before building on it |\n1206\t| Goalie believability | too good is frustrating, too weak is boring | a physical save solver (reaction, lateral speed, shapes) rather than dice; `balance.mjs` shoots 200 shots per type and checks the save-rate bands in 7.6 |\n1207\t| Curved boards, glass and depth sorting | custom drawing in a tile engine | far boards as background, end and corner panels queued per panel, near boards cut low; screenshots in all views at M1 |\n1208\t| Netcode under latency, loss and limits | shared world, 20 msgs/s, unreliable packets | a pure `skateStep` for prediction; press counters; snapshots under 1,200 bytes (a test asserts it); a fake hub in Node with latency and loss before the real harness |\n1209\t| Hub compliance | a session fails the harness's checklist | follow 14.2 step by step; the harness at M8 in all 4 configurations; no pause, quit or dialogs in sessions |\n1210\t| Audio quality (babble, horn, organ) | voices can sound like noise | the sound test in Dev from M4; tune formants by ear; keep the voice bus quieter than the sfx bus |\n1211\t| PlayStation glyphs in the pixel font | they rendered as `?` | the font patch plus glyph chips at M2; a test renders each chip |\n1212\t| Scope | a big demo | milestones in value order; data-driven content; the systems shared by story, drills, attract and sessions (all are `Match` configs) |\n1213\t| Determinism (replays, tests, attract) | hidden `Math.random` use | only `RNG.sim` in the simulation; a test runs the same seed twice and compares a state hash |\n1214\t\n1215\t---\n1216\t\n1217\t## 18. Testing\n1218\t\n1219\t**One command**: `node tests/run.mjs` builds, then runs every suite in order and prints **only failures** plus one\n1220\tline: `ICE HOC-KABOOM TESTS: 214 passed, 0 failed (headless 9 suites, browser 3, hub 4) in 182 s`.\n1221\t`--quick` runs only the headless suites; `--only <suite>` reruns one (after changing the code it covers). Headless\n1222\tsuites load `build/game.js` into a `vm` context with the stand-ins from `engine/kits/test.mjs` (`window`,\n1223\t`addEventListener`, `location`). They drive the game with `game.advance`, `input.tap` and `input.hold`, and read\n1224\t`game.debug.snapshot()`. No subagents or workflows review anything; the scripts decide.\n1225\t\n1226\t### 18.1 Unit (pure functions)\n1227\tRink inside, normal and clamp at corners; the faceoff dot table; `skateStep` (time to top speed, stop distance, turn\n1228\tradius at speed, turbo drain); puck friction distance; board reflection angles; post ping; goal-line crossing (inside\n1229\tvs post); pass lead hits a moving mate; shot aim stays inside the mouth for σ = 0; save-shape tests; impulse\n1230\tthresholds; BOOM gain table; fight damage and stamina; tuning reset and resetAll; the glyph label per device and\n1231\tsetting; the name sanitizer; snapshot encode, decode and size (< 1,200 bytes for 8 entities, 3 items and 4 events);\n1232\tinput packet press counters across a dropped packet; objective predicates.\n1233\t\n1234\t### 18.2 Systems (headless game)\n1235\t- A faceoff leads to possession within 2 s.\n1236\t- A scripted wrist shot from the slot at an empty net scores.\n1237\t- A slapshot at the goalie from the blue line is saved.\n1238\t- A one-timer cross-crease scores at least 4 of 10 seeded tries.\n1239\t- A turbo check at full speed knocks down; a second hit into the same panel shatters it, and the puck leaves through\n1240\t  it → a faceoff.\n1241\t- Holding △ near a rival with a grudge starts a fight; scripted jabs win it; the loser is in the sin bin for 20 s; a\n1242\t  power-play banner shows.\n1243\t- Filling BOOM starts KABOOM; a KABOOM shot blasts the goalie; it ends after 15 s.\n1244\t- Each item applies its effect and expires; thin ice breaks after a big hit; a skater in a hole is frozen 3 s.\n1245\t- The period ends at 0:00 → intermission → the next period; OT is sudden death; the shootout reaches a decision.\n1246\t- Results show three stars.\n1247\t- 4 local players each move only their own skater.\n1248\t- Replay plays and returns.\n1249\t- The same seed and inputs twice give the same state hash after 60 s (determinism).\n1250\t\n1251\t### 18.3 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (`tests/play-story.mjs`)\n1252\tFrom boot: title → CUP RUN → for chapters 1 to 5: advance the cutscene (tap confirm; take choice 1 in chapters 1, 3\n1253\tand 5, choice 2 in 2 and 4), run warm-up drills 1–3 in chapter 1 by script, then play the match with **the bot\n1254\tcontrolling the human team's skater through `game.input`** (the CPU intent turned into stick and buttons, as in the\n1255\tSPORTS kit's `bot()`), with dev tuning giving the home team AI skill .95 and the rivals .3 so each game is won in real\n1256\tplay. Play 1 period for real, then warp the clock to 0:05 for the remaining periods, keeping the lead. Play the\n1257\tintermission Flood Wagon once with the bot steering, the chapter 4 Shootout Showcase, and the chapter 5 boss phases\n1258\t(the Boost and organ events must fire). Then the post-game, results, the map, the ending, credits and back to the\n1259\ttitle. Assert at each stage: the expected scene and chapter, at least one goal per game, no errors, stars recorded,\n1260\tthe save written, and every chapter's new mechanic event seen (one-timer, kaboom_start, thin_ice_break, fight_end,\n1261\tmascot_down, shootout_end, vault_cracked or a boss goal). If real play hasn't produced a chapter's signature event by\n1262\tthe end of its first period, trigger it with the Dev warp (`game.debug.warp('breakIce')` and the like), then assert\n1263\tthat the game handled it (its consequences, commentary and objective). Also play **Practice drills 1–7** by script and\n1264\tassert each passes.\n1265\t\n1266\t### 18.4 Other headless suites\n1267\t- **Attract**: idle 10 s from the title → attract; run 80 s; all 9 segments visited; tapping confirm → title with\n1268\t  the input consumed.\n1269\t- **Dev**: open from the pause menu item; change 3 sliders (the values apply to the match); reset one; reset all\n1270\t  (all defaults); a cheat toggles; warps work.\n1271\t- **Exhibition**: 60 s with 4 players, each scheme.\n1272\t- **Balance** (`balance.mjs`; it also prints a table when run alone): 20 AI-vs-AI games at Pro, averaging 5–10 goals\n1273\t  a game; save % .78–.90; at least 2 fights per 10 games; KABOOM 1–4 per game; plus 7.6's shot-type bands.\n1274\t- **Text**: every TEXT pool meets its minimum; every `{token}` resolves; no line wider than its box at scale 1.\n1275\t\n1276\t### 18.5 Fake-hub network test (headless, Node)\n1277\tTwo to four `vm` contexts, each with the engine, the game and a fake `AIHub` (an in-memory bus with configurable\n1278\tlatency 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss). It runs connect → card (scripted ready) → start → 60 s of scripted play → time-up.\n1279\tAssert: the host's and clients' scores match; a client's own-skater error stays below 12 u on average; presses are\n1280\tnever lost; `finish` is called once with valid standings; a leaving client's skater turns CPU; a server-mode host\n1281\tworks.\n1282\t\n1283\t### 18.6 Browser suites (Playwright 1.63, Chromium; `TMPDIR` set)\n1284\t- `engine/tools/check.mjs` on the built HTML and on `#match/muskrats/drillers/icebox`, `#fight` and `#kaboom`: no\n1285\t  errors, and every look note handled.\n1286\t- **Menus and input**: keyboard navigation through the main menu; mouse hover moves focus and a click picks;\n1287\t  `lastDevice` changes switch the prompt chips; Settings → Xbox changes the chips.\n1288\t- **Touch-only**: `--size 390x844@3` with coarse-pointer emulation shows the banner and SETTINGS, and attract starts\n1289\t  after 10 s.\n1290\t- **Hub harness**: serve `dev/hub/` (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page title, kill by\n1291\t  PID afterwards). Open `harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1`; then\n1292\t  `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; then the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; then\n1293\t  `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Each waits for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and asserts\n1294\t  `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, printing the failed checks otherwise. Then the game outside a session still\n1295\t  reaches the title.\n1296\t\n1297\t### 18.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge; `tests/shots.mjs`)\n1298\tAt 1280×720 and 1920×1080: title, the attract segments, side select with 4 players, setup, every arena at a faceoff,\n1299\ta big hit and shattered glass, a fight, KABOOM mode, a goal celebration, a replay, results with three stars, a\n1300\tcutscene with a portrait, the story map, a drill, the Flood Wagon, the Dev panel, Settings with Xbox glyphs, the\n1301\tAbout pages, the session card (from the harness), and the touch-only banner at 390×844. Look at every one, comparing\n1302\tagainst the look target (8) and the 10-foot rules (12).\n1303\t\n1304\t---\n1305\t\n1306\t## 19. Definition of done (TASK.md → where it is met)\n1307\t- [ ] Genre and perspective chosen and used (0, 7.15). Title from a real RNG (0).\n1308\t- [ ] Single HTML with the given name, the dev folder, no network requests (1).\n1309\t- [ ] Built on the handoff engine; changes logged (4) and summarized in About.\n1310\t- [ ] Native look with new hockey art (8); native animation with new hockey motion (9).\n1311\t- [ ] All audio in code; gibberish voices (10).\n1312\t- [ ] AI Hub sessions passing the harness, plus local multiplayer for the game on its own (14, 6.1, 12).\n1313\t- [ ] Feature-complete demo: story, exhibition, practice, records and every mechanic shown in play, drills and attract\n1314\t      (11, 12, 15.1).\n1315\t- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders and reset to defaults (15.3).\n1316\t- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on title and menus; any input exits (15.1).\n1317\t- [ ] 10-foot, controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse (aim, hover focus, click); prompts follow the last\n1318\t      device; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option (6, 12).\n1319\t- [ ] Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract runs (15.2).\n1320\t- [ ] Narrative tone: hockey broadcast and small-town hockey comedy (11.3, Appendix D).\n1321\t- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs (a test enforces it).\n1322\t- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About\n1323\t      screen; `exit-interview.json` in TASK.md's exact shape, parsing as JSON. Suggested `aiHub` values: name\n1324\t      \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\"; tagline \"Over-the-top 3-on-3 arcade hockey\"; description \"Glass-shattering hits, dropped\n1325\t      gloves and explosive KABOOM slapshots as the Mukluk Falls Muskrats fight to save their rink. Story, exhibition\n1326\t      and up to four players.\"; type \"Game\"; genre \"Sports\"; source \"Ice hockey\"; series \"\"; players \"1–4\"; controls\n1327\t      \"Stick/WASD skate · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L deke · △/I saucer & gloves · R2/Shift turbo\"; tags\n1328\t      `[\"arcade\", \"sports\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\", \"story\"]`. The Source Information `plan` field is\n1329\t      `PLAN.md`.\n1330\t\n1331\t---\n1332\t\n1333\t## Appendix A: Tuning defaults (`T`; every row is a Dev slider)\n1334\t| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Meaning |\n1335\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1336\t| Skating | skateMax | 132 | 80–200 | top speed (u/s) at rating 3 |\n1337\t| | skateAccel | 300 | 120–600 | acceleration |\n1338\t| | iceGlide | 28 | 0–120 | coasting deceleration |\n1339\t| | turnSlow / turnFast | 5.0 / 2.6 | 1–10 | rad/s at low and top speed |\n1340\t| | edgeGrip | 6 | 1–20 | sideways decay /s |\n1341\t| | stopDecel | 700 | 300–1400 | hockey-stop deceleration |\n1342\t| | turboMul | 1.45 | 1–2 | turbo speed factor |\n1343\t| | turboDrain / turboRegen | 0.45 / 0.18 | 0–2 | meter per second |\n1344\t| Puck & passing | puckFriction / puckDrag | 26 / 0.12 | 0–80 / 0–.5 | puck deceleration |\n1345\t| | boardBounce | 0.62 | .2–1 | boards restitution |\n1346\t| | pickupRadius | 8 | 4–16 | blade pickup |\n1347\t| | passMin / passMax | 240 / 420 | 150–600 | pass speeds |\n1348\t| | saucerApex | 10 | 4–24 | saucer height |\n1349\t| Shooting | wristSpeed | 330 | 200–500 | wrist shot |\n1350\t| | slapBase / slapGain | 380 / 160 | 200–600 / 0–400 | slapshot |\n1351\t| | slapCharge | 0.9 | .3–2 | seconds to full |\n1352\t| | oneTimerBonus | 1.15 | 1–1.6 | one-timer factor |\n1353\t| | shotError | 1.0 | 0–3 | scales all shot σ |\n1354\t| Goalies | goalieReact | 0.16 | .05–.4 | base reaction (s) |\n1355\t| | goalieLateral | 150 | 60–300 | lateral speed |\n1356\t| | goalieReach | 1.0 | .6–1.6 | save-shape scale |\n1357\t| | gloveCatch | 0.55 | 0–1 | glove freeze chance |\n1358\t| | reboundSpeed | 0.35 | 0–.8 | rebound factor |\n1359\t| | kaboomBlast | 0.6 | 0–1 | blast carries the puck in |\n1360\t| Hitting | checkPower | 1.0 | .3–3 | impulse scale |\n1361\t| | knockdown | 150 | 60–300 | big-hit threshold |\n1362\t| | glassCrack / glassShatter | 170 / 240 | 80–400 | board-impact speeds |\n1363\t| | accidentalHit | 180 | 80–400 | knockdown with no check |\n1364\t| AI | aiSkillHome / aiSkillAway | by difficulty | 0–1 | skill overrides (dev) |\n1365\t| | aiAggression | 0.5 | 0–1 | check vs poke |\n1366\t| | aiItemGreed | 120 | 0–300 | item detour range |\n1367\t| | aiShootRange | 200 | 80–400 | shooting zone |\n1368\t| BOOM & items | boomGain | 1.0 | 0–4 | all BOOM gains |\n1369\t| | kaboomTime | 15 | 5–40 | KABOOM seconds |\n1370\t| | itemEvery | 35 | 8–120 | mean seconds between throws |\n1371\t| Fights | fightBalance | 100 | 40–200 | fighter balance |\n1372\t| | fightGrudge | 40 | 0–100 | prompt threshold |\n1373\t| | fightMax | 3 | 0–10 | per game |\n1374\t| | sinBin | 20 | 5–60 | seconds |\n1375\t| Match | periodLen | 120 | 30–300 | exhibition period (s) |\n1376\t| | gameSpeed | 1.0 | .25–2 | `game.timeScale` |\n1377\t| | crowdHype | 1.0 | 0–2 | crowd reaction scale |\n1378\t\n1379\t## Appendix B: Event catalogue (`Bus`; consumers: stats, objectives, Talk, Fx, Crowd, Net, Replay)\n1380\t`faceoff_drop`, `faceoff_won{team, by}`, `possession{by}`, `pass{from, to, kind}`, `pass_complete`,\n1381\t`intercept{by}`, `shot{by, kind, speed, onGoal}`, `save{goalie, kind, freeze}`, `post{by, bar}`,\n1382\t`block{by}`, `goal{team, by, assists, kind, ppg}`, `stop{by}`, `rattle{x, y}`, `hit{by, victim, power, big}`,\n1383\t`glass{panel, state}`, `knockdown{victim}`, `deke{by}`, `deke_beat{by, victim}`, `poke{by, ok}`,\n1384\t`chirp{by, target, line}`, `gloves{by, target}`, `turtle{by}`, `fight_start{a, b}`, `fight_hit{by, kind, dmg}`,\n1385\t`fight_end{winner, loser}`, `sin_bin{who, t}`, `sin_bin_end{who}`, `item_throw{kind}`, `item{by, kind}`,\n1386\t`hazard{kind, victim}`, `thin_ice_break{patch}`, `plunge{victim}`, `mascot_down{by}`, `boom{team, n}`,\n1387\t`kaboom_start{team}`, `kaboom_end{team}`, `kaboom_shot{by}`, `blast{goalie}`, `vault_cracked`, `twister{by}`,\n1388\t`period_end{n}`, `intermission`, `ot_start`, `shootout_start`, `shootout_attempt{by, ok}`, `shootout_end{team}`,\n1389\t`final{winner}`, `hat_trick{by}`, `hoser_hat_trick{by}`, `boost_start`, `organ_boost`.\n1390\t\n1391\t## Appendix C: Cutscene data format\n1392\t```js\n1393\t{ id: 'ch1-pre', set: 'locker', music: 'locker',\n1394\t  cast: [{ id: 'marge', at: [96, 60], facing: Math.PI / 2 }, { id: 'dunny', at: [70, 92] }, /* … */],\n1395\t  steps: [\n1396\t    { cam: [96, 72], zoom: 1.4, t: 0 },\n1397\t    { say: 'marge', text: 'Sit down, shut up, and listen. I got a letter.', expr: 'angry' },\n1398\t    { move: 'glitterman', to: [130, 40], t: 1.2 },\n1399\t    { pose: 'lou', pose: 'kneel' },\n1400\t    { sfx: 'organ-sting-sad' },\n1401\t    { choice: { who: 'marge', text: \"Captain. Tell 'em how we play tonight.\",\n1402\t                options: [['CLEAN AND FAST', { tactic: 'finesse' }], ['MEAN AND LOUD', { tactic: 'grit' }]] } },\n1403\t    { wait: 0.4 } ] }\n1404\t```\n1405\tThe runner (`game.script`) plays steps in order: `say` waits for the dialog to close; `move` and `cam` tween; a\n1406\t`choice` sets story flags (saved). Hold ○ to skip, which applies the default choice.\n1407\t\n1408\t## Appendix D: Writing samples (the voice to match; TEXT holds the full pools)\n1409\t**Booth: CHUCK (play-by-play: present tense, rapid verbs, crescendo)**\n1410\t- \"Puck's dropped and we're under way at {arena}!\"\n1411\t- \"{name} with speed, through center, over the line—\"\n1412\t- \"{name} dangles, dances, and DEKES!\"\n1413\t- \"Big wind-up… {name} with the CLAPPER!\"\n1414\t- \"{name} SHOOTS — {name} SCORES!\"\n1415\t- \"TOP SHELF, where Grandma hides the cookie tin!\"\n1416\t- \"Bar down! They heard that one in the parking lot!\"\n1417\t- \"One-timer — BANG! {name} buries it!\"\n1418\t- \"Five-hole! Right between the pads!\"\n1419\t- \"Glove save, and a BEAUTY!\"\n1420\t- \"Off the POST! The iron says no!\"\n1421\t- \"OH! {victim} just got a free trip to next Tuesday!\"\n1422\t- \"THROUGH THE GLASS! Somebody get a broom!\"\n1423\t- \"The gloves are off! {a} and {b} are going at it!\"\n1424\t- \"The meter's full… it's… KA-BOOOOM!\"\n1425\t- \"The puck went in, and the GOALIE went with it!\"\n1426\t- \"Polar Pete is DOWN! Somebody check on the bear!\"\n1427\t- \"HAT TRICK! Here come the hats!\"\n1428\t- \"That's the end of the {period}. {home} {hs}, {away} {as}.\"\n1429\t\n1430\t**Booth: MOOSE (color: folksy, mangled metaphors, ex-enforcer)**\n1431\t- \"He stopped that with his face, Chuck. You can't teach that.\"\n1432\t- \"Ding-dong, nobody home.\"\n1433\t- \"He hit him so hard his ancestors felt it.\"\n1434\t- \"That's a delivery, Chuck, and nobody signed for it.\"\n1435\t- \"That glass is coming out of somebody's paycheque.\"\n1436\t- \"Now THIS is hockey. Grab a seat. Grab a hot dog. Grab two.\"\n1437\t- \"Octopus on the ice. It's tradition, Chuck. Don't ask which tradition.\"\n1438\t- \"I played eleven seasons. Lost fourteen teeth. Found nine.\"\n1439\t- \"My first coach said I had the hands of a surgeon. Then he saw me skate.\"\n1440\t- \"Thin ice? I never skated on the thick stuff.\"\n1441\t- \"Somebody call the fire department. And my mother.\"\n1442\t\n1443\t**Chirps (rhymes and comparisons, PG)**\n1444\t- \"Nice flow! Did your mom cut it with a skate blade?\"\n1445\t- \"You skate like a fridge on a waterbed!\"\n1446\t- \"Is that a stick or a toothpick?\"\n1447\t- \"Your five-hole's wider than the highway!\"\n1448\t- \"You're a pylon with a pulse!\"\n1449\t- \"Hey goalie, want a net? You're not using yours!\"\n1450\t- \"Your slapshot couldn't pop a bubble!\"\n1451\t- \"You've got the hockey sense of a boiled perogy!\"\n1452\t- \"Nice turnover! Bake it yourself?\"\n1453\t- \"My grandma checks harder, and she's ninety!\"\n1454\t\n1455\t**Tips (Coach Marge; `{action}` becomes a glyph chip)**\n1456\t- \"Skate with the stick. Hold {turbo} to turbo. It runs out, so pick your moments.\"\n1457\t- \"{pass} passes. Point where you want it to go.\"\n1458\t- \"Tap {shoot} for a wrister. Hold it for a slapshot. Let go to fire.\"\n1459\t- \"Pass coming your way? Hit {shoot} for a ONE-TIMER.\"\n1460\t- \"No puck? {shoot} checks, {deke} pokes, {pass} switches to whoever's closest.\"\n1461\t- \"With the puck, {deke} dekes past a check. Fools goalies too.\"\n1462\t- \"Hits, passes, saves, goals: they fill the BOOM meter. Fill it and the whole team goes KABOOM.\"\n1463\t- \"Somebody's got a grudge. Hold {lob} to drop the gloves.\"\n1464\t- \"In a scrap: {pass} jab, {shoot} haymaker, {deke} duck, {lob} yank the sweater.\"\n1465\t- \"Fans throw goodies on the ice. Skate over 'em.\"\n1466\t- \"Power play! They're a skater short. Move it and shoot.\"\n1467\t- \"{lob} with the puck flips a saucer over their sticks.\"\n1468\t- \"{chirp} chirps. Gets in their heads.\"\n1469\t- \"Shootout! In net: {pass} butterfly, {shoot} poke, {deke} dive.\"\n1470\t\n1471\t**Three stars (CHUCK)**: \"The third star: {name}, who hit everything but the Flood Wagon.\" · \"Second star: {name},\n1472\twith {g} goals and a smile that could melt the ice.\" · \"And the first star of the game… {name}!\"\n1473\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"20d546e7-1aad-485c-aa52-d25f44269498","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:27:09.250Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261103-182647__x9a2bbb/work/PLAN.md","content":"```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Outscore the other team in one 3-minute period\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD skate · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L deke · R2/Shift turbo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n```\n\n### 14.2 Flow (when `AIHub.active`)\n1. There is no title, attract or menu. Boot first calls\n   `info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If `info` is null, carry on\n   exactly as outside a session. Otherwise it picks the teams and the arena (step 2), builds the arena, and calls\n   `AIHub.ready()` (step 4).\n2. **Teams**: even seats (0, 2) are HOME and odd seats (1, 3) AWAY; with one player, that player is HOME vs the CPU.\n   The two teams and the arena are picked by `AIHub.rng('setup')`, the same on every copy; the host's first snapshot\n   confirms them. The CPU fills the rest. In a 2v1, the lone human's CPU teammates get AI skill +.15.\n3. **Our own card** (scene `session`, until `start`): the arena at night with spotlights; each player's skater lined\n   up on their team's blue line with a nameplate in their seat color (names sanitized for the pixel font, drawn on\n   the canvas, never put into HTML); \"HOW TO WIN: Outscore the other team in one 3-minute period\"; THIS PLAYER'S\n   CONTROLS as glyph chips for their device; a ✓ on each ready player; the countdown from the `card` event. Enter or\n   ✕ (button 0), or a click or tap on READY, calls `AIHub.answer('ready')`. △ (button 3), T, or a click on MORE TIME\n   calls `AIHub.answer('more')` (pressing again takes it back). The card changes nothing in the round.\n4. Call `AIHub.ready()` once the arena is built, with no key press.\n5. On `start`, show a big 3–2–1 while `AIHub.time() < 0`, then a faceoff at time 0. The match config is 1 period of\n   3:00, then sudden-death OT capped at 1:00, then a tie. Replays are 3 s, there are no intros and no Flood Wagon;\n   fights and items are on.\n6. **The host** (`info.isHost`) runs `Match.step` with all CPU AI and the remote players' intents. It calls\n   `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, stats, awards })` exactly once: at the final horn, on `time-up` (at once, with\n   the current score), or when a round that began with 2+ players is down to one human (`leave`; the leavers are left\n   out of the standings). Standings list the winning team's remaining players in one array and the losers in the\n   next; a tie puts everyone in one array. With 1 player,\n   `standings: [[id]]` and `won: true | false`. `scores` maps each id to their own points (goals + assists); `stats`\n   maps each id to `{ Goals, Assists, Hits, Fights }`; `awards` are the three stars that are humans\n   (`{ id, title: '1st Star', detail }`).\n7. **Leaving**: a human who leaves becomes a CPU skater. The hub voids the round when the host leaves.\n8. On `end`: stop input and sound (`audio.music(null)`, mute), freeze on the final score, and send nothing more.\n9. **No pausing in a session**: the gameplay scene is not `pausable` and `autoPause` is off. Options (or Esc) opens a\n   small non-pausing overlay (Sound, Music, Voices, Button symbols, Camera, Back), during which the local skater\n   coasts. There is no Quit, Restart or Dev Mode. Create + Options belongs to the hub (engine patch 2). Use no\n   `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt` or `window.open`, and no network but the hub.\n10. **Server copies** (`info.server`: the host with no player): they run the same host code with no local input or\n    camera and draw only a small \"HOSTING\" line.\n\n### 14.3 Netcode (it stays within 20 messages a second per copy and 16 KB per message)\n- **Clients → host**, 15 Hz, unreliable, `{ t: 'in', s: seq, at: AIHub.time() rounded, mx, my (×100 rounded),\n  h: bits (shoot, lob, turbo), c: [pass, shoot, deke, lob, chirp, switch] press counters (mod 256), ax, ay (aim, or\n  omitted) }`. The host turns counter differences into presses, so a lost packet loses no taps, and treats the\n  latest packet as held state. The host acknowledges with `ack` per player.\n- **Host → all**, 15 Hz, unreliable, under 1,200 bytes: `{ t: 's', n: tick, at, ph: phase code, p: period,\n  k: clock ×10, sc: [h, a], b: [boomH, boomA, kaboomFlags], pk: [x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, owner], e: [[id, x, y, vx, vy,\n  facing (0–255), state code, stateT ×10, flags], × 8 (6 skaters + 2 goalies)], ack: { playerId: seq }, it: items,\n  f: fight state (when fighting), ev: [recent events with ids, each repeated in 4 snapshots] }`. Integers only.\n- **Reliable host messages** (rare): `setup` (teams, arena, seat → skater map), `phase` changes (goal, period end,\n  final, fight start and end), and `glass` and `hole` state changes.\n- **Clients render** others interpolated about 120 ms behind the newest snapshot (two snapshot intervals less a\n  margin; tune it with the harness's latency and jitter settings). **Their own skater is predicted**: it\n  starts from the snapshot's authoritative state at `ack`, re-applies the pending intents with `Skater.skateStep`\n  (ignoring collisions), and blends the drawn position toward the result over 0.1 s, snapping when off by more than\n  48. While the client's skater owns the puck, the puck is drawn at its predicted blade. Each client plays effects,\n  sounds and commentary from the snapshot events it receives (deduplicated by id); the host sends commentary line ids\n  inside the events. Instant replays run on each copy from its own snapshot history.\n- **Budget**: the host sends 15 snapshots a second plus a few reliable messages, so it stays under 20/s. Each client\n  sends 15 inputs a second plus rare reliable messages.\n\n---\n\n## 15. Attract mode, touch-only devices and dev mode\n\n### 15.1 Attract mode (scene `attract`)\n- **Idle timer** on title, menus, side select, setup, the story map, records and about: 10 s without any input (keys,\n  buttons, clicks, wheel, a mouse move of more than 8 px, a stick or trigger past .3) → `game.go('attract', null,\n  { fade: 'dissolve' })`. Not during cutscenes, matches or the engine's open menus, and never in sessions.\n- **The reel**: a script (`game.script`) of segments, each built on the real match simulation with every skater on\n  AI, cheats free (infinite turbo, forced events, warping the puck or players). Each loop picks a new arena and teams.\n  1. *Puck Drop* (8 s): the intro spotlights, a faceoff, play.\n  2. *Big Hits* (8 s): a forced turbo big hit into the glass, which shatters.\n  3. *Highlight Goal* (12 s): a set-up 2-on-1, a cross-crease pass, a one-timer goal, the horn and the instant replay.\n  4. *Gloves Off* (10 s): an AI-vs-AI fight to a knockdown.\n  5. *KABOOM!* (10 s): forced KABOOM mode, a KABOOM shot that blasts the goalie into the net.\n  6. *Fan Frenzy* (7 s): items thrown and grabbed; an octopus slip.\n  7. *Story teaser* (8 s): 3 cutscene lines with portraits and babble.\n  8. *Flood Wagon* (6 s): the AI driver resurfacing scuffed ice.\n  9. *Records card* (5 s): the logo, `PRESS ANY BUTTON`, and the top records.\n  The loop is about 75 s, then it starts again.\n- **Overlay**: a `DEMO` tag, the logo bug, and `PRESS ANY BUTTON` (glyph per device) blinking. On touch-only devices\n  it reads \"Controller or keyboard required\" instead.\n- **Any input** ends it: back to the title with that input consumed (`input.consumeAll()`), so it triggers nothing\n  else. The audio follows the settings (browsers stay silent until a first gesture anyway).\n\n### 15.2 Touch-only devices\n- **Detection**: `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches`, no gamepad\n  seen, and no key pressed since load. Re-check on `gamepadconnected` and the first `keydown`; either one switches to\n  normal at once.\n- **Touch-only**: no touch controls anywhere (`touch: []` on every scene, the engine's touch buttons hidden). The title\n  shows a large banner, \"Controller or keyboard required\", and a big **SETTINGS** button (a tap opens\n  `game.menu('settings')`); the engine's corner menu button stays. Taps don't start the game. The attract mode runs by\n  the same 10 s rule, and taps don't leave it (only to open Settings).\n\n### 15.3 Dev mode (scene overlay `Dev`, from the pause menu's **Dev Mode** item; also `#dev`)\n- Choosing it closes the engine's pause menu and opens the Dev panel. While the panel is open the match holds its own\n  `devPause` flag (the engine's `game.paused` is false, so the panel can read input), unless **Live** is toggled on: the panel docks to the right at 45% width and the game runs behind it, so slider\n  changes show at once.\n- **Navigation**: L1/R1 (or Tab, or a click) switch tabs; up/down move; left/right adjust (hold to accelerate; L2/R2\n  ×10 steps); △ (or R) resets the row; **RESET ALL TO DEFAULTS** is the first row of TUNING; ○ / Esc closes. The mouse\n  hovers to focus rows, drags sliders and clicks toggles. Each row shows its value and its default.\n- **TUNING** tab: every `T` key with a slider (Appendix A), grouped Skating, Puck & Passing, Shooting, Goalies,\n  Hitting, AI, BOOM & Items, Fights, Match. Values persist in `E.store('dev:tuning')`. **Log tuning** prints a JSON of\n  the non-default values to the console, for designers.\n- **CHEATS**: infinite turbo; god mode (no knockdowns); always KABOOM; puck magnet (the puck comes to the human's\n  blade); freeze AI; CPU goalies off; big heads; octopus rain; glow puck; retro rigs; instant BOOM full (an action).\n- **WARP**: start any chapter or cutscene; jump to period 2, 3 or OT, or the shootout; set the clock to 0:10; score\n  +1 for home or away; win or lose this game now; spawn each item or hazard at center; start a fight; start KABOOM;\n  break the thin ice; shatter a panel; trigger the Flood Wagon; go to results, attract, about or the lab.\n- **DEBUG**: overlays (bodies and radii, blade points, AI roles and targets, the puck's predicted path, goalie save\n  shapes, grudge numbers, rig skeletons via `rig.debug(r)`), FPS, slow motion (1, .5, .25), frame step (paused: ✕\n  advances one step), free camera (the stick pans, the triggers zoom), hide the HUD (screenshot mode), the RNG seed,\n  and a **sound test** (play every sfx, song, layer, organ sting and voice, including a babble line per character).\n- **Not available in AI Hub sessions.**\n\n---\n\n## 16. Build order and milestones\nBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tests/run.mjs`) and a look at its screenshots.\nThe game must be playable from M3 on.\n\n| M | Deliverable | Acceptance |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0 Setup** | dev folder, the engine copied, the vendor files, `tools/build.mjs`, `tests/run.mjs` running an empty suite, `src/` skeleton, a title scene that boots in the browser and headless, ENGINE-CHANGES.md started | the built HTML opens from `file://` with no errors (`tools/check.mjs`); the headless boot test passes |\n| **M1 Rink, skating, rigs** | `Rink` geometry and drawing (ice, lines, boards, glass panels, nets, benches), the floor TileMap, `skateStep`, SkaterRig (stride, glide, stop, crossovers, stick idle), the broadcast camera, the animation lab | unit tests for geometry and skating; filmstrips of stride and stop look right; screenshots of the Icebox rink in all 3 views |\n| **M2 Puck play** | the puck, possession, stick-handling, passes (lead, saucer), one-timers, wrist and slap shots, goal detection, posts, net bulge, Goalie v1 (positioning, save solver, rebounds, freeze), HOCKEY_KEYS, mouse and right-stick aim, glyph chips, font patch, HUD v1 | headless: a pass reaches a stationary and a moving mate; a shot into an empty net scores; a shot at the goalie is saved; a post hit emits `post`; glyph labels per device |\n| **M3 First playable match** | Match flow (faceoffs, clock, stoppages, goals, celebrations, periods, final, results, three stars), team AI, the referee, the crowd v1, audio v1 (sfx, the horn, the organ, the crowd bed, the theme), Exhibition Setup (1 player) | AI vs AI plays 3 periods with no errors and 3–12 goals; a bot-driven human match (the bot of 18.3) completes; `balance.mjs` runs |\n| **M4 Over the top** | checks, knockdowns, the glass, turbo, deke, poke, BOOM and KABOOM, items and hazards, chirps, commentary with babble voices, instant replay, Fx | headless: the big-hit threshold, glass crack then shatter, KABOOM start, shot and end, item effects, replay playback ends and returns to a faceoff |\n| **M5 Fights, OT, multiplayer, menus** | fights and the sin bin, OT and the shootout (manual goalie), local 1–4 players and side select, all 10-foot menus, settings, records, about | headless: a fight from gloves to a winner and the sin bin timer; a shootout to a decision; 4 inputs each moving their own skater; mouse hover focus and click in menus (browser) |\n| **M6 Story and content** | all 5 arenas dressed (lights, props, crowds, hazards), all 6 teams, the story map, the cutscene runner and every script, choices, objectives, stars and unlocks, the Flood Wagon minigame, the 7 practice drills, the boss (The Vault, Golden Twister, Gilded Mode, Boost and organ), the ending and credits with highlights, saves | the whole-story playthrough test passes (18.3); screenshots of every arena and every cutscene set |\n| **M7 Attract, touch, dev** | the attract reel, idle detection, touch-only mode, the Dev panel (all 4 tabs), the sound test | headless: idle 10 s → attract; all 9 segments visited; any input → title; dev slider change and reset; browser: a touch-only emulation shows the banner and attract runs |\n| **M8 AI Hub** | `Net` (connect, card, host and client, prediction, events, finish), the metas, session flow | the fake-hub headless test (18.5) passes; the real harness passes in all 4 configurations (18.6) |\n| **M9 Polish and balance** | tuning passes with `balance.mjs`, act on `check.mjs` look notes, every screenshot reviewed at 1280×720 and 1920×1080, the About pages and `exit-interview.json` filled in, the final build | the full `node tests/run.mjs` is green; no TODO or placeholder strings; `exit-interview.json` parses; the HTML runs from `file://` with no network requests |\n\n---\n\n## 17. Risks and how to de-risk them\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| Skater and stick animation | new motion on a procedural rig decides whether it reads as hockey | built first (M1) in the animation lab; filmstrip every motion; keep solvePose overrides small and data-driven; fall back to the engine's poses for rare states |\n| Puck feel (possession, passes, one-timers) | the core of the fun; easy to get floaty or sticky | every constant a slider from day one; headless pass and shot tests; play it at M2 before building on it |\n| Goalie believability | too good is frustrating, too weak is boring | a physical save solver (reaction, lateral speed, shapes) rather than dice; `balance.mjs` shoots 200 shots per type and checks the save-rate bands in 7.6 |\n| Curved boards, glass and depth sorting | custom drawing in a tile engine | far boards as background, end and corner panels queued per panel, near boards cut low; screenshots in all views at M1 |\n| Netcode under latency, loss and limits | shared world, 20 msgs/s, unreliable packets | a pure `skateStep` for prediction; press counters; snapshots under 1,200 bytes (a test asserts it); a fake hub in Node with latency and loss before the real harness |\n| Hub compliance | a session fails the harness's checklist | follow 14.2 step by step; the harness at M8 in all 4 configurations; no pause, quit or dialogs in sessions |\n| Audio quality (babble, horn, organ) | voices can sound like noise | the sound test in Dev from M4; tune formants by ear; keep the voice bus quieter than the sfx bus |\n| PlayStation glyphs in the pixel font | they rendered as `?` | the font patch plus glyph chips at M2; a test renders each chip |\n| Scope | a big demo | milestones in value order; data-driven content; the systems shared by story, drills, attract and sessions (all are `Match` configs) |\n| Determinism (replays, tests, attract) | hidden `Math.random` use | only `RNG.sim` in the simulation; a test runs the same seed twice and compares a state hash |\n\n---\n\n## 18. Testing\n\n**One command**: `node tests/run.mjs` builds, then runs every suite in order and prints **only failures** plus one\nline: `ICE HOC-KABOOM TESTS: 214 passed, 0 failed (headless 9 suites, browser 3, hub 4) in 182 s`.\n`--quick` runs only the headless suites; `--only <suite>` reruns one (after changing the code it covers). Headless\nsuites load `build/game.js` into a `vm` context with the stand-ins from `engine/kits/test.mjs` (`window`,\n`addEventListener`, `location`). They drive the game with `game.advance`, `input.tap` and `input.hold`, and read\n`game.debug.snapshot()`. No subagents or workflows review anything; the scripts decide.\n\n### 18.1 Unit (pure functions)\nRink inside, normal and clamp at corners; the faceoff dot table; `skateStep` (time to top speed, stop distance, turn\nradius at speed, turbo drain); puck friction distance; board reflection angles; post ping; goal-line crossing (inside\nvs post); pass lead hits a moving mate; shot aim stays inside the mouth for σ = 0; save-shape tests; impulse\nthresholds; BOOM gain table; fight damage and stamina; tuning reset and resetAll; the glyph label per device and\nsetting; the name sanitizer; snapshot encode, decode and size (< 1,200 bytes for 8 entities, 3 items and 4 events);\ninput packet press counters across a dropped packet; objective predicates.\n\n### 18.2 Systems (headless game)\n- A faceoff leads to possession within 2 s.\n- A scripted wrist shot from the slot at an empty net scores.\n- A slapshot at the goalie from the blue line is saved.\n- A one-timer cross-crease scores at least 4 of 10 seeded tries.\n- A turbo check at full speed knocks down; a second hit into the same panel shatters it, and the puck leaves through\n  it → a faceoff.\n- Holding △ near a rival with a grudge starts a fight; scripted jabs win it; the loser is in the sin bin for 20 s; a\n  power-play banner shows.\n- Filling BOOM starts KABOOM; a KABOOM shot blasts the goalie; it ends after 15 s.\n- Each item applies its effect and expires; thin ice breaks after a big hit; a skater in a hole is frozen 3 s.\n- The period ends at 0:00 → intermission → the next period; OT is sudden death; the shootout reaches a decision.\n- Results show three stars.\n- 4 local players each move only their own skater.\n- Replay plays and returns.\n- The same seed and inputs twice give the same state hash after 60 s (determinism).\n\n### 18.3 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (`tests/play-story.mjs`)\nFrom boot: title → CUP RUN → for chapters 1 to 5: advance the cutscene (tap confirm; take choice 1 in chapters 1, 3\nand 5, choice 2 in 2 and 4), run warm-up drills 1–3 in chapter 1 by script, then play the match with **the bot\ncontrolling the human team's skater through `game.input`** (the CPU intent turned into stick and buttons, as in the\nSPORTS kit's `bot()`), with dev tuning giving the home team AI skill .95 and the rivals .3 so each game is won in real\nplay. Play 1 period for real, then warp the clock to 0:05 for the remaining periods, keeping the lead. Play the\nintermission Flood Wagon once with the bot steering, the chapter 4 Shootout Showcase, and the chapter 5 boss phases\n(the Boost and organ events must fire). Then the post-game, results, the map, the ending, credits and back to the\ntitle. Assert at each stage: the expected scene and chapter, at least one goal per game, no errors, stars recorded,\nthe save written, and every chapter's new mechanic event seen (one-timer, kaboom_start, thin_ice_break, fight_end,\nmascot_down, shootout_end, vault_cracked or a boss goal). If real play hasn't produced a chapter's signature event by\nthe end of its first period, trigger it with the Dev warp (`game.debug.warp('breakIce')` and the like), then assert\nthat the game handled it (its consequences, commentary and objective). Also play **Practice drills 1–7** by script and\nassert each passes.\n\n### 18.4 Other headless suites\n- **Attract**: idle 10 s from the title → attract; run 80 s; all 9 segments visited; tapping confirm → title with\n  the input consumed.\n- **Dev**: open from the pause menu item; change 3 sliders (the values apply to the match); reset one; reset all\n  (all defaults); a cheat toggles; warps work.\n- **Exhibition**: 60 s with 4 players, each scheme.\n- **Balance** (`balance.mjs`; it also prints a table when run alone): 20 AI-vs-AI games at Pro, averaging 5–10 goals\n  a game; save % .78–.90; at least 2 fights per 10 games; KABOOM 1–4 per game; plus 7.6's shot-type bands.\n- **Text**: every TEXT pool meets its minimum; every `{token}` resolves; no line wider than its box at scale 1.\n\n### 18.5 Fake-hub network test (headless, Node)\nTwo to four `vm` contexts, each with the engine, the game and a fake `AIHub` (an in-memory bus with configurable\nlatency 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss). It runs connect → card (scripted ready) → start → 60 s of scripted play → time-up.\nAssert: the host's and clients' scores match; a client's own-skater error stays below 12 u on average; presses are\nnever lost; `finish` is called once with valid standings; a leaving client's skater turns CPU; a server-mode host\nworks.\n\n### 18.6 Browser suites (Playwright 1.63, Chromium; `TMPDIR` set)\n- `engine/tools/check.mjs` on the built HTML and on `#match/muskrats/drillers/icebox`, `#fight` and `#kaboom`: no\n  errors, and every look note handled.\n- **Menus and input**: keyboard navigation through the main menu; mouse hover moves focus and a click picks;\n  `lastDevice` changes switch the prompt chips; Settings → Xbox changes the chips.\n- **Touch-only**: `--size 390x844@3` with coarse-pointer emulation shows the banner and SETTINGS, and attract starts\n  after 10 s.\n- **Hub harness**: serve `dev/hub/` (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`, confirm the page title, kill by\n  PID afterwards). Open `harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1`; then\n  `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; then the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; then\n  `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. Each waits for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and asserts\n  `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, printing the failed checks otherwise. Then the game outside a session still\n  reaches the title.\n\n### 18.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge; `tests/shots.mjs`)\nAt 1280×720 and 1920×1080: title, the attract segments, side select with 4 players, setup, every arena at a faceoff,\na big hit and shattered glass, a fight, KABOOM mode, a goal celebration, a replay, results with three stars, a\ncutscene with a portrait, the story map, a drill, the Flood Wagon, the Dev panel, Settings with Xbox glyphs, the\nAbout pages, the session card (from the harness), and the touch-only banner at 390×844. Look at every one, comparing\nagainst the look target (8) and the 10-foot rules (12).\n\n---\n\n## 19. Definition of done (TASK.md → where it is met)\n- [ ] Genre and perspective chosen and used (0, 7.15). Title from a real RNG (0).\n- [ ] Single HTML with the given name, the dev folder, no network requests (1).\n- [ ] Built on the handoff engine; changes logged (4) and summarized in About.\n- [ ] Native look with new hockey art (8); native animation with new hockey motion (9).\n- [ ] All audio in code; gibberish voices (10).\n- [ ] AI Hub sessions passing the harness, plus local multiplayer for the game on its own (14, 6.1, 12).\n- [ ] Feature-complete demo: story, exhibition, practice, records and every mechanic shown in play, drills and attract\n      (11, 12, 15.1).\n- [ ] Dev mode from the pause menu with live sliders and reset to defaults (15.3).\n- [ ] Attract mode after 10 s idle on title and menus; any input exits (15.1).\n- [ ] 10-foot, controller-first UI; native keyboard and mouse (aim, hover focus, click); prompts follow the last\n      device; PlayStation glyphs with an Xbox option (6, 12).\n- [ ] Touch-only: \"Controller or keyboard required\", the settings button, attract runs (15.2).\n- [ ] Narrative tone: hockey broadcast and small-town hockey comedy (11.3, Appendix D).\n- [ ] No TODOs, placeholders or stubs (a test enforces it).\n- [ ] Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in the chat reply **and** the About\n      screen; `exit-interview.json` in TASK.md's exact shape, parsing as JSON. Suggested `aiHub` values: name\n      \"Ice Hoc-Kaboom\"; tagline \"Over-the-top 3-on-3 arcade hockey\"; description \"Glass-shattering hits, dropped\n      gloves and explosive KABOOM slapshots as the Mukluk Falls Muskrats fight to save their rink. Story, exhibition\n      and up to four players.\"; type \"Game\"; genre \"Sports\"; source \"Ice hockey\"; series \"\"; players \"1–4\"; controls\n      \"Stick/WASD skate · ✕/J pass · □/K shoot · ○/L deke · △/I saucer & gloves · R2/Shift turbo\"; tags\n      `[\"arcade\", \"sports\", \"versus\", \"comedy\", \"pixel art\", \"story\"]`. The Source Information `plan` field is\n      `PLAN.md`.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: Tuning defaults (`T`; every row is a Dev slider)\n| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Skating | skateMax | 132 | 80–200 | top speed (u/s) at rating 3 |\n| | skateAccel | 300 | 120–600 | acceleration |\n| | iceGlide | 28 | 0–120 | coasting deceleration |\n| | turnSlow / turnFast | 5.0 / 2.6 | 1–10 | rad/s at low and top speed |\n| | edgeGrip | 6 | 1–20 | sideways decay /s |\n| | stopDecel | 700 | 300–1400 | hockey-stop deceleration |\n| | turboMul | 1.45 | 1–2 | turbo speed factor |\n| | turboDrain / turboRegen | 0.45 / 0.18 | 0–2 | meter per second |\n| Puck & passing | puckFriction / puckDrag | 26 / 0.12 | 0–80 / 0–.5 | puck deceleration |\n| | boardBounce | 0.62 | .2–1 | boards restitution |\n| | pickupRadius | 8 | 4–16 | blade pickup |\n| | passMin / passMax | 240 / 420 | 150–600 | pass speeds |\n| | saucerApex | 10 | 4–24 | saucer height |\n| Shooting | wristSpeed | 330 | 200–500 | wrist shot |\n| | slapBase / slapGain | 380 / 160 | 200–600 / 0–400 | slapshot |\n| | slapCharge | 0.9 | .3–2 | seconds to full |\n| | oneTimerBonus | 1.15 | 1–1.6 | one-timer factor |\n| | shotError | 1.0 | 0–3 | scales all shot σ |\n| Goalies | goalieReact | 0.16 | .05–.4 | base reaction (s) |\n| | goalieLateral | 150 | 60–300 | lateral speed |\n| | goalieReach | 1.0 | .6–1.6 | save-shape scale |\n| | gloveCatch | 0.55 | 0–1 | glove freeze chance |\n| | reboundSpeed | 0.35 | 0–.8 | rebound factor |\n| | kaboomBlast | 0.6 | 0–1 | blast carries the puck in |\n| Hitting | checkPower | 1.0 | .3–3 | impulse scale |\n| | knockdown | 150 | 60–300 | big-hit threshold |\n| | glassCrack / glassShatter | 170 / 240 | 80–400 | board-impact speeds |\n| | accidentalHit | 180 | 80–400 | knockdown with no check |\n| AI | aiSkillHome / aiSkillAway | by difficulty | 0–1 | skill overrides (dev) |\n| | aiAggression | 0.5 | 0–1 | check vs poke |\n| | aiItemGreed | 120 | 0–300 | item detour range |\n| | aiShootRange | 200 | 80–400 | shooting zone |\n| BOOM & items | boomGain | 1.0 | 0–4 | all BOOM gains |\n| | kaboomTime | 15 | 5–40 | KABOOM seconds |\n| | itemEvery | 35 | 8–120 | mean seconds between throws |\n| Fights | fightBalance | 100 | 40–200 | fighter balance |\n| | fightGrudge | 40 | 0–100 | prompt threshold |\n| | fightMax | 3 | 0–10 | per game |\n| | sinBin | 20 | 5–60 | seconds |\n| Match | periodLen | 120 | 30–300 | exhibition period (s) |\n| | gameSpeed | 1.0 | .25–2 | `game.timeScale` |\n| | crowdHype | 1.0 | 0–2 | crowd reaction scale |\n\n## Appendix B: Event catalogue (`Bus`; consumers: stats, objectives, Talk, Fx, Crowd, Net, Replay)\n`faceoff_drop`, `faceoff_won{team, by}`, `possession{by}`, `pass{from, to, kind}`, `pass_complete`,\n`intercept{by}`, `shot{by, kind, speed, onGoal}`, `save{goalie, kind, freeze}`, `post{by, bar}`,\n`block{by}`, `goal{team, by, assists, kind, ppg}`, `stop{by}`, `rattle{x, y}`, `hit{by, victim, power, big}`,\n`glass{panel, state}`, `knockdown{victim}`, `deke{by}`, `deke_beat{by, victim}`, `poke{by, ok}`,\n`chirp{by, target, line}`, `gloves{by, target}`, `turtle{by}`, `fight_start{a, b}`, `fight_hit{by, kind, dmg}`,\n`fight_end{winner, loser}`, `sin_bin{who, t}`, `sin_bin_end{who}`, `item_throw{kind}`, `item{by, kind}`,\n`hazard{kind, victim}`, `thin_ice_break{patch}`, `plunge{victim}`, `mascot_down{by}`, `boom{team, n}`,\n`kaboom_start{team}`, `kaboom_end{team}`, `kaboom_shot{by}`, `blast{goalie}`, `vault_cracked`, `twister{by}`,\n`period_end{n}`, `intermission`, `ot_start`, `shootout_start`, `shootout_attempt{by, ok}`, `shootout_end{team}`,\n`final{winner}`, `hat_trick{by}`, `hoser_hat_trick{by}`, `boost_start`, `organ_boost`.\n\n## Appendix C: Cutscene data format\n```js\n{ id: 'ch1-pre', set: 'locker', music: 'locker',\n  cast: [{ id: 'marge', at: [96, 60], facing: Math.PI / 2 }, { id: 'dunny', at: [70, 92] }, /* … */],\n  steps: [\n    { cam: [96, 72], zoom: 1.4, t: 0 },\n    { say: 'marge', text: 'Sit down, shut up, and listen. I got a letter.', expr: 'angry' },\n    { move: 'glitterman', to: [130, 40], t: 1.2 },\n    { pose: 'lou', pose: 'kneel' },\n    { sfx: 'organ-sting-sad' },\n    { choice: { who: 'marge', text: \"Captain. Tell 'em how we play tonight.\",\n                options: [['CLEAN AND FAST', { tactic: 'finesse' }], ['MEAN AND LOUD', { tactic: 'grit' }]] } },\n    { wait: 0.4 } ] }\n```\nThe runner (`game.script`) plays steps in order: `say` waits for the dialog to close; `move` and `cam` tween; a\n`choice` sets story flags (saved). Hold ○ to skip, which applies the default choice.\n\n## Appendix D: Writing samples (the voice to match; TEXT holds the full pools)\n**Booth: CHUCK (play-by-play: present tense, rapid verbs, crescendo)**\n- \"Puck's dropped and we're under way at {arena}!\"\n- \"{name} with speed, through center, over the line—\"\n- \"{name} dangles, dances, and DEKES!\"\n- \"Big wind-up… {name} with the CLAPPER!\"\n- \"{name} SHOOTS — {name} SCORES!\"\n- \"TOP SHELF, where Grandma hides the cookie tin!\"\n- \"Bar down! They heard that one in the parking lot!\"\n- \"One-timer — BANG! {name} buries it!\"\n- \"Five-hole! Right between the pads!\"\n- \"Glove save, and a BEAUTY!\"\n- \"Off the POST! The iron says no!\"\n- \"OH! {victim} just got a free trip to next Tuesday!\"\n- \"THROUGH THE GLASS! Somebody get a broom!\"\n- \"The gloves are off! {a} and {b} are going at it!\"\n- \"The meter's full… it's… KA-BOOOOM!\"\n- \"The puck went in, and the GOALIE went with it!\"\n- \"Polar Pete is DOWN! Somebody check on the bear!\"\n- \"HAT TRICK! Here come the hats!\"\n- \"That's the end of the {period}. {home} {hs}, {away} {as}.\"\n\n**Booth: MOOSE (color: folksy, mangled metaphors, ex-enforcer)**\n- \"He stopped that with his face, Chuck. You can't teach that.\"\n- \"Ding-dong, nobody home.\"\n- \"He hit him so hard his ancestors felt it.\"\n- \"That's a delivery, Chuck, and nobody signed for it.\"\n- \"That glass is coming out of somebody's paycheque.\"\n- \"Now THIS is hockey. Grab a seat. Grab a hot dog. Grab two.\"\n- \"Octopus on the ice. It's tradition, Chuck. Don't ask which tradition.\"\n- \"I played eleven seasons. Lost fourteen teeth. Found nine.\"\n- \"My first coach said I had the hands of a surgeon. Then he saw me skate.\"\n- \"Thin ice? I never skated on the thick stuff.\"\n- \"Somebody call the fire department. And my mother.\"\n\n**Chirps (rhymes and comparisons, PG)**\n- \"Nice flow! Did your mom cut it with a skate blade?\"\n- \"You skate like a fridge on a waterbed!\"\n- \"Is that a stick or a toothpick?\"\n- \"Your five-hole's wider than the highway!\"\n- \"You're a pylon with a pulse!\"\n- \"Hey goalie, want a net? You're not using yours!\"\n- \"Your slapshot couldn't pop a bubble!\"\n- \"You've got the hockey sense of a boiled perogy!\"\n- \"Nice turnover! Bake it yourself?\"\n- \"My grandma checks harder, and she's ninety!\"\n\n**Tips (Coach Marge; `{action}` becomes a glyph chip)**\n- \"Skate with the stick. Hold {turbo} to turbo. It runs out, so pick your moments.\"\n- \"{pass} passes. Point where you want it to go.\"\n- \"Tap {shoot} for a wrister. Hold it for a slapshot. Let go to fire.\"\n- \"Pass coming your way? Hit {shoot} for a ONE-TIMER.\"\n- \"No puck? {shoot} checks, {deke} pokes, {pass} switches to whoever's closest.\"\n- \"With the puck, {deke} dekes past a check. Fools goalies too.\"\n- \"Hits, passes, saves, goals: they fill the BOOM meter. Fill it and the whole team goes KABOOM.\"\n- \"Somebody's got a grudge. Hold {lob} to drop the gloves.\"\n- \"In a scrap: {pass} jab, {shoot} haymaker, {deke} duck, {lob} yank the sweater.\"\n- \"Fans throw goodies on the ice. Skate over 'em.\"\n- \"Power play! They're a skater short. Move it and shoot.\"\n- \"{lob} with the puck flips a saucer over their sticks.\"\n- \"{chirp} chirps. Gets in their heads.\"\n- \"Shootout! In net: {pass} butterfly, {shoot} poke, {deke} dive.\"\n\n**Three stars (CHUCK)**: \"The third star: {name}, who hit everything but the Flood Wagon.\" · \"Second star: {name},\nwith {g} goals and a smile that could melt the ice.\" · \"And the first star of the game… {name}!\"\n","numLines":416,"startLine":1058,"totalLines":1473}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CyH5dZmoMBRKjkWyQSpJm1","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
