{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qzw8h3sRqyEcsiywmfrDUe","type":"tool_result","content":"engine/AI_GUIDE.md:74:1. **Game logic in world units, `dt` everywhere.** Never store screen pixels. Convert only when drawing (`r.w(x, y, z)`) or reading the mouse (`game.mouseGround()`). `update(dt)` runs in exact fixed steps: every 1/120 s of real time is one step of `dt = 1/120 * game.timeScale`, so the same inputs play the same at 60, 90, 120 or 144 Hz.\nengine/API-INDEX.md:485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n2633:  mouseGround() { const m = this.input.mouseScreen(); return m ? this.view.toGround(m[0], m[1]) : null; }\n2916:  _screenToGround(dx, dy) {\n2928:    if (dx || dy) { const [gx, gy] = this._screenToGround(dx, dy); c.tx += gx; c.ty += gy; moved = true; }\n2931:    if (z !== was && F.zoomAt !== false) { const q = I.zoomPoint(); if (q) { const k = z / was, [gx, gy] = this._screenToGround((q[0] - S.W / 2) * (1 - 1 / k) * k, (q[1] - S.H / 2) * (1 - 1 / k) * k); c.tx += gx; c.ty += gy; moved = true; } }","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"7b7cb7ac-f3b1-4216-abc9-ba4665e5a7da","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:54:13.304Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"engine/AI_GUIDE.md:74:1. **Game logic in world units, `dt` everywhere.** Never store screen pixels. Convert only when drawing (`r.w(x, y, z)`) or reading the mouse (`game.mouseGround()`). `update(dt)` runs in exact fixed steps: every 1/120 s of real time is one step of `dt = 1/120 * game.timeScale`, so the same inputs play the same at 60, 90, 120 or 144 Hz.\nengine/API-INDEX.md:485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n2633:  mouseGround() { const m = this.input.mouseScreen(); return m ? this.view.toGround(m[0], m[1]) : null; }\n2916:  _screenToGround(dx, dy) {\n2928:    if (dx || dy) { const [gx, gy] = this._screenToGround(dx, dy); c.tx +=