{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghDXW6hd6cw5cxDL5Qfz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1261,"cache_read_input_tokens":813019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1261},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"5128c592-6974-4c5e-b124-ee0c1cabca73","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:57:56.892Z","request_id":"req_011CghDXVpqCMtx7q43N1vY9","thinking_duration_ms":1417,"thinking_display":"updates"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghDXW6hd6cw5cxDL5Qfz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y6PRUSpnRGYLRW33dGzMZs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"node tools/build.mjs >/dev/null; export TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp; (timeout 900 node tests/shots.mjs fight kaboom shootout pond grind mall dome flood lab about credits attract dev drill cut2 cut3 cut4 cut5 ending > .tmp/shots.log 2>&1 &); cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2, handoff package)\n\nEvery change is applied by `tools/patch-engine.py` from the pristine `engine/my-3d2dge.orig.js` to `engine/my-3d2dge.js`,\nand marked in the source with `[ICE HOC-KABOOM]`.\n\n1. **Font**: the PlayStation face-button symbols (✕ ○ □ △) and a few typographic marks (· — … ✓ ☆ ◂ ’ “ ” ♦) added to the\n   5x7 font (`G57`). Why: canvas prompts showed `?` for the symbols `PAD_GLYPHS.playstation` itself uses.\n2. **AI Hub controller rule**: in the gamepad poll, button 9 (Options) is ignored while button 8 (Create) is held, and the\n   join check does the same. Why: AI Hub reserves Create + Options for its corner bar. Harmless outside the hub.\n3. **Humanoid gear**: `weapon: 'stick' | 'gstick'` are accepted (no built-in weapon drawn), and a gear hook, `o.gear(K)`,\n   runs in both `_drawHD` and `_drawClassic` before the depth sort, with the rig's projection helpers and its `ops` list.\n   Why: the hockey look rests on sticks, skates, helmets, masks, goalie pads, blockers, catchers, numbers and letters,\n   and drawing them inside the rig's own depth-sorted ops is the only way they sort correctly against the limbs. The game\n   draws all the gear itself through the hook (`src/21-rigs.js`), so the engine stays general.\n4. **Audio**: periodic waves `organ` (drawbars 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8) and `brass` (odd-heavy saw) for `sfx` voices and song\n   tracks; `lp` / `lpTo` / `q` (a lowpass, optionally swept) on oscillator voices and tracks; tracks also take `attack`\n   and `decay`; a `voice` bus routed to master with `audio.voiceVolume`; `audio.bus(name)` returns the master, sfx,\n   music or voice gain node for a game's own sound graphs. Why: the arena organ, the goal horn and the formant-filtered\n   babble voices need them.\n5. **Dialog voice hook**: `voice` may be a function `(ch, index, text, page)` called for each newly typed letter, on the\n   dialog or per `say()`. Why: every speaker babbles in their own voice.\n6. **Floor bake cache**: a TileMap keeps 12 baked floors (one per view and zoom), not 6. Why: a match uses the broadcast,\n   overhead and ice-level views at a few zooms; with 6 the cache cleared and re-baked mid-game.\nEOF\necho written","description":"Start screenshot batch; write ENGINE-CHANGES.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1261,"cache_read_input_tokens":813019,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1261},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bfc1153-d85f-4cc7-a4e9-74837d1d317d","uuid":"d6bbabb2-9a45-4628-a19a-3fce8f290684","timestamp":"2026-11-04T03:58:06.360Z","request_id":"req_011CghDXVpqCMtx7q43N1vY9","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Y6PRUSpnRGYLRW33dGzMZs":{"command":"node tools/build.mjs >/dev/null; export TMPDIR=$PWD/.tmp; (timeout 900 node tests/shots.mjs fight kaboom shootout pond grind mall dome flood lab about credits attract dev drill cut2 cut3 cut4 cut5 ending > .tmp/shots.log 2>&1 &); cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2, handoff package)\n\nEvery change is applied by `tools/patch-engine.py` from the pristine `engine/my-3d2dge.orig.js` to `engine/my-3d2dge.js`,\nand marked in the source with `[ICE HOC-KABOOM]`.\n\n1. **Font**: the PlayStation face-button symbols (✕ ○ □ △) and a few typographic marks (· — … ✓ ☆ ◂ ’ “ ” ♦) added to the\n   5x7 font (`G57`). Why: canvas prompts showed `?` for the symbols `PAD_GLYPHS.playstation` itself uses.\n2. **AI Hub controller rule**: in the gamepad poll, button 9 (Options) is ignored while button 8 (Create) is held, and the\n   join check does the same. Why: AI Hub reserves Create + Options for its corner bar. Harmless outside the hub.\n3. **Humanoid gear**: `weapon: 'stick' | 'gstick'` are accepted (no built-in weapon drawn), and a gear hook, `o.gear(K)`,\n   runs in both `_drawHD` and `_drawClassic` before the depth sort, with the rig's projection helpers and its `ops` list.\n   Why: the hockey look rests on sticks, skates, helmets, masks, goalie pads, blockers, catchers, numbers and letters,\n   and drawing them inside the rig's own depth-sorted ops is the only way they sort correctly against the limbs. The game\n   draws all the gear itself through the hook (`src/21-rigs.js`), so the engine stays general.\n4. **Audio**: periodic waves `organ` (drawbars 1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 8) and `brass` (odd-heavy saw) for `sfx` voices and song\n   tracks; `lp` / `lpTo` / `q` (a lowpass, optionally swept) on oscillator voices and tracks; tracks also take `attack`\n   and `decay`; a `voice` bus routed to master with `audio.voiceVolume`; `audio.bus(name)` returns the master, sfx,\n   music or voice gain node for a game's own sound graphs. Why: the arena organ, the goal horn and the formant-filtered\n   babble voices need them.\n5. **Dialog voice hook**: `voice` may be a function `(ch, index, text, page)` called for each newly typed letter, on the\n   dialog or per `say()`. Why: every speaker babbles in their own voice.\n6. **Floor bake cache**: a TileMap keeps 12 baked floors (one per view and zoom), not 6. Why: a match uses the broadcast,\n   overhead and ice-level views at a few zooms; with 6 the cache cleared and re-baked mid-game.\nEOF\necho written","description":"Start screenshot batch; write ENGINE-CHANGES.md"}}}
